</ul>
</li>
<li><a href="/#benefits">Benefits of Google Cloud hosting</a></li>
<li><a href="/#final">Final thoughts</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/google-cloud-wordpress-1024x768-1.webp" alt="hosting wordpress on google cloud" width="1024" height="768" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<h2 id="pricing">Google Cloud hosting for WordPress websites &#8211; Pricing</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you are willing to shop around and commit to a longer contract, you can find great WordPress hosting plans on shared servers at less than $5 per month. There are also unmanaged virtual private servers with prices starting at less than $10 per month, however, they do require some knowledge of server management.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Google Cloud, on the other hand, charges you per hour for the resources you use. To put things into perspective, let’s say you are running a 1 CPU machine with 4 GB of RAM. This will cost you $0.0475 per hour, which equals $24.2725 per month. This is very much in the same price range as many managed WordPress web hosts, but with one key difference &#8211; managed hosts often provide a hands-off experience while Google Cloud puts you in control over your cloud account.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Google also offers free credits for signing up as well as reasonable discounts for those that know how to configure their machine.</span></p>
<h2 id="infrastructure">The infrastructure behind Google Cloud hosting</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Let’s take a look at the components that power Google Cloud web hosting.</span></p>
<h4>Data centers</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Google has its hardware-based in data centers all across the globe. Furthermore, the software-defined network that forms the basis for their services is pretty extensive. Over the last two decades, they built an immense network that is said to deliver 20-30% of all internet traffic.</span></p>
<h4>Virtual machines</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Shared hosting is generally the most affordable option. However, it comes with a tradeoff since you have to share server space and resources with other sites. On the other hand, virtual private servers (VPS) provide websites with the privacy and resources they need by dedicating a specific area of a virtual server to use.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Cloud hosting holds the middle ground. Websites hosted on the cloud don’t have a dedicated virtual server but are instead hosted across a system of virtual machines called Compute Engine. That means websites are not limited to a single virtual machine and don’t use shared resources.</span></p>
<h4>Resource management</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Since Google Cloud is not a managed hosting solution, you are responsible for configuring your own resources. These resources are fully scalable, so in case your website experiences a spike in activity, you have an option to scale them up during that time frame and bring them down to optimal levels when the traffic returns to normal. That said, hosting on Google Cloud can be very cost-efficient when regularly monitored.</span></p>
<h2 id="install">How to install WordPress on Google Cloud</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Installing WordPress on Google Cloud is a bit more complicated than installing it on other web hosts. In this section of today’s article, our <a href="/">digital marketing agency Chicago</a> will walk you through the installation one step at a time to make the process as seamless as possible:</span></p>
<h3 id="deploy">Deploy a WordPress instance</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The very first thing you need to do is sign up for Google Cloud. This shouldn’t take you more than a couple of minutes. Once you gain access to the console, we suggest verifying the account with your bank or credit card, and Google will award you $300 worth of credits.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">After this is done, launch a new project by selecting the </span><b><i><a href="https://cloud.google.com/marketplace">Marketplace</a> </i></b><span style="font-weight: 400;">option from the left-hand side menu of your dashboard. </span></p>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/marketplaces.webp" alt="" width="279" height="387" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">On the next page, you will see the search feature which you can use to type in </span><b><i>WordPress</i></b><span style="font-weight: 400;">. You will be presented with a list of configurations that you can deploy in a couple of clicks.</span></p>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/marketlpace_wordpress-768x487-1.webp" alt="" width="667" height="423" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Navigate to the one that has </span><b><i>Google Click to Deploy</i></b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> in its subtitle.</span></p>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/click_to_deploy-1024x471-1.webp" alt="" width="800" height="368" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Upon selecting this option, you will be presented with a preview of estimated costs and the stack the package uses.</span></p>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/launch.webp" alt="" width="632" height="162" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">As you can see in the image above, this stack offers 1 CPU, 2 GB of RAM, and 10 GB of storage space. The estimated cost is approximately $13.61 per month with discounts for each month of full usage. This is perfect for running a website that receives a moderate amount of traffic. The next thing you need to do is click on </span><b><i>LAUNCH ON COMPUTE ENGINE</i></b><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></p>
<h3 id="create">Create and configure your project</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This step starts with choosing a name for your project and clicking the </span><b><i>Create </i></b><span style="font-weight: 400;">button.</span></p>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/new_project.webp" alt="" width="603" height="223" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The service should take a couple of minutes to set up. During this time you can further adjust the configuration of your new Google Cloud instance. Bear in mind that changing settings can reduce as well as increase your costs. Keep an eye on the estimated costs on the right-hand side.</span></p>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/wp_overview.webp" alt="" width="629" height="448" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Here are a few suggestions concerning this page. You need to make sure not to use less than 2 GB of RAM for optimal performance. Also, this setup suggests a shared CPU as its default option. To avoid any possibility of running a slow WordPress website, we suggest navigating to </span><b><i>Machine type</i></b> <span style="font-weight: 400;">and selecting </span><b><i>1vCPU with 3.75 GB of memory</i></b><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></p>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/machine_type.webp" alt="" width="626" height="214" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This will increase your monthly costs to $24.75, not including discounts. If you wish to further increase your performance, navigate to </span><b><i>Boot disk type</i></b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> and select </span><b><i>SSD Persistent Disk</i></b><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></p>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/disk.webp" alt="" width="625" height="113" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Your estimated costs are now around $25.97 each month, not including discounts. We found the default 10 GB of storage to be enough for the majority of websites. There are just a few more things to do before you move on:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Choose a region for your server</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Check the Install phpMyAdmin option</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Enable HTTP and HTTPS traffic</span></li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/https.webp" alt="" width="627" height="151" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">You are now ready to hit that </span><b><i>Deploy </i></b><span style="font-weight: 400;">button. Google Cloud should take a couple of minutes to get everything prepared. After that, you will be presented with the deployment page where you can view the credentials of your new installation. Here is how it looks.</span></p>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/deploy.webp" alt="" width="632" height="401" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Just make sure to </span><b>change your MySQL and WordPress admin users and passwords</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> on the right-hand side, and you are ready for the final step.</span></p>
<h3 id="map">Map a domain and set up an SSL certificate</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Your website is now live on the cloud, but it is currently accessible only via an IP address. Next step is mapping a custom domain name. Your domain name is very important for the future performance of your WordPress website. Here are some tips to keep in mind when choosing one:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Come up with a unique and memorable name that is likely to stick with your visitors</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Choose a name that gives new visitors as well as search engines an idea of what your website is about</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Keep in mind that your domain name impacts SEO</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Once you have decided on the domain name, you need to set up an SSL certificate for your website. This is basically all you need to know when it comes to Google Cloud hosting for WordPress websites. Make sure to keep a watchful eye on your billing costs, since Google will start charging you according to your payment method as soon as your free credits run out.</span></p>
<h2 id="benefits">Benefits of Google Cloud hosting</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Now that you know how to host your website on the Google Cloud Platform let’s check all the benefits this solution brings.</span></p>
<h4>Reliability</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">According to their Service Level Agreement (SLA), all customers are guaranteed a monthly uptime percentage of 99.5% for single instance VMs.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">That equals 716.4 hours of website online time. Also, since their network is widely distributed, in case one of the servers goes down, there are plenty more to ensure that your website stays active.</span></p>
<h4>Scalability</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Google Cloud gives you complete control over the number of resources you allocate to your website, and you can freely scale them up and down when required. However, the more server resources your website consumes, the bigger the costs.</span></p>
<h4>Speed</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Cloud network is configured to support high bandwidth and low latency. As it is located all around the world, your website data can be rapidly transferred to Google’s browser. The hosting scalability also plays a huge role here. In case your bandwidth and storage are configured for traffic surges, there is little to no risk of the server being pushed past its potential.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Enabling Google’s content delivery network (CDN) gives your website access to even more servers making static assets delivery go more smoothly.</span></p>
<h4>Security</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Google’s data center hardware is custom-built, and its employees monitor data-center facilities 24 hours a day. Furthermore, the data shared over Cloud are encrypted and distributed over multiple virtual machines.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">When it comes to website backups, emergency backup generators allow for the data to be immediately shifted to another server in case something unpredictable happens.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">However, it is essential to mention that you are still responsible for securing your WordPress website despite all the safety measures.</span></p>
<h2 id="final">Final thoughts</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">To those of you that have only used traditional hands-off hosting providers, switching to Google Cloud hosting for a WordPress website may feel like a huge step. With its unique pricing model and hosting configuration options, this model is probably very different from anything you have tried before, hence the reluctance. You may, however, soon find out that it pays huge dividends. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Google Cloud hosting provides your WordPress website with the next level of performance. If you crave limitless scalability, premium security, more control, and flexibility, the huge step you are about to take is certainly one in the right direction.</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/google-cloud-wordpress.png',NULL,'[]','[166,354]','2022-06-30T07:55:05','2022-06-30T07:55:05',1706,1,11),
  (14673,'/ahrefs-vs-semrush-vs-moz','ahrefs-vs-semrush-vs-moz','post','blog','Ahrefs vs Semrush vs Moz: Battle of SEO Tools','Ahrefs vs Semrush vs Moz: Battle of SEO Tools | Alpha Efficiency','Alpha Efficiency has deconstructed the top three SEO Tools to assist you in discovering which tool is best for your business.','https://alphaefficiency.com/ahrefs-vs-semrush-vs-moz',1,'When it comes to search engine optimization, picking the right tool for the job is an important part of reaching your entrepreneurial goals. Having a great idea won’t be able to reach its optimal potential unless you are able to maximize its reach. Ideas are worth little if they stay in the drawer. You have &hellip; Continued','<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"> When it comes to search engine optimization, picking the right tool for the job is an important part of reaching your entrepreneurial goals. Having a great idea won’t be able to reach its optimal potential unless you are able to maximize its reach. Ideas are worth little if they stay <i>in the drawer</i>. You have to spread them. </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">The </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">best way to reach your local market is with a sound </span><a href="/guide-on-how-to-do-seo-for-website"><span style="font-weight: 400;">SEO strategy</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. While the internet offers many online tools to do your SEO research, Ahrefs, Semrush, and Moz, are the three that dominate the SEO scene and are recommended by <a href="/">Alpha Efficiency</a>.  </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">At first glance, the differences between Ahrefs, Semrush, and Moz may seem small, however, the advantages that one of these tools offers over another may prove to be very significant for your campaign. In today’s article, our <a href="/seo-agency-chicago">SEO agency near Chicago</a> will take a thorough look into each of these tools revealing their key features, pros and cons, and pricing to better enable you to make the right choice for you and your goals. Ahrefs vs Semrush vs Moz &#8211; the Battle of SEO Tools.</span></p>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/seo-tools-e1628265338263.webp" alt="" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<h2 style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ahrefs        </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">                               </span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="http://ahrefs.com">Ahrefs</a> is the tool to invest in if you wish to build high-quality backlinks for your website. It is amongst the best when it comes to backlink analysis and boasts an excellent reputation as a checker of backlink authority. It possesses one of the most wide-reaching databases of live links and also crawling software to recreate your website from the point of view of a search engine. Whether you use it to unearth backlink profiles of your competitors or build your own backlinks, Ahrefs provides the best link indexing among all SEO tools.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Besides backlink building, Ahrefs also excels in monitoring your rankings on Google, performing technical audits, and keyword research with the help of its excellent Keywords Explorer tool. Although best known for its backlink analysis feature, over time, Ahrefs has evolved into a completely developed SEO software suite.</span></p>
<p><b>The key features of Ahrefs:</b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Site Explorer </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; Provides a detailed look at the organic search traffic and backlink analysis of URLs and websites. You can find out how many backlinks you have earned and how much your competitors do, but also analyze the quality of a backlink’s site in order to determine whether it is valuable as an authority site or not.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Keywords Explorer </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; When deciding which keywords to use, take a look at this dashboard to determine keyword difficulty, search volume, and many other important factors. Get traffic estimations as to how frequently a certain keyword appears in people’s searches and determine how difficult it will be to rank for a specific keyword. In the case your business operates outside of your country, their database covers keywords for over 100 countries.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Content Explorer </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; easily find high-performing content as well as gain insight into social share statistics. Analyze the popularity of the topics you target and use them for your content marketing campaign.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Rank Tracker </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; keep track of keyword rankings based on search volume and multiple other factors. You can also track your desktop and mobile rankings and receive daily, weekly, and monthly reports. That way, you can closely monitor your progress and effectively update and optimize your SEO strategy along the way.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Site Audit </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; audits your website for any possible lack of SEO. So, why do you need an SEO audit? Keeping track of your SEO campaign can be stressful at times, and that’s why this tool is highly useful, as it scans for any potential problems, informs you when they occur, and analyzes your website’s health.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Alerts </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; helps you monitor your SEO performance by providing notifications on new and lost backlinks, web mentions, and keyword rankings. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Domain Comparison </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; Provides the option to compare the backlink profiles of up to five domains.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Content Gap </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; offers insight into keywords that your competitors rank for, that you don’t in order to provide better insight on keywords you should be targeting among multiple competitors simultaneously. </span></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Pros</strong></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Excellent backlink analysis</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Highly accurate and reliable rank tracker</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Email alerts help you stay up to date when it comes to new and </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">lost </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">backlinks and your website’s rankings for keywords</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Its Keywords Explorer provides quality results in keyword research</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Top of the line outreach tool to combine with other marketing tools like Mailshake, Buzzsumo, or Ninja Outreach</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Cons</b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Site Audit takes a very long time to deliver an audit report</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Software could use more SEO reporting features</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">There are cheaper link building tools out there (Majestic SEO and Linkody, to mention a few)</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ahrefs offers no free trial. It will cost you $7 to test it out for a week</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>We found the most benefits in:</b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Transparency </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; Ahrefs lets you gain insight into your competitors’ campaigns with ease making the internet a more transparent place.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Optimization </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; Although it takes a long time to produce a report, Site Audit provides business owners the opportunity to improve their SEO without having to investigate multiple sources.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Easy to use</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; You can monitor your URLs’ health through numbers, stats, and graphs via Ahrefs dashboards.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Keywords at the palm of your hand</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; Whether you are searching for new keywords to include in your campaign or simply monitoring the performance of existing ones, Ahrefs makes the process flow seamless. </span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Pricing</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ahrefs offers four pricing plans:</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">annual plans: 20% discount</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Lite </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; $99 per month</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Standard </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; $179 per month</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Advanced </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; $399 per month</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Agency </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; $999 per month</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Also, if you decide to pay on an annual level, there is a discount for annual plans of 20%.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you are a solopreneur or manage a single blog, the Lite plan may be the best fit, as it features various <a href="/writerzen-vs-surfer-seo-vs-neuronwriter">blog optimization tools</a>. However, this plan comes with limitations for persons running multiple blogs. The Standard plan overcomes these limitations as it allows you to track more keywords and backlinks. The Advanced and Agency plans are both tailored to suit the needs of agencies that offer </span><a href="/seo-agency-chicago"><span style="font-weight: 400;">search engine marketing services</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> and manage big clientele on a daily basis. </span></p>
<p><b>Our thoughts on Ahrefs</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Over the years Ahrefs has proven to be a reliable backlink analysis and competitive research tool. With the recent launch of new features, and upgrades to existing ones, it has become a full-fledged SEO tool. Its high ROI more than compensates the fact that Ahrefs is on the pricier side.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">SEMrush</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="http://semrush.com/">SEMrush</a> is the perhaps most popular online tool for SEO. It is recognized as the world’s leading keyword research tool and can also be used for backlink building, competitor analysis, and technical SEO audit amongst many other features. SEMrush can also assist you in SEO, PPC, social media, and content marketing campaigns. It provides thorough aid and is suitable for people without much experience or knowledge in the field, and helps you determine what the current trends in your industry are. Clients like eBay or Quora show that this all-in-one digital marketing tool is key to higher SERP rankings and niche domination.</span></p>
<p><b>The key features of SEMrush:</b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Keyword Magic Tool</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; SEMrush possesses the largest keyword database on the market that includes more than 20 billion keywords. Here you can find different variations for the keywords you target and gain insight into valuable metrics such as search volume, CPC, or keyword difficulty score for each. This feature is unmatched, and you will definitely find it highly useful.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Site Audit Tool</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; This tool helps you identify and fix all the technical SEO issues that your site may have. Get to understand your own website better and constantly improve it. Keep track of your organic traffic and identify any weaknesses that might need to be tackled.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Position Tracking</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; SEO experts consider SEMrush’s position tracking tool to be the most accurate tool on the market. It allows you to track both your own and your competitors’ rankings for the keywords you target. The fight over keywords amongst competition can frequently be fierce, so it is of vital importance to closely monitor your competitors in order to outperform them.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Content Marketing Toolkit</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; This feature includes 6 tools for content creation and optimization that can help you improve your content’s ranking with ease.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Competitor Research Toolkit</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; This toolkit allows you to easily track PPC campaigns as well as SEO of your competitors and see their best-performing keywords and backlinks. It also includes Traffic Analysis that provides traffic metrics for the domain of your choice enabling you to compare your traffic with the traffic of your competitors.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Backlink Audit Tool</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; It lets you discover and eliminate those backlinks that can cause different penalties from Google.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>SEO Reports</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; This tool gives you the option to download PDF reports which you can further customize in order to better organize your SEO and PDF research data.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Pros </b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Provides an insight into SEO and PPC strategies of your competitors</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Includes the On-Page SEO Checker Tool that offers suggestions on how to optimize your keyword rankings, which semantically related words to include in your content , as well as recommendations relating to content length and readability</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Site Audit Tool is the major upside as it identifies SEO errors and recommends actions that you can take to improve the overall SEO health of your website</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">One of the best online keyword research platforms with the Keyword Magic Tool</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Cons</b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Mastering SEMrush and all of its features takes time</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">SEMrush’s Backlink Analytics tool is not as accurate as Ahrefs’ Site Explorer</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>We found the most benefits in:</b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Transparency </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; It takes just a couple of clicks to see your competitors’ SEO and marketing strategy. You can also discover who is backlinking to your content.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Analysis </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; You can easily improve your SEO thanks to in-depth analytics tools.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Easy Fixes</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; Fix broken links and improve on-site SEO.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Pricing</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">SEMrush offers three monthly pricing plans:</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">annual plan: two months free </span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Pro </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; $119.95 per month</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Guru </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; $229.95 per month</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Business </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; $449.95 per month</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Instead of giving a total discount, in case of an</span> <span style="font-weight: 400;">annual plan, two months are given for free.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The annual plan discount can come in handy if you use SEMrush as your go-to SEO research tool. There is also a </span><b>free plan </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">that doesn’t require an account. However, the package contains only a small number of basic tools.</span></p>
<p><b>Our thoughts on SEMrush</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you are looking for the ultimate SEO tool, look no further. SEMrush is loaded with features, from discovering the most profitable keywords for your business to competitor analysis and content marketing tools. SEMrush has everything you need to boost your SEO and climb the SERP rankings.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">Moz</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Developed by Rand Fishkin in 2004, <a href="http://moz.com/">Moz</a> relies on SEO metrics like Domain Authority and Page Authority to provide details on link equity, keyword rankings, page optimization, and many more. It is primarily an SEO and data management software that focuses on categorizing and prioritizing keywords as well as providing intuitive keyword suggestions based on a very extensive database. It is simply put an all-in-one SEO software. However, this tool has not seen much improvement ever since Rand Fishkin left the company in 2018.</span></p>
<p><b>The key features of Moz are:</b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Global Rank Tracking</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; This tool lets you track keywords for three of the most popular explorers, Google, Bing, and Yahoo, in over 200 countries on a weekly basis. You can also apply segmentation by the campaign, keyword label, and location.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Keyword Research</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; Find the best keywords to target for your website. Determine which keyword your audience uses to search for your products or services and how to rank higher in those searches. Identify which keywords to target according to a variety of metrics and keep track of <a href="/keyword-search-volume-explained">keyword research volume</a> on a monthly basis.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Link Profile Analysis</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; It allows you to utilize industry-leading metrics so you can find the most relevant links. It also enables you to recognize bad links that may potentially cause negative effects on your website.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Site Crawl</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; This tool crawls your website in search of SEO errors and provides recommendations on how to fix them in order to improve your website’s overall SEO health. This is a very useful tool that keeps your website running smoothly and gives you peace of mind.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Page Optimization </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; Search the internet for the best-performing content and apply different strategies to boost your own.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Reporting </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; Delivers data and suggestions on how to improve your website’s traffic. Monitor your success constantly; improvement is an ongoing process.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Pros</b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">“Moz recommends Fixing” is a useful feature incorporated into their Site Audit tool where Moz’s SEO experts recommend steps for fixing critical issues on your website</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Page Optimization feature allows you to easily fix on-page issues and improve search rankings</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Great customer support</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Cons</b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Search volume data could be improved</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The site audit reports often struggle to find common SEO errors</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Not always accurate backlink data</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Moz takes time to master</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The user interface doesn’t follow the latest trends</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>We found the most benefits in:</b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Transparency </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; Just like the other two tools, Moz reveals all SEO-related content across the web.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Free toolbar </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; SEO consultants and business owners can reap many benefits that this toolbar has to offer at no cost at all.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Discovery </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; Unravel top backlinks, SEO optimization strategies, find new keywords, anchor text, and many more.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Pricing</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Moz offers four monthly pricing plans:</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">annual plan: 20% discount </span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Standard </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; $99 per month</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Medium </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; $179 per month</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Large </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; $249 per month</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Premium </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; $599 per month</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Similar to Ahrefs, in the case of an annual plan, Moz provides a 20% discount.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If your SEO budget is tight and you simply can’t afford a monthly subscription, Moz offers </span><b>free services</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> for you to boost your SEO ranking. These services include:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Link Explorer </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; For tracking your link profile and finding new link-building opportunities.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Keyword Explorer </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; For finding the most profitable keywords in your niche.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>MozBar </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; A Google Chrome extension that provides an insight into any website’s Page Authority and Domain Authority as well as the option to do keyword research and link analysis of those websites directly from the browser bar.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Our thoughts on Moz</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">People from Moz are doing a fantastic job in regularly updating their blog and YouTube channel providing us with a plethora of SEO-related news and resources. However, when it comes to the tool itself and the features it offers, Moz falls behind the other two tools that we are evaluating in this article. While offering extremely useful features for free is definitely a gesture worth admiring, the rest that is included in their monthly plans is simply not enough to keep up with the competition.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ahrefs vs SEMrush vs Moz: The battle outcome</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Without a doubt, the three tools that we have analyzed in this article can all help you take your SEO game to the next level and provide exceptional results for your campaign. However, before we announce a winner, there are a couple of things to consider other than the features and benefits of each tool. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The three above-mentioned tools have multiple integrations. This means that if something works well for one SEO expert, it doesn’t necessarily mean it will work for you too. This is why it is a good idea to consider the tools you are already using and see whether they complement or integrate with the SEO research provider of your choice.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Continuing on, picking one of these tools doesn’t mean that you have to exclude the other two. For example, you could be using both Moz and SEMrush (or any of the three) as complementary tools, each in a different circumstance; it all comes down to your own preferences. Take the outcome of this comparison as our suggestion rather than as a rule to follow.</span></p>
<p><b>In our opinion amongst the SEO Tools, SEMrush would deliver the best results. </b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> <a href="/7-essential-steps-to-profitable-keyword-research-service-that-drive-results">Long-tail keywords</a> and low-competition keywords are the cornerstones of SEO. This is where SEMrush beats its competition by a large margin with its database that counts over 20 billion keywords. This makes obtaining thousands of keyword variations for the keywords you target nearly effortless. SEMrush is also the best tool on the market when it comes to providing the most accurate search volume data for keywords. Whether you are a blogger looking to improve the search engine optimization of your posts or an experienced marketer running the Google Ads real estate race, you can always rely on SEMrush to deliver the most accurate metrics.</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/seo-tools-e1628265338263.webp',NULL,'[]','[166,344]','2022-08-08T14:00:35','2022-08-08T14:00:35',2765,7,1),
  (14702,'/affordable-local-seo-services','affordable-local-seo-services','post','blog','Affordable local SEO services','Affordable local SEO services | Alpha Efficiency','Let us advise you on the capabilities of affordable local SEO services to launch your business effectively and efficiently to maximize outreach.','https://alphaefficiency.com/affordable-local-seo-services',1,'Reaching the first page on Google shouldn&#8217;t be a primary goal of low-budget local SEO campaigns. Ranking for a competitive keyword in a crowded niche is an impossible task if you aren&#8217;t making significant investments into backlinks and content.This inability to rank makes investing in SEO crucial. Smart business owners understand that investing in SEO &hellip; Continued','<p>Reaching the first page on Google shouldn&#8217;t be a primary goal of low-budget local SEO campaigns. Ranking for a competitive keyword in a crowded niche is an impossible task if you aren&#8217;t making significant investments into backlinks and content.This inability to rank makes investing in SEO crucial. Smart business owners understand that investing in SEO means playing a long-term game. Bottom of the funnel competitive keywords are often out of reach, but that doesn&#8217;t mean you can&#8217;t drive results on long-tail keywords and hyper-local/personalized search results.</p>
<p style="color: #2632bc; text-decoration: underline; text-align: left;"><a style="color: #2632bc; text-decoration: underline;" href="/#Why"><br />
</a><strong style="color: #323232;">Table of Contents:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li style="text-align: left;"><a href="/#Why">Why SEO services should be an indispensable part of your marketing budget</a></li>
<li style="text-align: left;"><a href="/#Customized">Customized Local SEO Packages</a></li>
<li style="text-align: left;"><a href="/#How">How can Local SEO strategy affect the customer&#8217;s journey?</a></li>
<li style="text-align: left;"><a href="/#solution">Why affordable local SEO services are the solution for your limited budget</a></li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/local-seo2.png" alt="Solution for limited budget: Affordable local SEO services" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<h3><strong>How Local SEO rankings work, and why it isn&#8217;t necessary to rank for your desired keyword to drive visits and results</strong></h3>
<p>Let&#8217;s assume that you have the desired keyword you want ranked. In our case, it would be <a href="/seo-agency-chicago"><em>&#8220;SEO agency Chicago</em></a>.&#8221; Typing this keyword out will pull up the map listings under Google Ads listings and above Organic listings. We typically refer to these as ad &#8220;local pack,&#8221; &#8220;3  pack,&#8221; or &#8220;maps.&#8221;</p>
<p>Typing this query will pull the strongest websites in Chicago per algorithm. However, if you aren&#8217;t located in Chicago these results are potentially irrelevant.</p>
<p>Your location plays a key role in determining what will show up in your &#8220;local pack&#8221;. Aspects that will determine what you will see will be three following things:</p>
<ol>
<li>Proximity to local maps listing</li>
<li>The date of the most recent review</li>
<li>Overall review frequency and number of reviews</li>
<li>Accuracy of NAPs and local directories pointing to your local listing and website</li>
<li>Local authority perceived by Google</li>
</ol>
<p>We’ve seen local listings that never rank for their “keyword + location” query, but consistently pull local and relevant traffic due to geographic results.</p>
<p>In hindsight, it should be the result of conjoined marketing strategies and tools. The design of the website, coding, link building, copywriting, blogging, etc., are all defined as an integral part of the <a href="/guide-on-how-to-do-seo-for-website">SEO strategy</a> that affects your online business visibility.</p>
<p>Using local SEO services is an excellent maneuver for reaching your final target, and getting your business recognized at the local level without ranking for specific competitive keywords.</p>
<h3 id="Why"><strong>Why SEO services should be an indispensable part of your marketing budget</strong></h3>
<p>Limited budgets mean you have to plan your investments wisely, especially at the beginning of your business odyssey. Considering that 34% of small business owners have said that using SEO strategies has helped them reach new customers, the decision to invest in digital tools can be crucial for the development of your small business.</p>
<p>Using local SEO services is an affordable and effective solution for enhancing the visibility of your small business, especially at the local level. Investing in local SEO enables business growth and drives traffic.</p>
<p>While SEO strategy is a rational investment decision, results don&#8217;t happen overnight. SEO is a long-term, pre-planned strategy that requires time to rank your business in search pages. We strongly advise planning at least 6 months before to get the results you&#8217;re aiming for.</p>
<h3 id="Customized"><strong>Customized Local SEO Packages</strong></h3>
<p>Every business requires a specific approach to its local SEO strategy; more important than it seems at first glance.</p>
<p>The fact of the matter is, half of the 67,000 Google queries generated every second are executed using keywords attached to a local place or business. This alone proves the significance of local SEO. In order to drive traffic towards your brand, we recommend a few different steps of a local SEO strategy that will improve your search engine ranking.</p>
<p><strong>#1 step:</strong> Conducting an in-depth <a href="/schedule-a-call">local SEO audit</a> will indicate your current position on search engines. This will help us set the right goal to increase customers, business, and revenue growth.</p>
<p><strong>#2 step:</strong> Identifying keywords that indicate the most used local search terms. Allows us to target local customers who are searching for terms that are similar to the products or services you sell.</p>
<p><strong>#3 step:</strong> Setting up your Google My Business profile with detailed information such as website address, store address, operation hours, Google Maps, photos, business directories and customer reviews all serve as important components for getting search engines to favor you. Reviews have an incredible impact on your customers&#8217; decisions as well. They show the opinions of other consumers who testify in favor of the trustworthiness of your brand, and the quality of your product or service.</p>
<p><strong>#4 step:</strong> Creating Google posts is an additional feature of Google My Business that grants you the ability to push your short content onto the first page of the search engines. This content should be relevant to fresh news around your business such as an upcoming event, any product changes, or seasonal sales.</p>
<p><strong>#5 step:</strong> Auditing the website&#8217;s mobile usability. Smartphone usefulness is essential for your business. Google itself positions websites with this feature; 52% of Google searches are executed on a mobile phone. Another important aspect is that 82% of consumers search for local businesses close to them.</p>
<p><strong>#6 step:</strong> Refining Local Technical SEO requires working on backend coding. It contributes to taking the strain off of search crawlers by making the structure of your site easier to process. Equally as important, is the creation of rich snippets. When optimized these increase your website&#8217;s click-through rate.</p>
<p><strong>#7 step:</strong> Using <a href="https://backlinko.com/white-hat-seo">White Hat SEO</a> techniques uses a mix of practices that increase the probability of your website being seen. These techniques contain monitoring functions that help with optimizing any site attributes such as broken links, website speed, title tags, meta descriptions, and building backlinks from high-authority websites.</p>
<p>Successful backlink strategies can also be based on your social media business profiles where you can share the links directing to your website. This will increase your visibility and positively impact your dealings with Google since their algorithm prefers these types of &#8220;natural&#8221; and unpaid links.</p>
<h3 id="How"><strong>How can Local SEO strategy affect the customer&#8217;s journey?</strong></h3>
<p>Depending on your business type and niche, customer journey maps can be created in several different ways. The first step of every customer journey is the acknowledgment of your business and its brand awareness.</p>
<p>When searching for businesses close by, your potential customers are most likely going to use search engines from their smartphones. This is how the journey starts.</p>
<p>The next step a potential customer will take is to find some comparative reviews between your product(s) and the competition. After that, a customer will usually make an in-store visit.</p>
<p>However, this is only a small part of a customer&#8217;s journey, they will research your business online. Their research process could consist of more than 500 touchpoints before this prospect is converted to a buyer.</p>
<p>They need to be convinced that your business is trustworthy and that other consumers have had a positive experience with your product or service. They will check your social media, read reviews, go through your website, along with other outlets to ensure they are about to make the right decision. This is where your content and reviews can play a key role. The content you are providing should affirm your customers that your brand is reliable and trustworthy.</p>
<p>Opposite to the linear marketing funnels, customer journeys are made of many crosswise interactions that a local SEO strategy can successfully streamline via:</p>
<ul>
<li>Enhancing local directories</li>
<li>Utilizing high-quality images and design on Google’s local listing itself and off of 3rd party directories</li>
<li>Keeping phone numbers visible and easily accessible</li>
<li>Continuously improving client feedback and reviews</li>
<li>Ensuring 100% NAP consistency</li>
</ul>
<p>Ultimately, local SEO is so much more than rankings. It is about the maintenance of local digital reputation. It means not only offering visibility, but improving the general impression your brand makes on your soon-to-be clients.</p>
<h3 id="solution"><strong>Why affordable local SEO services are the solution for your limited budget</strong></h3>
<p>A limited budget doesn&#8217;t necessarily mean limited options. Today, only 27% of small businesses are using the full potential of local SEO. The decision to use affordable local SEO services can launch your business effectively and efficiently, giving you a favorable position in the local small business environment. Once you take advantage of this, you will set up solid pillars for your SEO rankings that will ensure a consistent and reliable edge over your competition.</p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/local-seo2.png',NULL,'[]','[318,344]','2021-05-26T09:44:01','2021-05-26T09:44:01',1384,3,1),
  (14733,'/how-to-make-your-first-online-sale','how-to-make-your-first-online-sale','post','blog','How to Make Your First Online Sale','How to Make Your First Online Sale | Alpha Efficiency','Our team of E-commerce professionals is dedicated to providing you with the information you need to strengthen your online presence.','https://alphaefficiency.com/how-to-make-your-first-online-sale',1,'Making your first sale online is a significant milestone to achieve. Once you have established your online store, it is easy to submit to endless tweaking in search of perfection. This can take a lot of focus and energy that can be better utilized towards more important tasks like making that first online sale. There &hellip; Continued','<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Making your first sale online is a significant milestone to achieve. Once you have established your online store, it is easy to submit to endless tweaking in search of perfection. This can take a lot of focus and energy that can be better utilized towards more important tasks like making that first online sale. There are virtually hundreds of channels and ways to promote your business online, that often entrepreneurs find it difficult to choose what will produce the most meaningful results. Luckily, E-commerce professionals from our <a href="/">digital marketing agency in Chicago</a> are here to advise new as well as future entrepreneurs like you on how to best produce traffic and make your first sale online.</span></p>
<p><strong>Table of Contents: </strong></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#target">Targeting traffic is crucial for new stores</a></li>
<li><a href="/#utilize">Utilize your personal networks</a></li>
<li><a href="/#paid">Paid advertising</a></li>
<li><a href="/#outreach">Outreach</a></li>
<li><a href="/#outshine">Outshine your competitors with comparison shopping engines</a></li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/sell-online-1024x768.png" alt="" width="1024" height="768" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<h2 id="target">Targeting traffic is crucial for new stores</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">As previously mentioned, new online store owners easily get tangled in a web of constant font switching, second-guessing on their prices, and many other minor details in an effort to improve their store. The truth is that any meaningful improvement will only be significant once your store has an online presence. In other words, you need hard numbers and consistent traffic to your site. Once you manage to drive traffic to your store you will be able to gain hard data to discover if your prices are too high and if your brand resonates with your intended audience.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">In order for you to achieve your first online sale, we’ll start by introducing some free traffic sources and highly targeted marketing strategies that require more time and investments. </span></p>
<p><b>A piece of advice for the road</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Not every business can apply the same techniques and be equally successful. If a certain tactic doesn’t apply to your store, rather than skip it, we help in customizing it to best apply to you and your business. On another note, setting up Google Analytics is vital in order to monitor traffic as you implement different marketing strategies. Taking advantage of this, allows you to gain a clearer picture of which tactics bring the most benefits to your E-commerce efforts and which ones do not. </span></p>
<p><b>Free traffic sources</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Exploring free traffic sources involves manually sharing your store with relevant online communities. Below we have provided you with a couple of things to keep in mind in order to produce the best possible results:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Offer incentives in form of discount codes to entice people to visit your store</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Make sure to add your store URL to all of your personal online profiles</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Always look to provide real value to your visitors instead of constantly spamming them with repetitive promotional messages</span></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="utilize">Utilize your personal networks</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">As a prospective entrepreneur yourself, you know that your first 3 or 4 sales are most likely to come from your own personal connections. This is why in order to make your first sale online it is crucial to share your store on all social media platforms you possess. You could also send an email to your closest connections and inform them about your store’s launch or even organize an <a href="/email-marketing-automation">email marketing campaign</a>.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Employing your personal connections is a great way to get quick feedback. However, if this strategy doesn&#8217;t produce the results you were expecting you shouldn’t feel discouraged; this is the least qualified source of traffic. You will soon discover that nothing beats the feeling of earning the trust of your prospects and transforming them into loyal customers. </span></p>
<p><b>Build an email list</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">According to </span><a href="https://dma.org.uk/uploads/misc/marketers-email-tracker-2019.pdf"><span style="font-weight: 400;">research conducted by DMA</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">, the average ROI of email campaigns is forty-two dollars for each dollar that you spend. The best way to start building your email list is to include an email subscription form on your website. Your list will rapidly increase if you decide to include some form of incentive for signing up. Whether it’s a discount coupon or a chance to win a free product every week, you are only limited by your own imagination. Once you have a list of your current and potential customers, you will find it easier to get your message across since your product information and content will land directly into their inboxes avoiding spam filters.</span></p>
<p><b>Join online communities</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Posting a link to your store on forums such as Reddit or joining different Facebook groups is an effective way to find niche online communities in your industry. In channels like these people organize themselves around specific interests. Conducting quality research will help you find those interests that closely relate to your business. Once you have found your target audience and what their interests are, become an active member and connect with others. These communities are a great opportunity for you to build a reputation and establish authentic connections for your business. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Below are groups of experienced entrepreneurs that you can go to for extra help and support:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">r/Entrepreneur</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">r/ecommerce</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Shopify Entrepreneurs Facebook Group</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Grow and Sell Facebook Group</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Bright Ideas and Entrepreneurs LinkedIn Group</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Shopify Community</span></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="paid">Paid advertising</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Paid advertising is a reliable way to get targeted traffic. Many paid advertising platforms will only ask for compensation if someone clicks on your ad. In some instances, you don’t even have to dedicate a large portion of your budget to this type of advertising. Some campaigns go for as low as $10 dollars. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Google Ads is one of the most popular pay-per-click (PPC) advertising networks on the web and gives you a variety of options to make your first online sale. It allows marketers to post ads on Google search results pages, as well as YouTube videos, and partner websites.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The most prominent feature of Google Ads is its massive reach. With just a few steps, you can launch a campaign that will be seen by people all across the internet. Better yet, Google Ads campaign options allow you to set up targeted campaigns which are only triggered when someone types in your predefined keywords in a search engine console. Your ads will also appear on websites and articles that contain similar keywords. However, it is very important to conduct thorough keyword research to check the search volume for terms that your target audience is looking for.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Leaving the <a href="/google-ads-targeting-expansion">Google Ads targeting expansion</a> turned on will include a lookalike audience in your marketing campaign. Expanding your desired audience outside of your desired targeting can bring you more clicks. However, with this, there is a good chance that you will end up paying for unqualified clicks that won’t convert, which can end up costing you more and affecting your efficiency. If you are interested in trying Google Ads, check out our blog for a guide on how to set up your campaign as well as what to do and not to do when it comes to digital advertising.</span></p>
<p><b>Facebook advertising</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Facebook is one of the most popular social networks. It has the most diverse user base in terms of age, income, gender, and ethnicity. This is why Facebook is one of the most profitable marketing channels on the web today and a great chance for you to make your first sale online.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Marketers reach their customers by leveraging the social network’s targeting options. This tool helps you segment users by age, gender, job title, location, and interest. If you have a clear idea about the likes and interests of your prospects, this type of segmentation is the perfect opportunity for audience targeting.</span></p>
<p><b>Instagram advertising</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">With its visual format, you may consider Instagram to be a predominantly millennial thing. That being said, </span><a href="https://www.smartinsights.com/social-media-marketing/social-media-strategy/new-global-social-media-research/"><span style="font-weight: 400;">according to Smart Insights</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">, Instagram has one of the most engaged user bases. This makes it a perfect platform for influencer marketing. However, you don’t have to be an influencer or employ your own to enjoy its benefits. By using relevant hashtags, your posts can reach a considerable amount of people and drive traffic to your online store.</span></p>
<p><b>Pinterest marketing</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">From Promoted Pins to Buyable Pins, this social network offers a lot of opportunities for you to achieve your first online sale. The database is </span><a href="https://business.pinterest.com/en/"><span style="font-weight: 400;">mostly comprised of female users</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">, and according to HootSuite, have </span><a href="https://blog.hootsuite.com/pinterest-statistics-for-business/"><span style="font-weight: 400;">disposable income</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Using Pinterest is much like scrapbooking. Users create boards where they save pins based on different themes. It is widely used for event planning, saving interesting articles, and curating a wardrobe.</span></p>
<h2 id="outreach">Outreach</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Advertising your brand alone won’t drive the amount of traffic you are looking to reach. You need to build credibility for your brand, and the best way to do so is through partnerships and collaborations with other people. Below are a couple of ways to achieve this: </span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Write a guest post</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; If you consider yourself to be an expert on a topic, share your expertise through a guest post. Putting a link to your shop in your bio is a perfect way to make your first sale online.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Ask for product reviews</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; Many brands, especially those just starting out, give their product(s) to bloggers for free in exchange for reviews and a chance to market in front of other people’s audiences.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Send free samples to influencers</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The internet is packed with bloggers, journalists, entrepreneurs, and vloggers. They come from a huge array of industries and niches. Most of them have a large base of followers on social media as well as a loyal audience on their sites.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Sending a free sample of your product to influencers within your industry is a win-win situation. On one hand, you show them that you appreciate their work, while on the other hand, you may be mentioned on one of their platforms. This results in a huge credibility boost followed by a spike in social media followers; thus traffic to your online store.</span></p>
<p><b>Start your own blog</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Running a blog associated with your store is a great way to take advantage of the limitless capabilities of content marketing. Producing free and valuable content creates trust with your customers and keeps them informed. At the same time, this also gives you the opportunity to share content on social media and boost your SEO rank.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The most frequently asked questions about your product and industry are the perfect starting point. Use your blog to answer these questions in separate articles and soon you will notice just how powerful content marketing can be as your social media shares start to increase.</span></p>
<p><b>Keep an eye on Google Analytics</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Gaining insight into the behavior of your audience will help you understand what improvements need to be made in order to increase sales. Analytics will show you how frequently users enter your website, which pages they enter, how much time they spend on certain pages, and which route they took to exit. Best of all, Google Analytics’ services are completely free. It is vital to your business to dedicate a portion of time to analyze traffic in order to increase presence and drive sales.</span></p>
<h2 id="outshine">Outshine your competitors with comparison shopping engines</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">People tend to shop around before deciding to buy a product. Comparison shopping engines compare a large number of stores and products simultaneously. To be successful play by the rules of each engine and stay competitive with pricing, while simultaneously figuring out which gives you the best ROI. Here are some of the most popular comparison shopping engines:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Google Shopping</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">PriceGrabber</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Shopping.com</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Shopzilla</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Become</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Bing Shopping Campaigns</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Pronto</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Bizrate</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Amazon Sponsored Products</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Camelcamelcamel</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">ShopMania</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">BuyVia</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">ShopSavvy</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Yahoo Shopping</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Pricepirates</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">MyShopping Datafeed</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Idealo</span></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Final thoughts</strong></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">We at Alpha Efficiency understand that starting your first online store can be an overwhelming experience. However, having a solid plan can take the pressure off and enable you to make your first online sale in no time. With the right approach, you will need no more than a handful of strategies we have previously discussed. Taking advantage of what social media has to offer will allow your business to easily adapt and turn your prospects into customers. With this in mind,  blogging and producing engaging content will drive loyal customers eager to give you their business. To finish, remember to keep in mind the importance of Google Analytics and plan your steps accordingly.</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/sell-online.png',NULL,'[]','[318]','2021-06-04T09:30:37','2021-06-04T09:30:37',2022,3,1),
  (14777,'/6-most-profitable-digital-products-to-sell-in-2021','6-most-profitable-digital-products-to-sell-in-2021','post','blog','6 Most Profitable Digital Products to Sell in 2021','6 Most Profitable Digital Products to Sell in 2021 | Alpha Efficiency','With so many digital products to sell online, our team has provided which ones are worth your time in 2021 along with some common challenges.','https://alphaefficiency.com/6-most-profitable-digital-products-to-sell-in-2021',1,'Due to the growing popularity of digital products, many companies build their businesses around these intangible goods. From music to videos, ebooks to online courses, they have found their way into the homes of countless consumers worldwide. Trading digital products is a low-cost way to open a new stream of income since these types of &hellip; Continued','<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Due to the growing popularity of digital products, many companies build their businesses around these intangible goods. From music to videos, ebooks to online courses, they have found their way into the homes of countless consumers worldwide.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Trading digital products is a low-cost way to open a new stream of income since these types of products can be created once and sold over and over again without having to replenish any inventory. Whether you have dreams of making it big or are simply looking for a passive income stream, diversifying your revenue is a smart thing to do. In today’s article, our <a href="/">digital marketing agency here in Chicago</a> will guide you through some of the most profitable digital products to sell in 2021.</span></p>
<p><strong>Table of Contents: </strong></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#what">What are digital products</a></li>
<li><a href="/#top">Top reasons for selling digital products</a></li>
<li><a href="/#challenges">Challenges to overcome</a></li>
<li><a href="/#which">Which digital products to sell in 2021</a></li>
<li><a href="/#where">Where to sell your digital products</a></li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/6-Most-Profitable-Digital-Products-.png" alt="" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>

<h2 id="what"><strong>What are digital products?</strong></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Digital products are software-enabled intangible products. They often come in the form of downloadable or streamable digital files (MP3, PDF, videos, plugins…). Basically, it is any virtual item that can be downloaded, streamed, or transformed into a physical product through technological devices.</span></p>
<h3 id="top"><strong>Top reasons for selling digital products </strong></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Selling digital products offer many advantages, especially when compared to trading physical goods:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Low investment/high ROI</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; You don’t have to be tech-savvy or have an entire team behind you to create digital products. Sometimes all you need is time and creativity. When it comes to ebooks, for example, you don’t have any printing costs; all you need to do is write and upload it. This opens up the potential for higher profit margins.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>No need for a physical store, inventory, and shipping</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; E-commerce marketplaces are relatively cheap compared to renting a physical store. Since the item you are selling is intangible, you can forget about storing and shipping costs, as well as the logistics.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>More profitable than physical products</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; Not only can you sell digital products at higher margins, but that margin also has the ability to increase over time since you don’t need any extra money to create more units.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Automated delivery</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; Even if you spend most of your time doing your regular full-time job, automated delivery will keep a constant cash flow.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Serving a niche</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; Serving a specific target audience is much easier than competing on a larger scale. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Shifting towards online education</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; As more and more businesses shift online, the demand for digital products is skyrocketing. The global online education market is estimated to reach </span><a href="https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2020/04/16/2017102/0/en/Global-Online-Education-Market-Worth-319-Billion-by-2025-North-America-Anticipated-to-Provide-the-Highest-Revenue-Generating-Opportunities.html"><span style="font-weight: 400;">$319+ billion by the year 2025</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></li>
</ul>
<h3 id="challenges"><strong>Challenges to overcome </strong></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">When looking for digital products to sell in 2021, it is important to consider the challenges that trading these types of goods may bring:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Competing with free content </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; No matter what type of digital product(s) you choose to sell, there are usually free alternatives online. This is why you need to carefully choose your niche, produce high-quality products, and employ a strategy to raise awareness about your brand.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Susceptibility to piracy</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; When it comes to digital products, there is always a risk of piracy. However, it can be avoided or at least reduced if you employ the right tools and steps to protect your intellectual property.</span></li>
</ul>
<h3 id="which"><strong>Which digital products to sell in 2021?</strong></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">With so many digital products to sell, we have provided you with a plethora of insight into the different categories you can sell online.</span></p>
<p><b>Ebooks</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">You don’t have to be a bestselling writer to write an ebook. As long as you have some knowledge to share, you qualify.  With people constantly searching for more knowledge, ebooks have shown to be one of the best digital products to sell. All that an ebook needs are a few relevant images, and quality text for your specific audience. Think about how you can share your expertise with others and transform it into writing.</span></p>
<p><b>Online courses</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Online courses, like ebooks, are all about turning your expertise into a source of revenue. Combine it with a passion for sharing and creativity, and you have the perfect digital product to sell.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Whether it’s a new hobby or simply looking for ways to advance professionally, people like learning from the comfort of their own homes. To get yourself in the best position to create an engaging educational course, start with learner outcomes. In other words, think about what you want your online students to know or be able to do at the end of the course. From there you can incorporate quizzes or different interactive activities, anything that helps you and your students break up the content and make studying fun.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Below are some areas of expertise that when translated into online courses, make perfect digital products to sell:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Sewing</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Yoga</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Guitar or any other instrument lessons</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Meditation</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Dance classes</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Resumes</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Job search</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Professional development</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Photography</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Copywriting</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Graphic design</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Arts and crafts</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Online courses are not limited to education. You can also tap into your customers’ own potential after the sale and teach transformative ways for how they can improve. </span></p>
<p><b>Memberships</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Rather than selling individual digital products, you may choose to bundle them together. Disclosing these products behind a paid subscription is a great way to generate a steady inflow of revenue. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This approach is extremely popular among those who maintain a growing library of premium content since it allows them to nurture a community of members and cash in their content marketing efforts. As your content is accessible to your paying subscribers, you can also host exclusive content available for download as well as streaming.</span></p>
<p><b>Graphic design</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">As an agency that offers <a href="/ecommerce-web-design-services">web design services</a>, we are aware that there are many designers out there on a tight schedule and in search of the right elements necessary to complete their work. If you are a passionate designer, then your toolbox is likely to be packed with everything you need to produce attractive digital products to sell. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">From vector icons and textures to objects and typefaces, you are only limited by your imagination and the time you set aside. There is an array of products that can generate passive income while you continue your day-to-day work with your clients.</span></p>
<p><b>Digital templates</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Whether you are a blogger using <a href="/sage-framework-wordpress">Sage WordPress theme</a> or a couple looking for that perfect wedding invitation, templates get the job done fast. From designing a website to designing a business card, professionals use templates to complete tasks that either falls out of their area of expertise or require a substantial amount of time to finish. Here are some of the templates you could sell:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Digital marketing strategy templates</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Business planning templates</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Excel templates</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Business contracts</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">WordPress themes</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">PowerPoint presentations</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Mobile apps</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Graphic design templates for brochures, flyers, posters, business cards…</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Resume templates</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Stock photos</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Websites, blogs, and media platforms all have one thing in common &#8211; a need for premium high-quality stock photos. This makes them one of the most profitable digital products to sell in 2021. If you have an eye for light, color, and framing, you can either work with websites like Fotolia, Unsplash, and iStockphoto, or choose to sell images on your own website.</span></p>
<h3 id="where"><strong>Where to sell your digital products</strong></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">You should choose your selling platform based on items you plan to sell and your budget. The usefulness and the appearance of your digital store are also important factors to take into consideration. There are two options to choose from: </span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Selling through your own site</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Selling through marketplaces</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Selling through your own site</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">E-commerce platforms like <a href="https://shopify.com">Shopify</a> offer the option to create your own digital store and customize it with your unique brand. You also have full control over how much you wish to charge for your products. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For example, Shopify’s monthly prices start at $29 with a payment processing of 2.9% + 30¢ USD. For that price, you get the option to store unlimited products, free templates, and 24/7 customer support.</span></p>
<p><b>Selling through marketplaces</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Marketplaces like <a href="https://amazon.com">Amazon</a> are great for reaching more consumers, but they take a big cut of your profits in return. You also have no control over your branding whatsoever, and your competitor’s products are listed alongside yours.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For example, Amazon charges $39.99 per month for their Professional Plan, plus $0.15 per digital item, plus a $1.80 closing fee for each book, music, or video item you sell.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">On the other hand, marketplaces can be a great marketing channel to complement your digital store. They are perfect for generating leads which can then drive larger purchases or subscriptions to your store. </span></p>
<p><b>Final thoughts</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">To conclude, we hope that we have given you a solid idea of where to start. Once you know your strengths, decide which digital product(s) to sell, and jump to the development process as soon as possible. Keep in mind that your product needs to offer quality value to your consumers. With a combination of creative marketing, choose the platform that suits your business needs and get started.</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/6-Most-Profitable-Digital-Products-.png',NULL,'[]','[318]','2021-06-10T19:12:03','2021-06-10T19:12:03',1499,3,1);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (wp_id,path,slug,type,track,title,meta_title,meta_description,canonical,robots_index,excerpt,body_html,hero_image,wp_template,tags,categories,published_at,updated_at,word_count,internal_links,image_count) VALUES
  (14805,'/free-stock-image-websites-that-will-help-you-embellish-your-blog-pages','free-stock-image-websites-that-will-help-you-embellish-your-blog-pages','post','blog','Free Stock Image Websites To Help You Embellish Your Blog Pages','Free Stock Image Websites To Help You Embellish Your Blog Pages |','Get ahead of the curve with these key fundamentals to help guide you on your journey to optimizing your website.','https://alphaefficiency.com/free-stock-image-websites-that-will-help-you-embellish-your-blog-pages',1,'Photography is one of the crucial parts of web design. Our brains process images 60,000 times faster than text, this means that your creative content plays a major role in engaging your followers. Recently, stock photography has developed a bad reputation due to cliché pictures of men in corporate suits shaking hands or those of &hellip; Continued','<p>Photography is one of the crucial parts of web design. Our brains process images <a href="https://www.fastcompany.com/3035856/why-were-more-likely-to-remember-content-with-images-and-video-infogr">60,000 times faster than text</a>, this means that your creative content plays a major role in engaging your followers. Recently, stock photography has developed a bad reputation due to cliché pictures of men in corporate suits shaking hands or those of absurdly happy people receiving a loan from a bank. Regardless of this type of content, the truth is that free stock image websites create a competitive environment for photographers. These websites are constantly on the lookout for those who possess the perfect framing, motives, and lighting techniques.</p>
<p><strong>Table of Contents </strong></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#about">About Licenses</a></li>
<li><a href="/#image">Free Stock Image Websites</a></li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/free-stock-photo-websites.png" alt="" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>

<p>Over the years there has been a growing number of<a href="/10-mind-blowing-statistics-about-great-websites"> mind-blowing websites</a> with exceptional imagery offered free of cost. Our <a href="/">digital marketing agency here in Chicago</a> has done its own research to better inform you on the websites that offer free stock images to embellish in your blog pages and give you that wow factor.</p>
<h2>About Licenses</h2>
<p>While visiting the following websites, you will find photographs that are free of copyright restrictions or licenses. Regardless, we strongly suggest that you read the terms and conditions of each website you visit so you know when and what type of attribution is required.</p>
<h3>What are Creative Commons?</h3>
<p>Creative Commons is a nonprofit organization that allows users to share knowledge and creativity through free legal tools. There are several types of Creative Commons licenses. Some allow offer no restrictions or required attributions, others allow only certain uses and no changes.</p>
<h3>What is Public Domain?</h3>
<p>Public domain is a summary of works with expired, forfeited, or inapplicable copyrights. However, keep in mind that just because something is on the internet doesn’t mean that it is also in the public domain.</p>
<h3>What is Royalty-Free?</h3>
<p>Images that are “royalty-free” aren’t necessarily free. It means that you don’t have to pay royalties to the owner every time you use an image(s). However, you usually do have to pay a one-time fee for rights to use the image if you’re planning to use it as many times as you wish.</p>
<h2>Free Stock Image Websites</h2>
<p>Now that we have clarified all the perplexities about licensing, let’s get back to the subject of our article. Here are our top picks for the best free stock image websites.</p>
<p><strong>StockSnap.io</strong></p>
<p><a href="https://stocksnap.io/" rel="nofollow">StockSnap.io</a> has a huge database filled with beautiful free stock photos and high-resolution images. Their search feature enables easy browsing through countless images available. You can also search for the most popular photos since the website tracks both views and downloads. With hundreds of new photos being added every day, they are all released under creative commons with no attribution required.</p>
<p><strong>Pexels</strong></p>
<p>This website offers free high-quality stock images licensed under the Creative Commons Zero (CC0) license. All of their images are nicely tagged, and easy to search for and discover through the website’s discover page.</p>
<p><strong>Unsplash</strong></p>
<p><a href="https://unsplash.com/">Unsplash</a> is one of the most popular free stock image websites. The website harbors a huge collection of free high-resolution photographs released under the Unsplash license. Their team of professionals goes through new submissions daily and features only the very best images on their home page.</p>
<p><strong>Burst (by Shopify)</strong></p>
<p>Shopify launched <a href="https://burst.shopify.com/">Burst</a> to help entrepreneurs embellish their product pages, websites, and marketing campaigns. Their photos are also free, with some being licensed under Creative Commons Zero and others falling under Shopify’s photo license. While you can find more general photos on this website, most of them were taken indoors to serve different business niches.</p>
<p><strong>Reshot</strong></p>
<p><a href="https://www.reshot.com/">Reshot</a> has a large library of unique handpicked free stock images that are free to use both commercially and editorially, with no attribution required. In the introduction of this article, we mentioned how the internet is full of cliché stock photos. This website was built to fight that trend with amazing images made for startups, freelancers, and makers alike.</p>
<p><strong>Pixabay</strong></p>
<p><a href="https://pixabay.com/">Pixabay</a> provides a collection of free stock images, vectors, and art illustrations licensed under Creative Commons Zero.</p>
<p><strong>FoodiesFeed</strong></p>
<p><a href="https://www.foodiesfeed.com/">FoodiesFeed</a> is a perfect fit for food bloggers as it offers thousands of free high-resolution photographs of different kinds of food.</p>
<p><strong>Gratisography</strong></p>
<p>This website features amazing pictures captured in high resolution by Ryan McGuire of Bells Design. New photos are added every week. They are free of copyright restrictions and perfect for both personal and commercial projects.</p>
<p><strong>Freestocks.org</strong></p>
<p>Freestocks.org provides numerous high-quality images. All of them fall under the Creative Commons CC0 license.</p>
<p><strong>Pictography</strong></p>
<p>Pictography is a website filled with amazing free stock images released under Creative Commons Zero. Photos are submitted by Dave Meier and many other photographers.</p>
<p><strong>Canva</strong></p>
<p><a href="https://www.canva.com/">Canva</a> is an online graphic design tool. However, it also offers free stock photos that can easily be turned into a custom graphic that can then be used on social media or your blog pages. Whether you gravitate towards <a href="/mobile-first-web-design-an-overlooked-profit-opportunity">mobile-first web design</a> or desktop websites, Canva should have a special place in your toolbox.</p>
<p><strong>Getty Images</strong></p>
<p><a href="https://www.gettyimages.com/">Getty Images</a> provides photos for you to use on your non-commercial websites for free by embedding them. However, downloading pictures and uploading them to your website is not allowed. Embedding pictures is very different than simply adding them. Embedded pictures keep their own frame, share buttons, and branding.</p>
<p><strong>PicJumbo</strong></p>
<p><a href="https://picjumbo.com/">PicJumbo</a> entertains a large library of various pictures that you can use for free with no registration required. If you choose to subscribe to their newsletter, you can get new free images every so often. We are bending the rules lightly, but with a bit of extra budget to spare, you will gain access to their premium photo collections. Here, you can even find vertical images perfect for your Stories content.</p>
<p><strong>iStock</strong></p>
<p>This website uploads a ton of new free stock images every week which you can access by signing up for a free membership.</p>
<p><strong>StyleStock</strong></p>
<p>StyledStock is oriented towards female entrepreneurs. They offer a collection of feminine stock photography free for both commercial and personal use.</p>
<p><strong>Final words</strong></p>
<p>The web offers a ton of amazing free stock image websites, along with new ones every day. Whether you are a designer, marketer, or blogger, there are so many options to choose from. Not having to rely on cliché stock imagery is certainly a blessing. Stock photography is gaining positive recognition. We love it, our clients and visitors love it, and your visitors are sure to love it too.</p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/free-stock-photo-websites.png',NULL,'[]','[166,318]','2021-06-18T15:11:55','2021-06-18T15:11:55',1064,3,1),
  (14822,'/designing-ui-for-web-apps','designing-ui-for-web-apps','post','blog','Designing UI for web apps doesn’t need to be a nightmare','Designing UI for web apps doesn’t need to be a nightmare |','Our team of design professionals have come up with 7 core principles to ease the process towards creating your unique UI design for your business.','https://alphaefficiency.com/designing-ui-for-web-apps',1,'The user interface design is inextricably linked to the creation of the user&#8217;s experience. In a way, UI determines the quality of the user experience, in most cases &#8211; it&#8217;s not only the app&#8217;s visual impression but the feeling associated with it as well. Although it might sound like an ordeal, strengthening the visual aspect &hellip; Continued','<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The user interface design is inextricably linked to the creation of the user&#8217;s experience. In a way, UI determines the quality of the user experience, in most cases &#8211; it&#8217;s not only the app&#8217;s visual impression but the feeling associated with it as well. Although it might sound like an ordeal, strengthening the visual aspect of an app doesn&#8217;t imply numerous complicated elements, but rather &#8211; simple, elegant, and easily navigable designs. Still, sometimes attaining simplicity can be a very complex process.</span></p>
<p><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/UI-design--1024x768.png" alt="Designing UI for web apps" width="1024" height="768" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>Table of Contents:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#what">What is the User Interface (UI) Design?</a></li>
<li><a href="/#core">The 7 Core UI Principles that Make Up a Great User Interface</a></li>
<li><a href="/#how">How Visual Interface Design Supports UI</a></li>
<li><a href="/#goals">Ultimate Goals of UI Design</a></li>
</ul>
<h5 id="what"><b>What is the User Interface (UI) design?</b></h5>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">To be pedantic, UI is defined as a human-first approach to designing the aesthetic experience of a product. It applies to digital products only, unlike UX design, which can also be used for physical products.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">UI determines how your customer will interact with your product or service via visual touchpoints that inspire the desired action. A quality UI means that a specific web app will function flawlessly and that the overall aesthetics will speak in favor of your business. A worthy UI also implies designing an intuitive and easy-to-use interface representing a particular business&#8217;s specific branding strategy.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This is why our <a href="/web-development-agency-chicago">web development agency in Chicago</a> decided to present you with 7 core UI principles that make up top-level User Interfaces to provide the best user experience to your customers.</span></p>
<h5 id="core"><b>The 7 Core UI Principles that Make Up a Great User Interface</b></h5>
<ol>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Clarity</b><b><br />
</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">The very first principle every quality UI designer will follow is &#8220;simplicity&#8221;. All UI design elements such as language, visual content, flow, or hierarchy, need to be convenient and effortless to use, providing your customer with a great user experience.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Conciseness</b><b><br />
</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">The second principle is directly linked to the first one &#8211; conciseness. Conciseness and Clarity allow you to use less and focus more on the aesthetic and usability. A wide range of different elements placed on a screen can confuse users, preventing them from finding what they actually want or need. This is why you should not insist on too many elements when designing a UI for web applications.   </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Familiarity</b><b><br />
</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Designing a UI for web applications implies designing the user experience, which in turn means fulfilling the user&#8217;s subconscious and conscious expectations of how the app should function. A quality UI design will provide the user with a sense of familiarity with the app, even if they are just seeing it for the first time. When we work on E-commerce web design, for example, we input commonly accepted symbols such as &#8220;x&#8221; for exit from the app or &#8220;+&#8221; for adding a product in the chart.  </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Responsiveness</b><b><br />
</b><a href="https://xd.adobe.com/ideas/principles/web-design/responsive-web-design-2/"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Responsiveness</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">, in terms of UI design for web applications, means that all visual elements of the interface will react differently based on screen size, whether it be a smartphone, PC, MAC, or tablet. In this way, all elements of the app are optimized regardless of the platform. </span><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br />
</span><span style="font-weight: 400;">Responsiveness also has to do with the loading speed of the web app and reducing the interface to its simplest form to provide instantaneous interactivity with the user.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Consistency</b><b><br />
</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">The whole UI design should serve one goal, to provide consistent visual and brand identity that is able to function regardless of device. Consistency requires user-friendliness and intuitive design whose aesthetic will speak positively of said product or brand. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Aesthetics</b><b><br />
</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Aesthetics are there to encompass and unify all the elements. Creating aesthetics is a specific UI design process that is actually meant to create such content for not only the product but the service and website as a whole. Since the UI design is mostly data-driven decisions are guided based on what works, what doesn&#8217;t, and what could improve. Naturally, these answers will effect the aesthetics of the final product.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Efficiency</b><b><br />
</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Enabling the user to be more productive on a certain web app is how great UI design can directly impact an app&#8217;s efficiency. When we try to measure the productivity level of a UI design, we analyze the app’s interface design and use of the screen area against the interactions users are having with it. Is the web app too cluttered or busy? Is it too complicated to use? How can it motivate the user to use it more often and for longer sessions? Answering these questions will demonstrate a certain app&#8217;s functionality, efficiency, and potential bugs. In turn, these results will ultimately shed light on what could be improved.</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br />
</span><b>Bonus Tip that can Boost App’s Efficiency:</b><b><br />
</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Forming Help, FAQ pages, or a knowledge base can be helpful for users who are not familiar with your app and need extra support. This will facilitate the app&#8217;s usage, giving them the freedom to master the process on their own without getting stuck.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">However, be aware that designing and changing each element means you&#8217;re affecting another. Therefore the UI design should be observed as a system that entails a multitude of decisions on how an app should look and function, so the user has the best experience and interacts to its maximum potential. </span></p>
<h5 id="how"><b>How Visual Interface Design Supports UI</b></h5>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Visual interface design is a specific process that influences the final look of the web app&#8217;s interface and how the users interpret it on the screen of their smartphone, tablet, computer, or any other device. The goal of visual interface design is to communicate the meaning of a product and intuitively guide the navigation and interaction throughout the web app. This goal is achieved by combining typography, color palettes, animations, buttons, icons, and loading indicators, to create visuals that portray what the application is intended for and how it operates.</span></p>
<h5 id="goals"><b>Ultimate Goals of UI Design </b></h5>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The ultimate goal of UI design is to create aesthetically alluring products that catch the eye of the customer and speak in favor of the brand’s strengths and assets. Designing UI for web applications is a continuous process. It requires constant evaluation of user&#8217;s expectations, research and analysis, and implementation of all conclusions into a web app interface. Following these insights and associated steps will enable you to implement regular improvements towards your web app&#8217;s growth.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">When designing a UI for web applications, functionality, technical constraints, trends, and user expectations are the core elements we take care of at our web design agency here in Chicago. Since this is an ever-evolving process, a quality UI design implies frequent adjustments made to all previously mentioned elements. If handled in an efficient manner, these adjustments will positively impact your website&#8217;s ROI and your business&#8217;s profits overall &#8211; all while providing your customers with a comfortable and enjoyable experience while utilizing your app.</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/UI-design-.png',NULL,'[]','[357,353]','2021-06-24T12:21:49','2021-06-24T12:21:49',1123,1,1),
  (14834,'/figma-on-ipad-pro','figma-on-ipad-pro','post','blog','Turn Your iPad Into a Designing Tool: Figma on iPad Pro','Turn Your iPad Into a Designing Tool: Figma on iPad Pro | Alpha Efficiency','A third-party app called Figurative for iOS has set the golden standard for using Figma on iPad Pro. Your answer for efficiency on the go.','https://alphaefficiency.com/figma-on-ipad-pro',1,'Wondering what is the most effective way to use Figma on iPad Pro? Whether it&#8217;s sketching out ideas while sipping coffee at a café or making quick edits during a commute, the idea of turning an iPad into a powerful design tool is incredibly appealing. However, if you&#8217;ve tried using Figma on an iPad before, &hellip; Continued','<p>Wondering what is the most effective way to use Figma on iPad Pro?</p>
<p>Whether it&#8217;s sketching out ideas while sipping coffee at a café or making quick edits during a commute, the idea of turning an iPad into a powerful design tool is incredibly appealing.</p>
<p>However, if you&#8217;ve tried using Figma on an iPad before, you might have faced some challenges. From struggling with browser-based limitations to missing out on essential features, iPad Pro Figma combination can quickly frustrate you if you don&#8217;t approach it properly.</p>
<p>I’ve found a solution that works smoothly for me and my team at my <a href="/">web design agency</a>.</p>
<p>In this article, I&#8217;ll show you <strong>how to take full advantage of the Figma app on iPad Pro</strong>. You&#8217;ll discover a third-party app that makes iPad Pro Figma combination enjoyable, and <strong>best practices for creating designs on the go</strong>.</p>
<p>But before you dive in, you might also want to check out my <strong>free mini-course</strong>, <a href="https://get.alphaefficiency.com/7-days-to-profitable-aeshtetics">7 Days to Profitable Aesthetics</a>. In seven lessons, delivered directly to your email inbox, you&#8217;ll learn <strong>common mistakes designers make that lead to low conversion rates</strong> (and how to avoid them on time), plus <strong>evergreen principles for increasing online sales by up to 50%</strong>.</p>
<h5>Table of Contents:</h5>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#app">A Third-Party App I Use For Working On Figma Files on iPad Pro</a></li>
<li><a href="/#perform">Figurative performance </a></li>
<li><a href="/#works">Figure works best with an external keyboard </a></li>
<li><a href="/#other">Other use cases </a></li>
</ul>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/figma-on-ipad-1024x768.png" alt="Figma on iPad Pro" width="1024" height="768" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h2 id="app">A Third-Party App I Use For Working On Figma Files on iPad Pro</h2>
<p>Created by Matías Martínez, a third-party app called <a href="https://figurative.design/">Figurative</a> for iOS has really set the golden standard for using <a href="https://figma.com/">Figma</a> on iPad Pro. It has easily emerged as the best option for using Figma on iPadOS 14.5 and higher. Being the game-changer that it is, Figurative completely eliminates the need to access Figma through Chrome or Safari for iPad.</p>
<p>This app has really made life easier for my team and I<a href="/">.</a> Whether we are relaxing by Lake Michigan or returning from the gym, Figurative has enabled us to be more mobile and efficient on the go.</p>
<p>These are some of the features I have found to be the most prominent:</p>
<ul>
<li aria-level="1"><strong>Custom fonts</strong> – Before Figurative, the only way to access custom fonts in Figma on iPad was through a Figma enterprise account. Using this app allows you to access all the fonts previously installed from custom profiles. This has opened a world of options for iOS interface designers.</li>
<li aria-level="1"><strong>Export options </strong>– The familiar iOS share panel that Figurative uses for exports give you more flexibility.</li>
<li aria-level="1"><strong>Optimized screen design </strong>– Figurative supports multiple tabs while eliminating the need for a URL field, which significantly saves your screen real estate. Incorporating <a href="/mobile-first-web-design-an-overlooked-profit-opportunity">mobile-first web design</a> enables screen scaling. This allows users to see more of the canvas, equally benefiting, regardless if they’re using a smaller screen like an iPad or connecting to an external monitor.</li>
<li aria-level="1"><strong>Apple Pencil compatibility </strong>– Figurative makes using Apple Pencil with Figma on iPad flow seamlessly. It easily beats the option of using Chrome for iPad and requesting the mobile website for Figma.</li>
<li aria-level="1"><strong>Touch shortcuts </strong>– The app provides quick touch-friendly shortcuts for useful actions like deleting and duplicating objects. Though it is very helpful to have a keyboard, it makes work much easier for those that have to edit something on the go by using Figma on iPad.</li>
<li aria-level="1"><strong>Undo and redo gestures</strong> – Before Figurative was developed, users often struggled with accidentally moving objects around. Figurative overcame this problem by incorporating a simple multi-finger tap to undo or redo actions.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="perform">Figurative performance</h3>
<p>Though Figma relies heavily on the GPU, the iPad Pro has proven to be powerful enough to handle tasks, such as rendering, without too much trouble.</p>
<p>However, <strong>one of the Figma issues I&#8217;ve faced</strong> while using Figma on iPad Pro is Figurative’s need to <strong>occasionally reload tabs in the middle of work</strong>. Figma announced at Config Europe that it was improving file size memory. However, this has yet to translate into better performance on iPad.</p>
<p>Another thing that Figurative<strong> struggles with is handling large Figma files</strong>. For example, 145,000 layers and 0.19 G memory files fail to load properly. Truth be told, this is also the case with both Chrome for iPad and Safari, so maybe Figurative is not the one to blame. To overcome this problem, you will need to manage file sizes and split your work into smaller chunks.</p>
<p>The desktop app is still necessary if you plan to code your own plugins. Though many plugins run like a charm, those that require a desktop interface to function properly won’t work with Figma on iPad Pro.</p>
<p><strong>As I&#8217;ve already mentioned, Figurative supports the use of Apple Pencil.</strong></p>
<p>This makes it the only app that allows using Figma on iPad without a mouse or keyboard. Figurative easily recognizes whether you are using your fingers or the pencil and will respond accordingly. The app doesn’t allow you to create and edit objects by using just your fingers. However, we suggest turning off the Scribble feature to provide the best possible performance.</p>
<p><strong>I was amazed by freehand drawing performance</strong> with near-zero latency on iPadOS 14.5 or higher during our testing.</p>
<p>If you wish to use Figma on iPad Pro connected to an external monitor, USB-C Digital AV Multiport Adapter might be just what you need. This adapter lets you mirror the display to an external HDMI-compatible monitor and charge your battery at the same time.</p>
<p>Figurative supports both wired keyboard and mouse (if you have a USB-C to USB adapter) as well as Bluetooth. However, the iPad Pro Magic Keyboard is a much more mobile solution.</p>
<h3 id="works">Figma works best with an external keyboard</h3>
<p>Here is why I strongly recommend using an external keyboard with Figma on iPad:</p>
<ul>
<li aria-level="1">Actions such as nudging objects or copying and pasting are much easier to do via keyboard commands</li>
<li aria-level="1">External keyboard eliminates cases of moving objects around accidentally</li>
<li aria-level="1">The external keyboard maximizes canvas viewing space in contrast to the on-screen keyboard</li>
<li aria-level="1">It makes it easy for you to access the modifier keys</li>
<li aria-level="1">It is easier to select multiple items or view context menus</li>
</ul>
<p>We, designers, love keyboard shortcuts. An external keyboard will allow you to manage multiple aspects of Figma design that you simply can not do with touch controls.</p>
<p>It will make the journey of learning <a href="/how-to-use-figma-for-web-design">how to use Figma for web design</a> more enjoyable.</p>
<h3 id="other">Other use cases</h3>
<p>By logging into Figma on both your desktop and iPad, you can use the latter as a Wacom tablet. Though we have noticed a slight delay for the desktop screen to update, this gives you the option to use the iPad Pro along with the Apple Pencil as a second input device.</p>
<p>Sidecar is a feature that allows you to manage multiple Figma windows since it significantly extends your screen real estate. Besides, Apple Pencil shows better performance when the iPad is in Sidecar mode.</p>
<p>You can also run a prototype and editor at the same time simply by running Figurative in multiple windows (either split or float on top). For example, when you&#8217;re creating <a href="/figma-hover-effect">Figma hover effects</a>, all of the changes you make to the editor on iPad will be reflected on a prototype in real-time.</p>
<h2>Final thoughts</h2>
<p>For a device not officially supported by Figma, thanks to Figurative, it is very encouraging to see that it can function so seamlessly on the iPad.</p>
<p>Another big boost that Figma has on iPad Pro is the inclusion of top-of-the-class mouse support on iPadOS.</p>
<p>It seems that we have finally come to the point where we can put our laptops aside and rely on iPads and iPad apps for most of the work on the go.</p>
<p>However, there are still some issues such as large files and browser memory limits. Let’s all keep our fingers crossed for this to be addressed in the near future. I hope that this article has given you yet another, among other reasons, <a href="/top-10-why-iphone">why to get an iPhone</a> or an iPad.</p>
<p>If you&#8217;re serious about <strong>mastering web design so you can start making $10k in additional monthly income</strong>, check out my course, <a href="https://get.alphaefficiency.com/profitable-website-from-scratch">Profitable Websites From Scratch</a>. In this course, I’ll guide you through the <strong>4% of skills that lead to 64% of the results clients value most</strong>. You will be able to consistently create and sell highly sought-after websites to the craving market.</p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/figma-on-ipad.png',NULL,'[]','[166,353]','2021-07-26T11:43:32','2021-07-26T11:43:32',1399,6,1),
  (15076,'/web-design-impacts-seo','web-design-impacts-seo','post','blog','Does Web Design Impacts SEO &#038; Revenue?','Does Web Design Impacts SEO & Revenue? - Alpha Efficiency.™','By paying close attention to details in your web design you are allowing the science of SEO to do its magic for you. ','https://alphaefficiency.com/web-design-impacts-seo',1,'Search engine optimization (SEO), when adequately woven into the fabric of a website, provides higher page rankings on Google. People often ask: Does web design affect SEO? Web Design impacts SEO directly, especially considering that Google relies on Core Web Vitals algorithm update to evaluate the visitors&#8217; user experience they are sending you. In other &hellip; Continued','<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Search engine optimization (SEO), when adequately woven into the fabric of a website, provides higher page rankings on Google. People often ask: Does web design affect SEO? <strong>Web Design impacts SEO</strong> directly, especially considering that Google relies on <a href="/core-web-vitals-update">Core Web Vitals algorithm update</a> to evaluate the visitors&#8217; user experience they are sending you. In other words, it can place your web page on the first search page for its respective keywords. Imagine that your users don&#8217;t have to find themselves having to scroll endlessly to find your site, thereby increasing the traffic to your website. </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">This is where the role of web design steps in. By paying close attention to details in your web design, such as loading speed, Call To Action buttons, and utilizing keywords, you are allowing the science of SEO to do its magic for you.</span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/webdesignseo.png" alt="How Web Design Impacts SEO" width="800" height="512" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h2>Elements to adapt to web design and SEO</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Now that we understand the dynamic between the two, here are some specific elements that set the foundation for a well-optimized website:</span></p>
<h5>Code</h5>
<p>Choice of code is crucial as it has a tremendous impact on all further aspects of your website performance, such as site load and general user experience. It is the single thing that search engines and social media sites can see. With that being said, the matter of coding represents the most crucial aspect of optimizing the search engines and ensuring a high SEO ranking for your website. Without an excellent code function, you lose the opportunity for your website&#8217;s visibility and recognition, significantly affecting the overall user experience and causing potential customers to click off your page. Although using themes or builders may sound convenient, it&#8217;s now clear that <a href="/custom-coded-websites">custom-coded websites</a> are the only way to go if you strive for high quality, scalable, SEO, and PPC-friendly site for your business.<br />
<b></b></p>
<h5>Mobile accessibility<span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span></h5>
<p>Research shows that in this day and age, most of the population access the Internet via their smartphones or tablets due to constant WiFi availability. Without accessibility on a broad range of devices, you lose clicks and visits that might cost your business noticeability and general website traffic, making the search engines uninterested in your page and flunking it to a lower spot on the SEO ranking board. Taking this into account, it is of great importance that your website design and overall content translate well into mobile formats, as that will significantly improve the website&#8217;s SEO and ranking.<br />
<b></b></p>
<h5>Page speed</h5>
<p>The search engine ranking algorithm prefers highly responsive sites, whose said responsiveness dramatically depends on the loading speed of your page. To ensure web traffic, you should pay close attention to this detail as the general population&#8217;s attention span seems to become shorter by the minute. It is possible that users may be impatient or not have access to a good mobile data connection. Ensuring that you&#8217;re not overcrowding your code with unnecessary information will significantly improve the speed at which your page loads, both on desktop and mobile. Additionally, it&#8217;s vital to remember that <a href="/site-speed-and-seo">site speed and SEO</a> are inextricably linked; decreasing your website loading time will positively impact your SEO.<br />
<b></b></p>
<h5>File names and size</h5>
<p>As mentioned previously, loading speed is of colossal significance when ensuring web traffic and an excellent user experience. To further help this problem, focusing on file names and file size is a small but effective way to help search engines take notice of your page and put your photos in context with your site. Another helpful suggestion is to keep file sizes as small as possible. For example, smaller-sized images will look as good as the sizable ones but won&#8217;t take as long to load, keeping the user&#8217;s attention and compelling them to stay on your page.<br />
<b></b></p>
<h5>URL</h5>
<p>It&#8217;s easy for context to get lost in the long stream of the site&#8217;s URL link. To maximize its use, it is highly advised to create a custom URL that will be straight to the point, allowing the SEO algorithm to pick it up faster and rank your page higher. Working out the keywords that are the most related to your content will help you sum down to the most specific URL, which will help the overall placement of your website, not only on the ranking boards but also amongst a particular content niche, making it easier for potential customers to find your business and all you have to offer.<br />
<b></b></p>
<h2>Website structure</h2>
<p>The overall appearance and usability of your website play a crucial role in your search rankings. First impressions are always important. When focusing on the general quality of its service, and especially when aiming for a blog post that ranks highly, your main interests should be:</p>
<h5>Easy use</h5>
<p>A common mistake is overcrowding your website with information, leading to slow load times, especially on mobile devices, and making it hard for potential customers to find what they need. With that being said, your primary focus should be on presenting only the most essential information on the landing page and creating an easy way for your users to get around the site and further learn about what you have to offer. Keep in mind that not everyone is overly familiar with the virtual world and its complicated inner workings. This is a critical ranking factor to consider if you aim to rank higher.</p>
<h5>Simple design</h5>
<p>How your design affects the user experience is pivotal. On the other hand, what might repulse users from further investigating and participating on your page might be the over-the-top design of your webpage. Uniqueness is always welcome, but it&#8217;s crucial to understand how your design affects SEO. Make sure you&#8217;re not scaring users away with poor color coordination, outdated fonts, and an overall shabby and messy appearance. What initially meets the eye is what will lead users to decide if they will stay on your site, so it&#8217;s essential to ensure it is pleasant at first sight.</p>
<h5>Navigation</h5>
<p>Following up the advice on easy use is a well-structured navigation service. Creating a thought-out network of links, avoiding any broken link, and call-to-action buttons, and strategically placing them across the screen will ensure your visit rate and allow the SEO system to pick up on the activity, placing your page higher on the ranking board. The idea is to have a navigation system that flows, allowing your customers and users to surf your webpage mindlessly without having to put too much thought and effort into it.</p>
<h2><span style="font-size: 2rem;">Algorithm updates that are Web design and SEO focused</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">With the growing importance of being well aware of all aspects of your website performance </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">and quality, Internet tools have been created to enable simple tracking and insight, making sure you&#8217;re on top of your game.</span><b></b></p>
<h5>Lighthouse Speed algorithm<span style="font-weight: 400;"><br />
</span></h5>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="https://developers.google.com/web/tools/lighthouse">Google Lighthouse</a> is a free performance analysis tool that allows in-depth insight into crucial areas such as load speed and mobile experience factors that significantly impact your business&#8217;s online presence and user experience. The recently updated process of evaluation is based upon examination of six factors:</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br />
</span></p>
<ul>
<li><b>First Contentful Paint</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">, which marks the time at which the first text or image is painted;</span></li>
<li><b>Time to Interactive</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">, which represents the time it takes for the page to become fully interactive;</span></li>
<li><b>Speed Index</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">, which shows how quickly the contents of the page are visibly populated; </span></li>
<li><b>Largest Contentful Paint</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">, which marks the time at which the most significant text or image is painted;</span></li>
<li><b>Total Blocking time</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">, which represents the summation of overall time spent between First Contentful Paint and Time to Interactive, when the length of a task surpasses 50ms (milliseconds);</span></li>
<li><b>Cumulative Layout Shift</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">, which measures the movement of visible elements that are in the viewport; </span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Lighthouse Speed allows a thorough overview of what your website might be missing and lacking while offering you general information on how your website is overall. This platform is of massive value, considering it is free and constantly evolving to offer you the best service and experience when wanting to improve your website quality.</span><br />
<b></b></p>
<h5>Core Web Vitals</h5>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="/core-web-vitals-update">Core Web Vitals</a> are a variety of metrics used by Google to score the general user experience when loading your webpage. They are a part of Google&#8217;s overall evaluation of &#8220;page experience,&#8221; which, similarly to the previously mentioned Lighthouse Speed, offers you an in-depth overview of how the customers are experiencing your website and its services. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">It is calculated through three main metrics, which are: </span></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Largest Contentful Paint</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (LCP) measures the duration of the loading performance. Meaning the time it takes for the website content to load fully. Statistically, this action should take about 2.5 seconds within the initial page loading;</span></li>
<li><b>First Input Delay </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">(FID), whose role is to measure interactivity. To make sure that users are provided with the best experience, the pages should have an FID of less than 100 milliseconds; </span></li>
<li><b>Cumulative Layout Shift</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> (CLS), which measures visual stability. Have you ever visited a site, and the whole layout shifted with each time something loaded on the page? That means your CLS is bad. It means that there is content that loads after the overall main content. So you see the whole layout load repeatedly, causing it to glitch and move seemingly. To keep this from happening, you must go through your content and eliminate those who lag in loading speed or resize those files so they fall perfectly into the loading process. Generally, pages should maintain a CLS of less than 0,1. </span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Having free access to these ever-evolving platforms certainly makes the job of producing a unique website way easier as it supplies you with all necessary information and data, giving your business&#8217;s website a greater chance of being noticed and picked up by the SEO and ensuring a higher rank on the search boards. </span></p>
<h2>Final thoughts</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">You must pay attention to when building a virtual empire for your business. Web design and SEO are two essential but also highly intricate elements of the website building sphere. Properly utilizing both parties&#8217; aspects will surely lead you to great success for your business, its online presence, and further recognition. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Make sure to <a href="/schedule-a-call">book your meeting</a> with our <a href="/seo-agency-chicago">SEO agency in Chicago</a> which will help you build a bright future for your business. </span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/webdesignseo.png',NULL,'[]','[344,353]','2021-12-09T12:04:55','2021-12-09T12:04:55',1697,6,1),
  (15151,'/how-web-design-can-build-trust-with-customers','how-web-design-can-build-trust-with-customers','post','blog','How Web Design Can Build Trust With Customers','How Web Design Can Build Trust With Customers | Alpha Efficiency','There are so many elements when it comes to Web Design. Here, our team narrows in on the factors that build trust and rapport with your customers.','https://alphaefficiency.com/how-web-design-can-build-trust-with-customers',1,'Design is the first thing that catches the eye of your future customers; it communicates your brand’s personality. When done right, it becomes one of your strongest marketing assets filling in all the blanks where your campaign might have lacked. A design done right sets you apart from your competitors and creates long-lasting emotional connections &hellip; Continued','<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Design is the first thing that catches the eye of your future customers; it communicates your brand’s personality. When done right, it becomes one of your strongest marketing assets filling in all the blanks where your campaign might have lacked. A design done right sets you apart from your competitors and creates long-lasting emotional connections with your consumers. In today’s article, our <a href="/">web design agency here in Chicago</a> walks you through the best ways to build trust with customers through web design. </span></p>
<p><strong>Table of Contents: </strong></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#why">Why is it important to build trust with your customers?</a></li>
<li><a href="/#how">How to build trust with your customers? </a></li>
<li><a href="/#using">Using design to build trust with your customers</a></li>
<li><a href="/#security">Emphasize security and transparency</a></li>
</ul>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/How-to-build-trust-.jpg" alt="" width="800" height="550" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />

<h3>Why is it important to build trust with your customers?</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Today’s market is highly competitive and consumer-driven. Your potential customer is presented with an abundance of branded options for every choice they’re about to make. While one-time customers are valuable and undoubtedly bring profit, recurring customers will push your business to the next level. These are hard to obtain for unknown brands no matter how magnificent their product may be. Their only chance to level the playing field is to constantly strive to build trust with customers. Here are some of the benefits that will build consumers’ trust in your business:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Trust drives conversions</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; For companies running an online business with no means to directly communicate with consumers, earning and sustaining the trust of potential, as well as existing customers is crucial. It is the main factor in converting website visitors into leads and leads into customers.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Increased retention</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; Gaining the trust of your existing customers is the most important step in building strong relationships. Once you manage to bring that relationship to an emotional level, your customers will keep coming back for more products. Besides the obvious benefit mirrored through profit, nurturing existing customers also saves your company’s budget as </span><a href="https://www.huify.com/blog/acquisition-vs-retention-customer-lifetime-value"><span style="font-weight: 400;">it costs five times more to acquire a new customer than to retain an existing one</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Improved loyalty</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> &#8211; Trust boosts loyalty and transforms your customers into spokesmen that spread the word about your brand and establish it as an industry authority. With such an army of devoted advocates, your popularity will increase exponentially attracting more customers thus skyrocketing your revenue. </span></li>
</ul>
<h3>How to build trust with your customers?</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Content marketing and search engine optimization are two of the most important aspects of building customer trust. Engaging, accurate, and optimized content bolsters your reputation and authority leading to increased trust in your business. However, it is just as important to present your content in a professional-looking and aesthetically pleasing way to your website visitors. Whether it’s a blog post or a product description, you need to put a bow on it. In other words, you need to create the right design choices in order to connect with your customers on a more emotional level.</span></p>
<p><b>The Aesthetic-Usability effect</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The </span><a href="https://www.nngroup.com/articles/aesthetic-usability-effect/"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Aesthetic-Usability effect</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> is a term first used by the Nielsen Norman Group. Their research showed that aesthetically pleasing things are perceived as more valuable and easier to use. Now, let’s put this in the context of your site. Beautiful things generate positive emotions and your viewers are more likely to tolerate minor usability issues if they find an interface visually pleasing. This is why companies that have invested in good web design find it easier to build trust with customers. Eye-catching design grabs visitor’s attention and makes the website, as well as the brand itself, look valuable and trustworthy.</span></p>
<h3>Using design to build trust with customers</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Though people say “don’t judge a book by its cover”, this type of assessment has deep roots in human nature. A good design includes so many elements such as color, fonts, and imagery, not to mention numerous behind-the-scenes tweaks that <a href="/mobile-first-web-design-an-overlooked-profit-opportunity">mobile-first web design</a> requires. Just how do you find that golden ratio that instills trust? Well, here is how:</span></p>
<p><b>Lean towards existing trends to boost credibility</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">We are not advising you to follow every web design fad that is released. That would be tiresome and would repel your visitors rather than establish your website as stable and trustworthy. One of the crucial elements of trust-focused web design is conforming to modern design standards. If visitors perceive your design as outdated, they will probably think that there is much more hiding beneath the surface. They might figure that your product is outdated too or that your company is in a downward spiral. Making your website modern-looking shows that you care. When your design choices communicate that your business is in full swing, it becomes easier to appeal to your customers and build that rapport. </span></p>
<p><b>Focus on design consistency</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Keeping the design elements consistent throughout your website is very important if you wish to build trust with your customers. Imagine a website that changes its layout or a color scheme every time you switch to a new page. By adding something as simple as font inconsistencies and you can easily say that there is a circus in town. This can negate your visitors’ trust in a major way. A uniform look represents an uninterrupted stream of thoughts and shows the people behind the company are genuine and care about the well-being of their customers. And that’s exactly the message you want your website to communicate.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Design consistency is best achieved through regular </span><a href="https://www.appcues.com/blog/how-to-design-for-trust-and-keep-users-engaged-for-the-long-haul"><span style="font-weight: 400;">consistency audit</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. Every point of interaction between your website and visitors needs to be consistent in design, features, functionalities, labels, tone, and branding. If you entertain third-party elements, making them look native will provide a seamless experience.</span></p>
<h3>Emphasize security and transparency</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Another way to build trust with customers is to design a layout that puts transparency and security at the forefront. There are a couple of ways to do this:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you have an E-commerce website, design a page layout that draws visitors’ attention to your security policies</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Many enterprise companies have found success in building trust with customers through cleverly designed team and contact info. pages. This gives a company a human face that visitors can relate to</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Use design elements to highlight page sections where you provide elaborate explanations of how you protect your customer data</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Use simple terms and common language when you write about your products and services. Maximizing legibility in this way shows your future customers that you are not hiding any important information</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Remove visual clutter</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">A user-friendly website design breathes trust to visitors. To make your website more user-friendly, make sure to remove all visual interferences that clutter your pages such as unnecessary animations, pop-ups, and ads.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">We understand the business side of it, so we are not suggesting that your website shouldnt contain pop-ups and ads at all. We’re just advising you not to overdo it. By increasing white space, you can effectively direct your visitors where you want them to go; let’s say to your CTA button.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">By keeping the visual noise to a minimum you will provide a better user experience.</span></p>
<p><b>Final thoughts</b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you browse through our blog pages you will find multiple reasons to invest in web design. However, one of the most often overlooked reasons is that well-designed web pages can incite customer trust and help you establish long and meaningful relationships with your clients. Though building trust through web design is an investment, it’s the one that pays dividends in the long haul. A beautifully designed website with engaging content is like a well-oiled conversion machine. Design with your customers in mind. If you give them enough reasons to trust your company, they will have no reason to switch to your competitors.</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/How-to-build-trust-.jpg',NULL,'[]','[318,353]','2021-07-29T12:13:21','2021-07-29T12:13:21',1269,2,1),
  (15408,'/enterprise-wordpress-development','enterprise-wordpress-development','post','blog','5 Essentials for Enterprise WordPress Development','5 Essentials for Enterprise WordPress Development | Alpha Efficiency.™','Steal our winning Enterprise WordPress development guide, which ensures all KPIs and enterprise development demands are met.','https://alphaefficiency.com/enterprise-wordpress-development',1,'Not all WordPress is created equal. In fact, 95.6% of it runs on bloated builders and recycled themes. But when you&#8217;re building for enterprise, those shortcuts don&#8217;t just fall short; they jeopardize performance, compliance, and long-term growth. But enterprises need to go beyond copy-pasted templates and sloppy patchwork. That’s why enterprise websites demand more than &hellip; Continued','<p>Not all WordPress is created equal. In fact, <strong data-start="797" data-end="857">95.6% of it runs on bloated builders and recycled themes</strong>. But when you&#8217;re building for enterprise, those shortcuts don&#8217;t just fall short; they jeopardize performance, compliance, and long-term growth.</p>
<p>But enterprises need to go beyond copy-pasted templates and sloppy patchwork.</p>
<p>That’s why enterprise websites demand more than a pretty UI. They require a framework<strong> explicitly built for enterprise-level demands;</strong> a battle-tested framework designed to:</p>
