<h2></h2>
<h2 id="proper-framework">Choosing the Proper Enterprise WordPress Framework</h2>
<p>Enterprise WordPress websites are much different from 99% of WordPress websites.</p>
<p>They have the special needs listed above, and they require a unique workflow, one that will allow constant iterations without sacrificing speed, ADA &amp; Core Web Vitals compliance.</p>
<p>The natural function of the website is SEO.</p>
<p>Even in the age of AI, we are witnessing an increase in Google searches. And if you want your website to attract relevant mindshare and visibility, it needs to be created with SEO in mind.</p>
<p>Before you choose an agency, choose your foundation.</p>
<p>Enterprise WordPress isn’t like the rest; it requires a flexible framework trusted by names like:</p>
<ul>
<li>UPS</li>
<li>NASA</li>
<li>Target</li>
<li>Coca-Cola</li>
<li>Zillow Blog</li>
<li><a href="https://wordpress.org/showcase/the-white-house/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">White House</a></li>
</ul>
<p>That’s why we use the <strong data-start="2452" data-end="2471"><a href="/sage-framework-wordpress">Sage Framework</a>.</strong></p>
<p>Sage Framework allows for:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Modularity</strong> &#8211; so your website scales effortlessly.</li>
<li><strong>High-speed performance</strong> &#8211; built right into the foundation.</li>
<li><strong>Streamlined code</strong> &#8211; for faster load times and fewer headaches.</li>
<li><strong>Modern development workflow</strong> &#8211; to support continuous iteration.</li>
</ul>
<p>Sage checks off all enterprise boxes, which is why the White House dropped its outdated Drupal website in favor of <strong>WordPress</strong>.</p>
