<li><a href="/#social">Social media</a></li>
<li><a href="/#forums">Forums</a></li>
<li><a href="/#pr">PR</a></li>
<li><a href="/#sem">SEM</a></li>
<li><a href="/#ads">Social and display ads</a></li>
<li><a href="/#offline">Offline advertising</a></li>
<li><a href="/#community">Community building</a></li>
<li><a href="/#events">Live events</a></li>
<li><a href="/#gigs">Speaking gigs</a></li>
<li><a href="/#affiliate">Affiliate programs</a></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><a href="/#outbound">Outbound Lead Generation Channels</a>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#email">Email marketing</a></li>
<li><a href="/#calling">Cold calling</a></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><a href="/#final">Final thoughts</a></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The first paragraph could sum up the fate of many businesses today. Despite their best efforts, and though it often seems like everything is in place, many business owners are yet to see their hard work bring a return on investment. </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Why</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">, you wonder? The answer is simple &#8211; In order to cash in on your efforts, you need a sound lead generation strategy. This is where this guide comes in. Through these lines, we will share our experience and arm you with numerous tips and ideas on how to get more sales leads.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">As a successful <a href="/">digital marketing agency</a>, we generate our leads through a mixture of inbound and outbound marketing channels. For you to get a better understanding of the various strategies, let’s dig deeper into each of these two channels.</span></p>
<h2>Inbound Lead Generation Channels</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">When talking about how to get more sales leads through inbound lead generation, we are referring to content creation and campaigns that generate visitors and convert them into quality leads. Here are some of the most fruitful inbound lead generation techniques and channels.</span></p>
<h3 id="lead">Lead providers</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">To put it as simply as possible, lead providers are platforms that offer leads. However, choosing the right lead provider is not that simple. There are a variety of sources that provide information of different quality. These sources often help you fuel growth by offering B2B contact data for you to identify and connect with your future customers. Buying leads is tricky, and we advise caution since you can end up with leads that are difficult to nurture and convert into customers.</span></p>
<h3 id="seo">Search engine optimization</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Many businesses find search engine optimization the most important part of lead generation. A sound SEO strategy focuses on creating great content and achieving prime optimization so a steady stream of leads can be generated. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Quality leads can not be attracted overnight. SEO is a process that demands a good understanding of the fundamentals. However, if executed properly, many leads will end up on your websites and landing pages through organic search. This makes these leads valuable as they have shown genuine interest in your service or product.</span></p>
<h3 id="content">Content marketing</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Content marketing is the foundation of many lead generation campaigns. This type of marketing is a great way to engage your potential leads as they move through your sales funnel. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">By creating useful content like whitepapers, ebooks, or blog posts, you can educate leads and inspire them to act on your call to action to close deals. Throughout this process, you gather a ton of valuable information that helps you nurture your contacts or even engage them anew if necessary:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Email </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; This is the minimum to ask your future customers for. Email is a great way to contact your lead in a personalized message and engage them in an email marketing campaign.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Name </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; When addressing your lead, “</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Dear John” </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">sounds much better than a generic “</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Dear valued customer.”</span></i></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Company name </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; This can be a very valuable piece of information for any future engagement with the customer in question. By collecting their company name, you can perform background research on your lead’s industry to determine whether or not they can benefit from your offer. Also, it is a great way to determine the best marketing approach.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">You can ask your potential customers for anything you feel may help you communicate with them and personalize your message to ensure maximum relevance. Still, keep in mind that the less info you ask for, the more likely people are to provide it. Always make sure to ask only for the information you actually need.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Content marketing is where you can let your imagination run wild. You can always try and find new and exciting forms of relevant content as well as ways to drive quality leads to that content.</span></p>
<h3 id="social">Social media</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Social media is a huge part of many people’s everyday lives. You, of course, want to be where your potential customers are. Popular social media platforms such as Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, or Twitter can provide a constant stream of leads when appropriately used. They are also an extremely cost-effective tool that brings high ROI.</span></p>
<h3 id="forums">Forums</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Although not quite as flashy of a channel as social media, forums are places where you can find the most engaged people. Many businesses find forums an invaluable lead-generating tool to acquire organic leads. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Platforms like Reddit or Quora have very high traffic numbers. Keep in mind that it is essential to find a way to communicate authentically and organically if you aim to attract new customers through these platforms.</span></p>
<h3 id="pr">PR</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Public relations is not a new-age product. It has always existed in one form or another. Many businesses benefit from public coverage and become even more adept at taking a role in shaping the opinions of future customers. Just like with forums, if you communicate in an authentic and organic way when announcing important news, the subject of conversation is bound to generate intrigue and bring leads. So, whenever something important and newsworthy happens in your company, let the world know, and you will experience a burst of activity.</span></p>
<h3 id="sem">Search engine marketing</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="/seo-agency-chicago">Search engine marketing</a> is essential for boosting the profile and prominence of your website. With over 3.8 million searches that occur on Google every single minute, it is no wonder that every modern business engages with platforms like Google Ads on some level. Having a <a href="/perfect-ppc-strategy">perfect PPC strategy</a> in place is critical for getting your business and brand name recognized far and wide while at the same time collecting leads and watching that ROI skyrocket.</span></p>
<h3 id="ads">Social and display ads</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Despite all the ad blockers and banner blindness, the effectiveness of social and display ads at lead generation is still intact. This is why this type of digital advertising is undoubtedly a strategy to consider when figuring out how to get more sales leads. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Truth be told, it takes a lot of knowledge and experience to set up campaigns that make for a positive return on investment. If this kind of marketing represents uncharted territory for you, make sure to have an expert that is able to optimize your ad spend and make the most of your budget to drive sales and generate qualified leads.</span></p>
<h3 id="offline">Offline advertising</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Throughout this guide, we have been solely focused on marketing in the digital world. This is where we shift our focus for a moment since the physical world also offers amazing opportunities for lead generation. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Though some would consider it a lost art, a simple ad in newspapers or on a radio station is still a very powerful weapon at targeting local audiences. Being familiar with your local community’s needs and wants and using that knowledge to target your customers exactly where they </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">are </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">is the path most successful companies still walk along. Although marketing is shifting towards digital, you really can’t beat offline advertising.</span></p>
<h3 id="community">Community building</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Community building is a fun and rewarding way to interact with your audience while generating and nurturing genuine leads. We have developed as a species through social interactions &#8211; forging bonds over millennia. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Putting the power of social networks in use, you can create strong and vibrant communities that will further legitimize and highlight your brand. This gives you the ability to forge wholehearted connections with your leads and drive real value to them. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For example, creating a Facebook group for your leads to connect and chat with each other as well as get relevant questions in your field of expertise answered is sure to generate a lot of satisfied and returning customers.</span></p>
<h3 id="events">Live events</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Today, event marketing is bigger than ever. As the world turns digital, the appetite for an authentic experience and connections amongst people only grows. While you dwell on how to get more sales leads, we have another great idea for you. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">How about hosting a range of events to attract and engage people? Different seminars on a particular topic or informal events for a good cause can give you an opportunity to create in-person contacts and connections that go beyond company/customer relationships. Nothing is more valuable than the human touch and outreach. These connections are likely to last more than any other you make.</span></p>
<h3 id="gigs">Speaking gigs</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Instead of hosting your own event, why not take part and share your knowledge at different speaking gigs? Many businesses partake in these kinds of events in order to target a huge range of customers and demonstrate their commitment to their industry.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you feel like you can drive value through your unique experiences and abilities, then why not share your knowledge? If your future customers see you as an authority in your field of expertise, you are sure to make strong and authentic connections.</span></p>
<h3 id="affiliate">Affiliate programs</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Affiliate marketing is a strategy that revolves around paying commissions to affiliate websites that, in return, provide you with traffic. Safety is the name of the game here. Since these programs are commission-based, you only pay for the leads you get. At the same time, your partners are incentivized to do their best and provide quality leads for your business. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Although some companies feel that they are putting their reputation at risk by placing their brand name into someone else’s hands, if you choose your partners carefully, this could turn out to be a win-win deal for both of you.</span></p>
<h2 id="outbound">Outbound Lead Generation Channels</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Outbound lead generation is a strategy that involves reaching out to your potential customers directly in an effort to capture their attention. While this can be an extremely powerful tool for getting more sales leads, we advise you to err on the side of caution here since many people may find your direct approach to be disruptive.</span></p>
<h3 id="email">Email marketing</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Sounds a bit retro, right? Actually, 59% of B2B advertisers find it to be the most effective channel when it comes to ROI. With this in mind, it is no wonder that companies dedicate a vast portion of time and resources to cultivating accurate mailing lists. This tactic is perfect for sharing important news and always keeping your clients up to date on what’s cooking in your labs.</span></p>
<h3 id="calling">Cold calling</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">At one time or another, we have all been on the receiving end of these calls or part of <a href="/looking-to-increase-your-conversions-deals-a-step-by-step-guide-to-boost-your-cold-emailing-campaigns">cold email marketing</a> campaign. Many people find this type of advertising to be the most intrusive of all. If it makes you feel better, you should know that the salesperson on the other side of the line is hardly enjoying themselves either. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">There are, however, still some confident and talented salespeople out there that are hardened against rejection and strongly believe in the quality of the product they are selling. Those people are masters of their craft and collect leads for their company on a daily basis.</span></p>
<h2 id="final">Final thoughts</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">We have written nearly 2000 words in this guide with one goal in mind &#8211; to give you the best idea on how to get more sales leads. Here is one more piece of advice to go &#8211; always try to make the lead generation process a positive experience for both you and your potential customers. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Try different approaches. Play with different techniques until you find those that are the best fit for your business. Don’t be afraid to make a mistake every once in a while. You grow and learn as you go. And never forget to bring in a touch of soul.</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/salesleads.png',NULL,'[]','[318]','2022-02-08T09:24:14','2022-02-08T09:24:14',2036,4,1),
  (16968,'/how-to-run-a-google-ads-campaign','how-to-run-a-google-ads-campaign','post','blog','How to Run a Well-Rounded Google Ads Campaign','How to Run a Well-Rounded Google Ads Campaign - Alpha Efficiency','Launching a new Google Ads campaign is an exhilarating process, so we are here to assist you run a successful campaign.','https://alphaefficiency.com/how-to-run-a-google-ads-campaign',1,'In the year 2000, when the tech crunch was in full effect, Google launched the beta version of Ads (formerly known as AdWords) with just 350 advertisers. Twenty years later, Google had earned more than $52 billion in net annual ad revenue representing nearly 80% of all search ad revenue in the United States and &hellip; Continued','<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">In the year 2000, when the tech crunch was in full effect, Google launched the beta version of Ads (formerly known as AdWords) with just 350 advertisers. Twenty years later, Google had earned more than $52 billion in net annual ad revenue representing nearly 80% of all search ad revenue in the United States and 30% of global ad revenue. PPC experts at our <a href="/ppc-agency-chicago">PPC agency Chicago</a> attribute this success to the fact that Google Ads is one of the most cost-effective advertising methods for all companies, no matter their sizes. </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">Launching a new Google Ads campaign is an exhilarating process, so if you are just starting your journey, we are here to assist you run a successful campaign that will generate sales and profit.</span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/googleadscampaign.png" alt="" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h2>Consider micro-campaigns</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Most small to medium businesses with small budgets that can&#8217;t compete with big corporations can reap major benefits from micro-campaigns. The <a href="/how-to-generate-500-ctr-increase-on-google-ads-micro-campaigns">micro campaign</a> is a campaign that is deliberately focused on creating ad copies for small geographic areas as well as a very narrow keyword subset. The idea is to use up to 2 keywords per campaign bundled with a single zip code location or a smaller town. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you are targeting a zip code, it is a good idea to have a landing page designed specifically for that zip code and include the name of that location in Google Ads. This is a good reminder for your visitors that they have come to the right place. Our recommendation is to start small and play around with lower-end budgets until you start getting consistent results with your landing pages.</span></p>
<h2>Utilize SKAGs</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Single keyword ad groups (SKAGs) are a superior strategy in structuring your Google Ads campaign. It helps you achieve higher performance by giving you intense control over your keywords, campaign settings, ads, and bids. <a href="/single-keyword-ad-groups-skags">SKAG</a> is the ad group that contains one keyword to match the searchers&#8217; intent as closely as possible.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">With SKAGs, you can elevate your click-through rates and quality scores faster while earning more money in the process. SKAG provides data integrity helping you analyze your campaigns effectively. It makes it easier to track the whereabouts of your keywords and improves your metrics over time. You will be able to <a href="/improve-low-google-ads-keyword-quality-score">improve your Quality Score</a> and the CTR, which will boost your ranking position with <a href="https://ads.google.com/home/">Google Ads</a>.</span></p>
<h2>Improve your Quality Score</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">To really get the best out of your PPC campaign, your ads need to rank as high as possible in Google&#8217;s search engine. Quality Score has a noteworthy influence on the cost and effectiveness of your paid search campaigns. This is Google&#8217;s rating of the quality and relevance of your keywords and PPC ads. Google uses this rating to estimate your CPC and then multiplies the result by your maximum bid, determining how high your ad ranks in the auction process. Some of the factors that determine your Quality Score are:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Your click-through rate</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The relevance of each keyword to its ad group</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Landing page relevance and quality</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The relevance of your ad text</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Your historical Google Ads performance</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Improving your Quality Score reduces your cost per click, which lowers your cost per conversion, which ultimately means earning more money. Take a look at the following ways to improve your Quality Score:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Keyword research &#8211; Discover and add new, highly relevant keywords, including long-tail keywords.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Keyword organization &#8211; Split keywords into organized groups to tie them to individual ad campaigns</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Refine ad text &#8211; Make your ad copy more precisely targeted to your ad groups.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Optimize landing pages &#8211; They need to connect directly with your ad groups and provide a cohesive experience.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Add <a href="/negative-keyword-list-101">negative keywords</a> &#8211; Identify and exclude irrelevant search terms that drain your budget.</span></li>
</ul>
<h2>Beware of click frauds</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">While e-commerce marketers spend more and more on online advertising, they are facing unprecedented growth in click fraud. As much as one in ten clicks across all e-commerce campaigns today is fraudulent, and click fraud is set to cost nearly $4 billion for online retailers by the end of 2022.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Cyber-attacks are now even more sophisticated, so it is becoming harder to detect them. Fraudsters are incentivized with advanced tactics, and they realize that it&#8217;s improbable for outsiders to notice their activity. At the same time, they are encouraged to proceed by the fact that any form of prosecution has been shown to be impossible. Up until now, <a href="/google-ads-click-fraud-draining-your-advertising-budget-more-than-ever">click fraud solutions</a> have primarily focused on Google detecting basic invalid clicks through the use of IP blacklists. Today, many cybersecurity companies are making an effort to block invalid clicks across platforms using several different parameters and real-time machine learning.</span></p>
<h2>Final thoughts</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Given its reach and authority, Google Ads should be a part of every paid advertising strategy. Using the tips that we covered will help you run a guided and successful campaign. And remember that there are no Google Ads campaigns that don&#8217;t work; there are only those that need a bit more work.</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/googleadscampaign.png',NULL,'[]','[318,345]','2022-02-09T07:54:21','2022-02-09T07:54:21',826,6,1),
  (16978,'/web-development-certifications','web-development-certifications','post','blog','Web Development Certifications That Will Boost Your Reputation','Web Development Certifications That Will Boost - Alpha Efficiency.™','Developers earn web development certifications upon attending courses that teach basic or more in-depth coding and development methods.','https://alphaefficiency.com/web-development-certifications',1,'Web developers are in high demand, and opting for a career in this line of work can bring many job opportunities as well as a competitive salary. Whether you are starting to pursue a career in web development or just looking to expand your knowledge, there are plenty of certification options at your disposal at &hellip; Continued','<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Web developers are in high demand, and opting for a career in this line of work can bring many job opportunities as well as a competitive salary. Whether you are starting to pursue a career in web development or just looking to expand your knowledge, there are plenty of certification options at your disposal at each level.</span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/webdevcertifications.png" alt="web development certifications" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h5>Table of Contents</h5>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#beginner">Beginner-level web development certifications</a></li>
<li><a href="/#intermediate">Intermediate-level web development certifications</a></li>
<li><a href="/#advanced">Advanced-level web development certifications</a></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The entire web user interface is based on three programming languages. Learning HTML is usually the first stepping stone for enthusiasts aiming towards becoming web developers. Along with HTML, there are two more languages crucial for creating interactive pages. These are JavaScript and CSS.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For today’s article, our </span><a href="/"><span style="font-weight: 400;">web development agency Chicago</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> researched various web development certifications to help you find those that align with your education needs and can set you apart as a credible developer.</span></p>
<h2>What are web development certifications, and why are they important?</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Developers earn web development certifications upon attending certified courses that teach foundational or more in-depth coding and web development methods. Courses usually cover a variety of topics, some of which include:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">HTML coding</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">JavaScript coding</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">CSS coding</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Front-end development</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Back-end development</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Web design</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Earning web development certifications can bring multiple benefits to your future business efforts. Let’s explore some of them:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Through web development certifications, you’ll gain in-depth knowledge without having to go back for another degree. They also limit costs, and some of them even allow you to earn them while going at your own pace.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Web development certifications help you enhance your skills while ensuring you are up to date with the current development practices.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Including web development certifications in your resume will help you showcase your qualifications to potential employers as well as demonstrate that you thrive on self-improvement.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Besides gaining advanced knowledge in specialty areas, completing web development certifications also helps you gain leadership skills. This sets your career for growth as you qualify for management or advanced development roles.</span></li>
</ul>
<h2>How to choose a web development certification program</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Due to the sheer number of excellent web development certifications out there, some of which we will cover shortly, it is extremely important to make sure that the one you choose is indeed the one that best suits your goals. If you wish to nail your choice, we suggest you consider a few factors first:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Your current experience level: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">This should largely influence your choice. If you have no previous experience and are just starting to scratch the surface of web development, your best chance is to look for beginner certification programs. These will help you set a strong foundation and earn knowledge that you can build upon as you continue to advance your career. On the other hand, professionals in mid-level or senior positions should opt for intermediate or advanced web development certifications to expand their knowledge.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Your development strengths and weaknesses:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Knowing what you do well and where you perhaps lack some knowledge can help guide your decision-making process. Make sure to first focus your attention and energy on overcoming your weaknesses before deciding to boost your strengths.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Look at your schedule: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Not all certification programs allow you to go at your own pace, so this is definitely something you need to consider carefully. Think about the amount of time you can devote to completing a program during a week. If you have a busy schedule, pick a part-time course that you can attend on weekends.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Online or in-person programs:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Many certification providers offer both online and in-person programs. The type you choose depends mainly on your preference. We said </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">mainly</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> because if you prefer face-to-face interaction, you should do research and see if there are any courses of this type available around your area. On the other hand, if you are looking for a more independent learning experience, an online course may do the trick.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Research industry changes:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> If you are looking to advance your career in web development, research changes to industry practices. Perhaps there are some updates to programming languages that you were unaware of. This way, you’ll know if there is anything new you should learn.</span></li>
</ul>
<h2>The best web development certification programs</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Now that you’ve done some self-evaluation regarding your web development skills and gone through your schedule let’s explore which courses are worth your while. We’ll start with beginner-level web development certifications and make our way to intermediate and advanced ones. The stage is set; let’s roll.</span></p>
<h2 id="beginner">Beginner-level web development certifications</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you are at the very beginning of your journey to becoming a web developer, we recommend you consider the following courses to get yourself on the right track from the get-go:</span></p>
<h3>Web Design and Development (eCornell)</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This certification program offered by <a href="http://ecornell.com">eCornell</a> is designed for persons with little-to-no experience in web development. The program is six courses long, and each course includes two weeks of instructions, so it will take you </span><b>three months </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">to complete it with </span><b>7 to 10 hours per week</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">. During this time, you’ll learn the fundamentals of front-end development and web design. This includes:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Framing front-end development</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Structuring content with HTML</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Styling web content with CSS</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Composition and ways to </span><a href="/how-to-make-your-website-mobile-friendly"><span style="font-weight: 400;">make your website mobile responsive</span></a></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Improving UX with interactivity</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Collecting user data with forms</span></li>
</ul>
<h3>Professional Certificate in Coding: Full Stack Development With MERN (MIT)</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This program is tailored to teach entry-level web developers everything they need to know about full-stack development. It consists of three modules providing you with the knowledge on foundational components of web development before moving on to front-end and back-end development. The modules are as follows:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Web development</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Front-end development with a focus on React JavaScript coding</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Back-end development with a focus on MERN stack</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The MIT program should take no more than </span><b>15 to 20 hours of your time per week,</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> and you’ll be able to complete it in </span><b>32 weeks</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></p>
<h3>Professional Certificate in Front-End Developer (edX)</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="https://www.edx.org/professional-certificate/w3cx-front-end-web-developer">This certificate</a> provides fundamental instruction to future front-end web developers. It contains five courses during which you’ll learn about:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The basics of CSS</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">HTML5 and CSS fundamentals</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Using HTML5 for apps and games</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Foundations of JavaScript</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">By the end of the program, you should be able to code websites and interactive apps as well as other components important for the end-user. The program itself is </span><b>self-paced</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">, so it is entirely up to you how fast you will complete it. However, if you dedicate as few as 5 to 7 hours each week, you’ll finish it in less than seven months.</span></p>
<h3>CareerFoundry Full-Stack Web Development Certification Program</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="https://careerfoundry.com/en/courses/become-a-web-developer/">This certification program</a> is a perfect fit for individuals looking to start a career in web development but who have no previous experience in this field. It takes a very hands-on approach to learning since you are assigned a personal expert mentor as well as a tutor right from the start. If you prefer studying </span><b>at your own pace</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">, this flexible yet structured program is definitely something to look into.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The content of the course can be accessed through their </span><b>online </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">learning platform, and you’ll be able to complete the program in </span><b>three and a half months</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> dedicating 30 hours each week or in seven months at a 15 hours per week pace. Though you choose your own pace, there are still some deadlines to stick to in order to stay on track.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Another amazing feature of this program is that graduates are offered a job guarantee, making it a pretty secure investment. You’ll also spend time talking to a career advisor who will help you apply for jobs as well as get ready for interviews. A complete package indeed.</span></p>
<h3>HTML &amp; CSS Certification Course for Beginners (Udemy)</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="https://www.udemy.com/course/html-css-javascript-certification-course-for-beginners/">Udemy</a> provides a </span><b>self-paced</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> web development certification course composed of four hours of lectures that you can access in your own free time. Their tutors will start by teaching you the fundamentals of HTML and CSS coding and gradually go more in-depth on developing various components and customizing sites with the help of these two languages.</span></p>
<h3>Programming Foundations With JavaScript, HTML, and CSS (Duke University Online)</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Duke University partnered with Coursera Inc, a massive open online course provider, to offer a certification course to persons with no previous coding experience. <a href="https://www.coursera.org/learn/duke-programming-web">Coursera’s video lectures</a> are on-demand, which means this web development certification is entirely </span><b>self-paced</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">. All of the necessary material is at your disposal right from the start so you can take your time to complete the program. Their lectures start with familiarizing you with common programming terminology before teaching you about specific programming languages. The course will help you learn how to code basic websites using JavaScript, HTML, and CSS. Depending on the time invested, you should be able to earn this certificate within 33 hours.</span></p>
<h3>Ironhack Web Development Bootcamp</h3>
<p><a href="https://www.ironhack.com/en/web-development"><span style="font-weight: 400;">This </span><b>online</b></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> web development certification program is ideal for individuals that prefer a structured approach to learning new skills. You will be studying at certain times Monday through Friday with an option to participate full-time and complete it in</span><b> 9 weeks</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">, or you can complete it in 24 weeks if you opt for part-time learning.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The program is broken down into four modules:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The pre-work module (HTML, CSS, and JavaScript fundamentals)</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Responsive design</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Back-end programming</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Front-end technologies</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The sessions start at 9 am and last until 6 am. During this time, you will have four sessions led by an instructor (45 minutes each) and three independent study sessions.</span></p>
<h2 id="intermediate">Intermediate-level web development certifications</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Moving on, let’s check some of the certifications intended for individuals that already possess knowledge of the fundamentals of web development. These are, in our opinion, some of the best intermediate-level web development certifications.</span></p>
<h3>The Springboard Software Engineering Certification (Springboard)</h3>
<p><a href="https://www.springboard.com/courses/software-engineering-career-track/"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Springboard’s </span></a><b>online </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">web development certification program is perfect for entry-level web developers looking to create more advanced sites and apps by upgrading their JavaScript, CSS, and HTML knowledge. Over the course of </span><b>9 months </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">(20 hours per week), you’ll find out why companies like ours </span><a href="/why-use-node-js"><span style="font-weight: 400;">use Node.js</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> as well as cover other important topics and programming languages. Here is what the program includes:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Front-end development</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Back-end development with Python</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Flask and SQL</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Node and Express</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">ReactJS and Redux</span></li>
</ul>
<h3>Springboard Software Engineering Career Track</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="https://bootcamprankings.com/springboard-software-engineering-career-track/">This program</a> is designed for individuals with a problem-solving attitude and strong communication and collaboration traits who possess fundamental JavaScript, HTML, and CSS skills. The course takes place </span><b>online </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">and offers a job guarantee once you complete it. If you already have a background in web development and are seeking an opportunity to completely switch to a career in this line of work, definitely look into this one.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Springboard program takes approximately </span><b>9 months</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> to complete and requires 20 hours of study each week. Upon enrollment, you will be dedicated to a mentor who will work with you via weekly video calls. You’ll have over 800 hours of content at your disposal, along with an active online student community, unlimited consultations with a career coach, resume and portfolio reviews, as well as mock interviews. Once you graduate from the program, you will receive a certificate of completion.</span></p>
<h3>GIAC Certified Web Application Defender (GWEB) (GIAC Certifications)</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="https://www.giac.org/certifications/">GIAC</a> offers a </span><b>self-paced</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> web developer certification program that allows individuals with app development backgrounds to exhibit their know-how in cybersecurity. The training course called </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Defending Web Application Security Essentials</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> is provided through a partnership with the SANS institute and includes some of the major topics about access control, proactive defense measures, security testing, and web architecture. The lectures are held </span><b>online</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">. However, to pass the exam and receive certification, you will have to undergo an </span><b>in-person examination</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></p>
<h3>Technology Leadership Certificate (eCornell)</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">As the program’s name says, <a href="https://ecornell.cornell.edu/certificates/technology/technology-leadership/">this certificate</a> helps mid, or senior-level IT professionals acquire leadership skills. This is essential for persons who wish to qualify for promotional opportunities and team leader positions. The course takes place </span><b>online </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">and lasts for </span><b>three months </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">with 3 to 5 hours per week. It includes:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Strengths-based technology leadership</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Decision-making skills for technology leaders</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Collaborative communication for technology leaders</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Courageous communication for technology leaders</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Influence and motivation for technology leaders</span></li>
</ul>
<h3>BrainStation Online Web Development Diploma</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="https://brainstation.io/course/online/intro-to-web-development">This is yet another great</a> option for those looking to launch a new career in web development and possess some basic knowledge of HTML and CSS. Unlike other certification programs on our list, all applicants are required to attend the Prep Course here before acceptance.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Once you get accepted to this intensive, project-based, </span><b>online </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">web developer certification program, you’ll begin your </span><b>12-week long</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> journey dedicating 40 hours each week to a combination of live online lectures and hands-on projects. During this time, you will be taught how to create a complete software solution for the modern web with a strong focus on the JavaScript programming language. You’ll also receive constant feedback from field experts, ensuring that you don’t stray away from the path.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">BrainStation Online Web Development Diploma program also puts a strong focus on building your portfolio and preparing you for this line of work with extensive career coaching and interview preparation included in the curriculum.</span></p>
<h2 id="advanced">Advanced-level web development certifications</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Next, we’ll explore some of the best certification programs for seasoned web developers and IT professionals. Let’s dive in.</span></p>
<h3>Adobe Certified Expert (ACE) (Adobe Digital Learning Services)</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The first program on our advanced-level certification list is divided into tracts, each containing an individual course where you’ll master all the ins and outs of how JavaScript, front-end development, and cloud computing interact with Magento 2. The tracts include:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Adobe Certified Expert Magento Commerce JavaScript Developer</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Adobe Certified Expert Magento Commerce Front-End Developer</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Adobe Certified Expert Magento Commerce Cloud Developer</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The <a href="https://learning.adobe.com/certification.html">ACE certification course</a> is held </span><b>online </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">and can be completed within </span><b>2 to 3 days</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></p>
<h3>Oracle Certified Expert: Java Platform, Enterprise Edition 6 Front-End Developer (Oracle University)</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Oracle University’s program offers web development professionals a chance to learn how to use Java’s enterprise edition 6 software to code front-end development components. This </span><b>self-paced online</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> program contains one course followed by an examination.</span></p>
<h3>Oracle Certified Expert: Java Platform, Enterprise Edition 6 Back-End Developer (Oracle University)</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Just like the previous program on our list, this one is also part of Java enterprise edition courses provided by Oracle University. During three </span><b>self-paced online</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> courses, you will master back-end development components coding in accordance with Java’s enterprise edition 6 software.</span></p>
<h2>Final thoughts</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">We have come to the end of today&#8217;s article in which we presented what we feel are the most incredible web development certification programs available on the market. Whether you are the industry’s rookie or a seasoned veteran, including one or more of the aforementioned certifications in your portfolio will give you the best chance to secure a dream job or finally land that project you desire.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you still have some uncertainties on whether to pursue a web developer certification or even commit yourself to this line of work overall, we suggest you explore the field further before making a decision. Read through reviews, carefully study program curriculums, or check our article on must-have </span><a href="/must-have-marketing-certifications"><span style="font-weight: 400;">digital marketing certifications</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. Either way, we got you covered.</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/webdevcertifications.png',NULL,'[]','[354]','2022-02-11T08:43:47','2022-02-11T08:43:47',2517,4,1);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (wp_id,path,slug,type,track,title,meta_title,meta_description,canonical,robots_index,excerpt,body_html,hero_image,wp_template,tags,categories,published_at,updated_at,word_count,internal_links,image_count) VALUES
  (16986,'/google-ads-account-structure','google-ads-account-structure','post','blog','The Ultimate Guide to Google Ads Account Structure','The Ultimate Guide to Google Ads Account Structure - Alpha Efficiency.™','Interested in PPC? In this ultimate guide you will find everything you need to know about the Google Ads account structure.','https://alphaefficiency.com/google-ads-account-structure',1,'Hello, guys. In the past couple of months, we have been getting a lot of questions about the best way to structure a Google Ads account. This is why our Chicago PPC agency decided to dedicate today’s post to that question and compose this ultimate guide in which you will find everything you need to &hellip; Continued','<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Hello, guys. In the past couple of months, we have been getting a lot of questions about the best way to structure a Google Ads account. This is why our <a href="/ppc-agency-chicago">Chicago PPC agency</a> decided to dedicate today’s post to that question and compose this ultimate guide in which you will find everything you need to know about the Google Ads account structure.</span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/googleadsaccountstructure.png" alt="google ads account structure" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">We will approach the account structure from 5 levels and explain each so that by the end of this guide, you will have an account that will serve as a strong foundation for all of your current and future campaigns:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><a href="/#campaign"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The campaign level</span></a></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><a href="/#adgroup"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The ad group level</span></a></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><a href="/#keyword"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Keyword selection</span></a></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><a href="/#adcopy"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ad copy</span></a></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><a href="/#adextensions"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ad extensions</span></a></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="campaign">The campaign level</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">To lay a solid foundation for the rest of your account, you need to start by choosing the campaign type. The best way to do that is to ask yourself the question: What</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> is my advertising goal? </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The answer to that question will tell you which campaign type supports your efforts the best. Let’s see how:</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Answer:</strong> To find customers looking for my product (service).</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Campaign type: Search network.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Answer:</strong> To generate phone calls for my business.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Campaign type: Call.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Answer:</strong> To build brand awareness.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Campaign type: Display network.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Answer:</strong> To re-engage previous site visitors.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Campaign type: Remarketing.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Businesses usually start with search campaigns, but it is not necessarily the best choice for every type of business. Sometimes the best option is to create multiple campaign types to satisfy the different goals you have.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Depending on the way your business is structured, you may want to consider the following campaign settings:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Location targeting</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Language targeting</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Bid strategy (automatic or manual)</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Budget</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For Google not to overspend your advertising money, you need to determine your daily budget. The calculation itself is easy, you just divide your monthly budget by 30.4, but it is extremely important to know how many clicks a day your budget can support (based on your estimated cost per click).</span></p>
<h2 id="adgroup">The ad group level</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The next level of your Google Ads account structure consists of your ad groups. They are organized by theme, create the structure within each campaign, and control keyword-to-ad association.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you have any dilemmas about the size of an ad group, these are the guidelines to follow:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">no more than 7 to 10 ad groups per campaign.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">20 (approximately) keywords per ad group.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">2 or 3 ads per ad group.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">As every campaign is different, you don’t need to follow these guidelines strictly. These are only our suggestions of optimal numbers, so your ad groups don’t get bloated and become difficult to manage.</span></p>
<h2 id="keyword">Keyword selection</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The next step is defining your keywords. Keep in mind that no matter how savvy you are, this is not where you should rely on your instincts. The best practice is to use keyword tools like <a href="https://ads.google.com/home/tools/keyword-planner/">Google Ads Keyword Planner</a> to do your research to ensure that you are bidding on keywords with enough search volume.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">When it comes to <a href="/7-essential-steps-to-profitable-keyword-research-service-that-drive-results">profitable keyword research</a>, the most important thing to keep in mind is to choose keywords that have clear commercial intent. This means that people who search using those terms are looking to buy something. Keywords with intent often include:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Qualifying terms such as specific product details, brand names, the word </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">cost</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">, etc.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Location terms</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">It is essential to narrow down your audience as much as possible since very broad terms don’t show much intent, have low click-through and conversion rates, and have high CPAs.</span></p>
<h3>Keyword match types</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="/google-ads-match-types">Keyword match types</a> define how the keywords in your campaigns match up with the queries people search on search engines. Google provides four match types to choose from:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Broad match </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; This is the least restrictive match type. Your ad will match any generally related search terms, including synonyms.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Modified broad match </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; This is a little more restrictive match type since your ad will only match if the search term includes words that you specify with a plus sign, although they can show in any order.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Phrase match </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; The keyword must include the terms you are bidding on uninterrupted, and in the order you specify. However, it may include other terms before or after.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Exact match </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; Exact and precise are synonyms, but not according to Google. Therefore, this match type deserves more attention than the previous three. Let me explain.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">There has been quite a while since Google introduced changes to how exact match keywords work. The consequences of these changes are that your ad may show when the terms in your keyword are reordered, or the function words change. This has shown to be better for low-volume terms and niche-oriented industries, but not so much for branded campaigns.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">There is no simple answer to define the best match type. Choosing the keyword match type that would be the best fit for your campaign depends primarily on your account goals.</span></p>
<h3>Max CPC bids</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The next thing you need to do is set max CPC bids. This is your way of telling Google how much you are willing to pay for a click. Google will then determine your Ad Rank by multiplying your max CPC with your <a href="/google-ads-quality-score">Quality Score</a>, determining your ad position and cost per click. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">When it comes to new campaigns, there are a couple of ways to determine your max CPC bids:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Automatic bidding </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; We at Alpha Efficiency lean toward Manual bidding over Automatic; since we prefer to have full control over our bids rather than leaving it up to Google. However, starting a new campaign is one of the few good uses of Automatic bidding. You can let Google determine your max CPC until you get enough data to figure out the cost of a click. Once you get the feeling you can manage on your own, you can switch back to Manual bidding. When using Automatic bidding, make sure to:</span>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Use the Maximize Clicks strategy so Google would try to get as many clicks as possible out of your daily budget.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Set an overall limit that you don’t want Google to exceed (max CPC bid limit).</span></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Manual CPC </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8211; For full control, use the Manual CPC bidding strategy. There are a couple of metrics that can help determine your max CPC:</span>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Page #1 CPC</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Top of page CPC</span></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">These metrics are estimates that Google provides for each keyword so you can have an idea of how much it will cost you to rank on the first page of search results and at the top of that page.</span></p>
<h2 id="adcopy">Ad Copy</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Your Ad Copy is the part of your account that other people interact with. It is how you reach out to your potential clients, and it needs to reflect your brand or business. A few years ago, Google made Expanded Text ad their default ad type, maximizing your presence and performance with a bigger headline and an extra-long description.</span></p>
<h3>A/B testing</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Running tests on your ads is critical for finding the copy that resonates the most with your audience. Ideally, it should drive as many clicks and conversions as possible for lower costs. Here are some of the tests that we usually run:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Keywords vs creativity &#8211; The idea is to run two tests. The first version of your ad should be keyword-centric, while the other should be more creative and attention-grabbing. Look at the data you collect to determine which version is better for you.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Price vs no price &#8211; While specific numbers often drive clicks, they may also help you qualify your audience.</span></li>
</ul>
<h3>How to write ad copy with conversions in mind</h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you are looking to set the table for conversions with your ad copy, here are a couple of things to keep in mind:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Use self-selecting ad copy &#8211; Including pricing info in your ad copy will help you reach the exact audience you target and avoid paying for clicks from people that have no intent to buy your product.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Match your CTA to your landing page &#8211; The same call to action needs to appear both in your ad and on your landing page. This way, you are making sure that your visitors are in the right mindset to convert.</span></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="adextensions">Ad extensions</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ad extensions are a great way to make your ads more enticing since they bring high CTR’s at no added costs. While there are tons of ad extensions for you to choose from, with new ones appearing constantly, not all of them will prove useful for your account. Here are some of our top choices:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Sitelinks</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Callout extensions</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Call extensions</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Location extensions</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="/google-ads-sitelinks"><strong>Sitelinks</strong> </a>are clickable links to other pages on your website. They are pretty useful as they offer more options to your visitors than just one landing page. However, if you are using landing pages designed only to capture links, it is smarter to avoid sitelinks.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Callouts</strong> are additional, non-clickable snippets of text that form an extra line of copy.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Call extensions</strong> are designed with mobile users in mind providing them with the option to call you directly from SERP, skipping the landing page.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>Location extensions</strong> are great for local businesses because they offer your physical business information.</span></p>
<h2>Final thoughts</h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">As you can see, structuring a Google Ads account is no rocket science. But it does involve some contemplation about the goals you wish to achieve with your campaigns. Whether you are starting from scratch or want to overhaul an existing account, this is what you need to keep in mind:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Give your campaign structure and settings based on your goals.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ad groups work for you, controlling keyword and ad associations.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Make your keywords work for you. We prefer to use a phrase match in our campaigns since it gives us the necessary precision when it comes to keyword match types. However, if you are just starting, we suggest a modified broad match with 2 or 3 terms in each keyword that show clear intent.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Write an ad copy with conversions in mind.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Use ad extensions.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Always test everything.</span></li>
</ul>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/googleadsaccountstructure.png',NULL,'[]','[318,345]','2022-02-25T09:04:14','2022-02-25T09:04:14',1673,5,1),
  (17002,'/how-to-create-a-saas-website','how-to-create-a-saas-website','post','blog','The Importance Of a Great SaaS Website: How to Create Yours','The Importance Of a Great SaaS Website - Alpha Efficiency.™','How to create a SaaS website that fulfills your expectations? Today, we present you with a site map that will skyrocket your conversions.','https://alphaefficiency.com/how-to-create-a-saas-website',1,'Not so long ago, buying a piece of software meant you only had two options. Pay a visit to your local electronics store and see if you can find it in the vastness of CDs displayed. If it’s not there, go to the next one. And then the next one. If you end up empty-handed, &hellip; Continued','<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Not so long ago, buying a piece of software meant you only had two options. Pay a visit to your local electronics store and see if you can find it in the vastness of CDs displayed. If it’s not there, go to the next one. And then the next one. If you end up empty-handed, well, at least you had a nice walk. You are left with only one option: Order the CD online and wait until it gets delivered. </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">Maybe modern technology has spoiled us a bit. Maybe we became so accustomed to accessing all we set our minds to in a blink of an eye (the amount of time it takes us to click a button) that those past times seem like an endeavor. However, those days are behind us. Today, the Software as a Service delivery model dominates the industry. And luckily so, right?  </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">In today’s article, our </span><a href="/code"><span style="font-weight: 400;">web development agency Chicago</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> sheds some light on SaaS web applications and platforms and explores how to create a well-structured and high-converting SaaS website. Let’s go.</span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/saaswebsite.png" alt="how to create a great saas website" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h5>Table of Contents</h5>
