<h2 id="importance"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">How important is Web Design in 2024?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A website is a digital storefront that allows customers to learn more about your products or services 24/7. Today, customers expect businesses to have an online presence, and those that don&#8217;t are at a significant disadvantage. Investing time and effort into designing a high-quality website or hiring professional web design services usually proves beneficial, as it leads to increased sales and visibility in search engines. On the other hand, a poor web design can make potential customers click away before they even have a chance to see what you have to offer.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">In 2024, following </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/latest-ui-ux-design-trends" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">web design trends</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> will be more critical than ever for small businesses and large corporations. In fact, many companies are finding that their website is the most important part of their marketing strategy. It is a powerful way to reach new customers and improve the quality of relationships with them. You can also use it to keep existing customers informed about your products and services and ensure they remain loyal to your brand. What many business owners need to realize, however, is that the landscape of web design is constantly changing. What worked last year may not work this year, and what works this year may be outdated by next year. And as simply using the latest web design software for your projects is not enough, what can you do to ensure that your web design project will be successful? Let&#8217;s find out what our web design experts think&#8230;</span></p>
<h2 id="dos-and-don''ts"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Basic Dos and Don&#8217;ts of Effective Website Design</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">To build a successful website, you have to understand how different design decisions impact the user experience, the website&#8217;s performance in search engines, and similar. This delicate decision-making process starts just after you gather a web design team. You&#8217;ll immediately have to create an ideal buyer&#8217;s persona, choose between different e-Commerce platforms, put up a web design style guide everyone can follow, find a unique domain name, and much more. A deep insight into the different website dos and don&#8217;ts can help you avoid common mistakes that diminish the quality of results but also help you highlight web design elements that your website visitors are likely to find most important.</span></p>
<h3 id="navigation"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Website Dos and Don&#8217;ts for Navigation</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Navigation is one of the most important aspects of user experience web design, so it should be given careful thought and attention. Creating an effective navigation system for your website visitors is essential if you want them to stay on your site, find what they&#8217;re looking for, and come back again. Let&#8217;s take a look at some of the most important web design recommendations our experts have when it comes to designing navigation.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Dos for Navigation</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Use simple words in your navigation menus</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Change the colors of links a user has already visited</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Make it possible for website visitors to get to any page within three clicks</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Ensure the proper contrast between text and navigation buttons</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Making navigation as simple and intuitive as possible is crucial for enhancing the user experience on your website and preventing high bounce rates. That&#8217;s why you must create clear navigation labels, adequately adjust contrast, ensure visitors can quickly reach desired pages, and more. Various </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/wordpress-ada-compliance-website" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">WordPress ADA compliance</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> plugins can help you increase your website design&#8217;s accessibility and make navigation smoother.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Don&#8217;ts for Navigation</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t overcrowd your primary navigation by pacing more than seven links</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Avoid horizontal scrolling purely for the sake of uniqueness</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t make scrolling unpredictable for users</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A common mistake in web design is trying to fit too many links and options into the navigation bar. That not only looks bad, but it can also be confusing and off-putting for users. Instead, keep your navigation clean and simple so users can easily find what they&#8217;re looking for. It is also essential to give website visitors full control over scrolling, so avoid something commonly known as &#8220;scroll hijacking.&#8221;</span></p>
<h3 id="layout"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Website Dos and Don&#8217;ts for designing better Website Layout</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The website layout is a crucial aspect of web design for several reasons. Well-designed website layout creates a visual hierarchy that guides your visitors&#8217; eyes to the most important information on the page. It can also help you improve user experience by making it easy for visitors to find what they&#8217;re looking for. And it can also increase conversion rates on your website by making it more visually appealing. On the other hand, a poorly designed website layout can frustrate your visitors and cause lost business opportunities. So which website dos and don&#8217;ts should you give close attention to when designing a layout?</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Dos for better Website Layout</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Follow specific standards within the web design industry</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Use design elements familiar to your website visitors</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Keep it user-friendly</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Use a grid layout to build a visual hierarchy and convey information more easily</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Highlight the most important design elements</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Create a web design style guide before you start working on a web design project</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Keep natural scanning patterns in mind</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You need to make sure that your website visitors will fully understand the meaning of each web design element and won&#8217;t get confused upon landing on one of your pages. Avoid positioning common elements in screen spots where people aren&#8217;t used to seeing them for the sake of being unique. The website layout should be designed in a user-friendly fashion, so focus on your target audience&#8217;s needs and wants. Make it easy for people to notice CTAs, navigational elements, and similar.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Don&#8217;ts for Website Layout</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Avoid creating a too complex website layout</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Avoid walls of text on your pages</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t emphasize creativity</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t use a completely new website layout</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Simplicity is the goal you should strive for when designing a website layout. Even the most popular brands follow specific standards people get used to, so we strongly advise against too much experimentation in this field. Of course, you shouldn&#8217;t completely copy others either &#8211; finding the right balance between creativity and familiarity is the key to powerful website layout design.</span></p>
<h3 id="white-space"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Website Dos and Don&#8217;ts when using White Space</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you&#8217;ve ever looked at a website and thought it looked cluttered, you were probably right. One of the most important aspects of web design is white space. White space is the area of a website that is left blank, without any text or images. It may seem like a wasted opportunity, but white space is actually essential to good user experience web design. However, you need to be careful when using white space, as finding the right balance is essential here. Here are our web design recommendations for using white space:</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Dos for White Space</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Use the white space between different sections on the same page</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Make design elements distinctive by using white space</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Ensure there is enough white space around your CTAs</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Using white space can help you highlight the most critical elements on your page while achieving an elegant look. It is also a powerful way to naturally guide your website visitors&#8217; eyes through the page and improve the readability of your content by grouping related design elements together. Also, keep in mind that users are more likely to notice an object if there is a lot of white space around it. That&#8217;s why many famous brands use white space in their web design to increase conversion rates and make their products irresistible to observers.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Don&#8217;ts for White Space</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t confuse micro and macro white space </span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Avoid making your pages look too empty </span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t forget to adjust the white space for mobile device</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While using white space can help you improve the visual aspect of your website, it is vital to use it with taste to avoid creating pages that look too empty. And as achieving a fantastic look and feel of your website on mobile devices is equally important, before the launch date, make sure to check how white space is impacting your layout on smaller screens.</span></p>
<h3 id="typography"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Website Dos and Don&#8217;ts for Typography</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Typography is the art and technique of arranging type to make written language legible, readable, and visually appealing when displayed. It&#8217;s an integral part of web design, and it can significantly impact the overall look and feel of your site. Investing time into learning </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/typography-in-ux-design" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">typography for UX</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> will prove beneficial once you start working on the web design project for your business. But to help you get started, we&#8217;ve created a list of dos and don&#8217;ts you can use as a reminder when choosing typography for your website.</span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/websitedosanddonts2.png" alt="" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Dos for Typography</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Set a larger font size for headlines</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Make sure you&#8217;re using adequate letter spacing and line-heights </span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Set the limit for characters per line between 40 and 80</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">As each element of your website should have enough breathing room to be easily identifiable and clickable, the same goes for letter spacing in your content. Adequate letter spacing ensures that readers can quickly identify each word and follow along with your argument. A good rule of thumb is to use 1.5 times the point size of your font for letter spacing. Also, your headlines should be large enough to be easily visible but not so large that they obscure the rest of the page. When adjusting line lengths, keep in mind that if there are too many characters in each line, it could become difficult for visitors&#8217; eyes to track from the end of one line to the beginning of the next. That&#8217;s why you should limit characters per line to 80.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Dont&#8217;s for Typography</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t use more than three typefaces and font sizes </span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t use fonts that don&#8217;t fit your brand style</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Avoid fonts that are hard to read</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Avoid all-caps text</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Too many fonts can lead to a difficult reading experience for users and ultimately cause them to leave your site. Using three fonts is the optimal number for most websites and should be maintained unless there are specific reasons to use more. However, you must always ensure that each font fits your brand style before using it. And as all-caps texts can be challenging to read, we recommend avoiding them. All in all, typography shouldn&#8217;t be overlooked when designing a website, as it can either make or break the overall look and feel of your web design.</span></p>
<h3 id="speed"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Website Dos and Don&#8217;ts for Speed Optimization</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Having slow-loading pages can ruin the user experience for your website visitors and lead to increased bounce rates. But your problems won&#8217;t end with fewer conversions and a loss of credibility &#8211; website speed can also affect your search engine ranking. To secure a fantastic experience for your potential customers, you need to become aware of the specific website dos and don&#8217;ts when it comes to speed optimization during the design process.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Dos when Optimizing Page Speed</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Minify code</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Optimize images</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Implement loading indicator</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Take advantage of browser caching</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Writing clean code is necessary if you want to build a solid foundation for high website speed. Also, you should avoid serving website visitors with blank pages during the loading process, so consider designing a loading indicator to let them know everything will be okay. </span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Dont&#8217;s when Optimizing Page Speed</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t use drag-n-drop platforms for building your website</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t install unnecessary plugins</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Avoid using unnecessary pop-ups that can slow down your pages</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Business owners make a common mistake when trying to build a successful online presence for their brand: opting for a DIY web design approach and creating templated websites. Such websites can hardly compete with websites designed by professional web design firms when it comes to speed. That&#8217;s why we advise you to avoid drag-n-drop platforms and build your website from scratch. Also, keep in mind that installing <a href="https://www.hostinger.com/tutorials/how-many-plugins-are-too-many">too many plugins can lead to slow-loading pages</a>, too &#8211; so stick to only the ones that are essential for your needs.</span></p>
<h3 id="images"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Website Dos and Don&#8217;ts when implementing Images</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Images are an essential part of website design for several reasons. They can help to add visual interest to a page, break up the text, and convey information more effectively than words alone. When used correctly, images can also help to improve the overall user experience on a website.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">However, it&#8217;s important to use images wisely. Let&#8217;s see which web design recommendations our experts have when implementing images on your website.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Dos when it comes to using Images</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Optimize image file sizes</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Resize images to enhance the visual aspect of your page</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Combine images with text</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Make sure all images on the page are of the same style</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Write image alt texts to help search engines understand their context (it will also benefit your website visitors in case your pages don&#8217;t fully load)</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Images are a powerful tool for winning website visitors&#8217; hearts, enhancing your brand image, and supporting your website marketing efforts. However, as they are one of the heaviest resource-consuming elements in web design, images can slow down your website unless you take specific actions to optimize their file sizes properly. You also need to write image alt text for each image you include on your website to help search engines understand their context. That will also prove beneficial for users if your pages don&#8217;t fully load.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Don&#8217;ts when it comes to using Images</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Avoid using images that don&#8217;t correspond with your brand values</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t use too many generic stock photos just for decorative purposes</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t use an image unless you have a license or rights for it</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t include low-quality images on your website</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Too many images can make your site look cluttered and can be overwhelming for visitors. The key is to use images that are relevant and add to the overall design of your site. And to not endanger your brand&#8217;s trustworthiness and credibility, you need to make sure each image on your website is of high quality and owned by you.</span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/websitedosanddonts3.png" alt="" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3 id="mobile"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Website Dos and Don&#8217;ts for Mobile-Friendly Design</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">In today&#8217;s digital world, it&#8217;s more important than ever to have a mobile-friendly website. More and more people are using their smartphones and tablets to access the internet, and if your website isn&#8217;t designed for these devices, you could be missing out on potential customers. Whether you opt for adaptive or responsive web design, you need to be aware of common mistakes inexperienced designers make when trying to <a href="/mobile-first-web-design-an-overlooked-profit-opportunity">build a mobile-friendly website</a>. Here are our web design recommendations you can follow:</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Dos for Mobile-friendliness</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Make essential information easy to find on smaller screens</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Change the size of interactive design elements to make it easier for users to tap on them</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Consider taking the mobile-first approach</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Optimize your layout for portrait orientation too</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Simplify menus &#8211; use the hamburger menu instead of the navigation bar</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">As mobile devices have smaller screens, it is crucial to make all the vital information easy to notice, adjust element sizes to avoid misclicks that can frustrate users, and simplify navigation. By following the tips above, you can secure a great user experience, which leads to increased conversion rates and more quality relationships with your customers.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Don&#8217;ts for Mobile-friendliness</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t forget to properly format text for enhanced readability on mobile screens</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Avoid placing long forms for users to fill</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t settle for web design that doesn&#8217;t provide an equally amazing user experience on both desktop and mobile devices </span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">When designing a mobile version of your website, it is crucial to adjust design element sizes and format content for better readability. Also, keep in mind that filling out long forms on mobile devices can be a frustrating experience. In case you must include such forms on your website, we recommend implementing an auto-suggest feature to make the process smoother for visitors.</span></p>
<h3 id="serp"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Website Dos and Don&#8217;ts for achieving Better Rankings in Search Engines</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Many business owners think of search engine optimization as an afterthought. They build a website and then think about how to get people to find it. However, SEO should be a consideration from the very beginning of the web design process. Our </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/seo-agency-chicago" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">SEO agency in Chicago</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> advises you to pay close attention to these website dos and don&#8217;ts when building a digital landscape for your business.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Dos for Search Engine Optimization</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Choose an SEO-friendly domain name</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Check if there are broken links on your website</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Optimize image file sizes to achieve better website speed</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Make your URLs SEO-friendly</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Include only high-quality content</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Aim for high website speed</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">As there are many different factors, Google takes into account when ranking websites on search engine results pages &#8211; the best course of action for you is to consult with SEO experts during the website creation process. Your website needs to be designed in a way that is both visually appealing and easy to navigate. If your website is difficult to use or doesn&#8217;t look good, people will likely click away and look for another business with a better website. </span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design Don&#8217;ts for Search Engine Optimization</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t create an unclear site structure</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t plagiarize other website&#8217;s content</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t forget about your target audience&#8217;s needs</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t forget about the website&#8217;s security</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While designing a website, it is also important to take specific actions to ensure it will be easy to crawl by search engine bots while providing an amazing user experience for your target audience. Also, you shouldn&#8217;t take the content on your website lightly &#8211; as content quality is especially important for ranking your website high on Google in 2024. By plagiarizing other people&#8217;s content, you put your whole online presence in danger, as it will almost certainly lead to SEO penalties that are hard to recover from.</span></p>
