<h2 id="figma"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">What is Figma?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Figma is a popular vector graphic editor designers use to create user interfaces, illustrations, icons, and more. High-fidelity Figma designs can be converted to code or exported as PNGs, JPGs, and SVGs. While it is similar to other design tools, such as Adobe Photoshop and Sketch, Figma has some unique features that make it a valuable tool for designers. Some of the most popular features include:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The ability to create vector graphics that can be easily scaled and exported for use in web and native app design.</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> A wide variety of built-in shapes and objects can be used to create Figma designs.</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> A layer-based design interface that makes it easy to create complex designs.</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> A design library that web developers can use to create consistent designs across the web and native apps.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Figma can be utilized as a design collaboration tool that allows multiple designers to work on the same project simultaneously. That will allow you to give immediate feedback to the members of your design team and finish the web project more efficiently. And since Figma is a free design tool, you can start using it immediately.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It is worth noting that this vector graphics editor is web-based, which means that it can be used on any operating system and various devices, as there are even ways to use </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/figma-on-ipad-pro" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Figma on iPad </span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">as an app. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Figma was created by Dylan Field and Evan Wallace in 2016, and it was recently announced that Adobe would acquire it for an astonishing $20 billion. However, its creators claim that Figma will remain free for educational purposes and that Adobe will expand this tool&#8217;s features.</span></p>
<h2 id="wodpress"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Why should you use Figma to design WordPress websites?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">WordPress is a content management system (CMS) that enables you to create a blog or a website from scratch or to improve an existing website. It is free and open-source software released under the GPL and currently stands behind the most active websites. Ease of use and flexibility make this CMS an excellent choice for both beginners and experienced users.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">However, while building a simple website is very easy when using ready-to-go WordPress themes, by sticking with basic page editors, you will probably fail to impress your potential customers. That is because Elementor and other page builders will not only prevent you from creating a web design that goes hand in hand with your brand guidelines but also from fully optimizing your website for performance in search engines. To build a unique web design, you&#8217;ll need to either hire professional digital marketing services or utilize design tools on your own.</span></p>
<p>As a powerful designing and developing tool and vector graphics editor, Figma is one of the most popular choices for those who work on complex web projects. Figma to WordPress is a great combination because this design tool&#8217;s features compensate for the limitations WordPress page editors have, especially when it comes to the user-friendly and fully functional website visual aspects of a website.</p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Do big companies use Figma?</span></h3>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/bigcompaniesfigma.png" alt="big companies using figma" width="650" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">There is no one-size-fits-all answer to this question, as each company has its own needs, </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/website-quality-assurance-checklist" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">design QA checklist</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">, and budget. Figma is very popular among freelancers and small businesses since it is free and easy to use. However, many large companies also use Figma, as it is a powerful and versatile design tool that can be used for various purposes. That includes giants such as Google, Facebook, and Netflix, and Figma has even been used to design the interface for the Tesla Model 3. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This doesn&#8217;t come as a surprise, considering Figma&#8217;s rise in popularity in recent years. Companies use this design tool to create prototypes, enhance collaboration among their team members, find bugs more quickly, and build fresh-looking user interfaces for their websites and apps.</span></p>
<h2 id="figma-to-html"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Can I convert my Figma to HTML?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">By converting Figma to HTML, you can create clean, standards-compliant code that will render correctly in all browsers and then use it to customize your WordPress theme. This process is essential because it allows designers to test their designs in a real-world environment and ensure they work as intended. If you have a Figma design that you want to convert to HTML, you can do it by using several plugins:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Figma to HTML</span><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> </span></li>
<li><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://teleporthq.io/figma-export-to-html-plugin" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">TeleportHQ</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> </span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Builder.io HTML to Figma</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Although using Figma to HTML plugins can save you time, we prefer a manual approach to converting Figma to HTML in order to avoid any potential code errors. The best practice to manually turn Figma files into HTML is utilizing a CSS framework such as Bootstrap. You can do it by following these steps:</span></p>
<ol>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Open your Figma files</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Download the starter HTML template from </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://getbootstrap.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Bootstrap</span></a></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Proceed to create a page layout by working on the header section. Then, add the footer and the other page sections. Remember to add style.css and global.css to your colors, typography, buttons, and other elements.</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">In order to make it possible to transfer the files separately in WordPress later on &#8211; separate your page sections into different HTML sections.</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Keep coding the remaining pages of your design, and make sure to use media queries to make a website responsive.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Once your HTML pages are ready, you can move on to turning Figma to WordPress. Keep reading to find out exactly how you can do it.</span></p>
<h2 id="figma-to-wordpress"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Can you turn Figma into a WordPress website?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While there is no easy way to export Figma design as a WordPress theme, it is definitely possible. However, keep in mind that exporting Figma to WordPress without making serious changes to your website&#8217;s code can be a difficult task &#8211; so we strongly advise you to back up your files beforehand. That is especially important if your website is already live. Converting Figma to WordPress is best handled by professionals, as with neither of these methods, you can be 100% sure that no errors will occur during the process. So make sure to fully understand the desired method before doing any work.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you have followed the above guide, you have your HTML files ready. Now, here are three approaches to turning them into a functional WordPress site &#8211; creating a new theme from scratch, using an existing theme, or utilizing page editors.</span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/figmatowordpress-1.png" alt="figma design being converted to wordpress" width="650" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Converting HTML to WordPress by creating a new theme</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">With this method, you&#8217;ll first need to create a new theme from scratch, and make sure to create the following files:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">header.php</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">functions.php</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">footer.php</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">style.css</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">index.php</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">page.php</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">single.php</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Since this approach gives web developers full control over the website&#8217;s look and functionality, our </span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">WordPress SEO agency</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> highly recommends it for those confident in their skills. By creating a new WordPress theme from scratch, you&#8217;ll be able to write clean code, which will prove beneficial for the user experience and your website&#8217;s SEO.</span></p>
<iframe title="How to Perform Figma To WordPress Transfer With Enterprise-Level Quality" width="500" height="281" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/MktzvZ_cyuc?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
<h3 id="themes"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Making Figma to WordPress conversion by using existing themes</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">As building a WordPress theme from scratch can be very time-consuming, if you are short on time or lack resources, you might want to use a starter theme for the purpose of converting Figma to WordPress. For this purpose, we recommend utilizing <a href="/sage-framework-wordpress">Sage Framework</a>, as this starter theme has clean code and gives you a solid SEO foundation.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This method allows you to start converting your Figma designs into WordPress websites much faster, as starter themes will already have the necessary files. After you choose your theme, you have to implement your HTML code in order to achieve the desired look and feel before you activate the WordPress site. You&#8217;ll only need to understand the basic structures of WordPress themes to successfully turn your Figma design into a functional website with this method. Here is what you need to do:</span></p>
<ol>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Export Figma design as HTML files following the steps we&#8217;ve described</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Open these HTML files</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Choose a starter WordPress theme</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Fill in the existing code structure with your HTML code</span></li>
</ol>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Converting Figma to WordPress with the help of Page Builders</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">WordPress page builders are plugins that allow you to create custom pages or posts without having to code. They typically include a drag-and-drop interface and a library of pre-built elements that you can add to your pages. WordPress page builders can be used to create any type of page, including landing pages, sales pages, and membership sites. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While using page builders might be the easiest solution, especially for those who don&#8217;t possess any coding knowledge &#8211; we advise against this approach. That is because Elementor, Wix, and other page editors usually make your website slow to load due to code redundancies and create plugin and cyber security vulnerability conflicts.</span></p>
<h2><span data-preserver-spaces="true">How do I embed a Figma in WordPress?</span></h2>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/wordpressloadingfigma.png" alt="figma being loaded on a wordpress site" width="650" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">When you embed a Figma file, you&#8217;re essentially embedding a live, interactive version of that file on another website or blog. That&#8217;s different from simply sharing a link to a Figma file, as anyone who visits the page where you&#8217;ve embedded the file will be able to interact with it, just as they would if they were viewing it on Figma.com. Embedding a Figma file in WordPress is a great way to show off your work or to provide an interactive element to a blog post or tutorial. Keep in mind that updates will automatically go live when changes are made to the original Figma file.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Here is a simple step-by-step guide for embedding a Figma file in WordPress:</span></p>
<ol>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Open the desired Figma file</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Click the Share button that is located in the top right corner of the screen</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Click the Embed tab</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You&#8217;ll see an Embed code appearing; copy it</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Use your WordPress editor to open the desired page of your website, then open the HTML tab</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It is time to paste the code where you want your Figma design to appear</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Save page</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">That&#8217;s it; now your visitors will be able to interact with your fantastic Figma design. However, if this doesn&#8217;t work for you, or the page doesn&#8217;t look the way you wanted it to, here is what you need to know:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You might need to adjust your iframe width and height depending on your WordPress theme</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Before embedding a Figma file, you need to make sure it&#8217;s published first</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It is essential to copy the right code from Figma in case of any error &#8211; repeat the whole process and explore similar options in the app</span></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="plugins"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Is there good Figma to WordPress plugins?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The answer to this question heavily depends on the complexity of your web project. If you plan on creating a simple website, some Figma to WordPress plugins will probably give you satisfying results. On the other hand, the chances that code errors will occur increase with the rising complexity of your Figma design.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you want to automate the process of converting Figma to WordPress, there is one plugin that you might find helpful &#8211; </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://www.figma.com/community/plugin/1452961512245649324/export-kit" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">ExportKit</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">. Using this plugin can save you time and money, and you only need to have a basic understanding of various WordPress theme structures to start using it. </span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/exportkitfigma.png" alt="wordpress exportkit and figma" width="650" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Still, you need to keep in mind that automatically generated codes still can&#8217;t compete with the ones that humans write. That&#8217;s why we advise you to either manually convert Figma to WordPress on your own or hire professional web developers to do it for you.</span></p>
<h2><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Get in touch</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Are you excited about turning your amazing Figma design into a fully functional WordPress website? There are multiple ways to achieve this, and Alpha Efficiency will help you choose the right one based on your needs. Here is what you&#8217;ll get by partnering up with our </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/web-design-agency-chicago" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Chicago web design agency</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">: </span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Fast and quality Figma to WordPress conversion &#8211;</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> Our team will ensure that each pixel of your Figma design displays on your website in the way you intended</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Perfect Figma to WordPress SEO build &#8211; </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While using Elementor and other page builders might sound like an easier option, it usually proves disastrous for your SEO results. By coding your WordPress theme from scratch, we&#8217;ll secure top-notch performance for your website.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Detailed progress reports &#8211; </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you&#8217;d like to get more involved in your Figma to WordPress project, our team will be open for full collaboration. </span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">24/7 support from our team &#8211; </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">To make sure everything goes as planned upon the launch date, our team will stay available to you at any time. Don&#8217;t hesitate to contact us in case any problem arises, and we&#8217;ll fix it on the shortest notice.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you want to turn your Figma designs into an astonishing WordPress website without having to write a single line of code yourself, we&#8217;d gladly help you. Feel free to</span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/schedule-a-call" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> schedule a call</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> so we can discuss your next project.</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/figmatowordpress.png',NULL,'[]','[166,354]','2022-12-06T11:24:22','2022-12-06T11:24:22',2446,7,5);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (wp_id,path,slug,type,track,title,meta_title,meta_description,canonical,robots_index,excerpt,body_html,hero_image,wp_template,tags,categories,published_at,updated_at,word_count,internal_links,image_count) VALUES
  (18546,'/organic-shapes-design','organic-shapes-design','post','blog','Will organic shapes change web design in 2024?','Will organic shapes change web design in 2024? - Alpha Efficiency','So what will happen in 2023? Will organic shapes continue to grow as a trend in web design, or will something new take over? ','https://alphaefficiency.com/organic-shapes-design',1,'Shapes are building blocks of every web and graphic design project. Web designers who know how to take advantage of different shape meanings have a better chance of building fresh-looking and high-converting websites. In recent years, we have seen a shift towards organic shapes in web design. The idea behind this is that more attention &hellip; Continued','<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Shapes are building blocks of every web and graphic design project. Web designers who know how to take advantage of different shape meanings have a better chance of building fresh-looking and high-converting websites. In recent years, we have seen a <strong>shift towards organic shapes in web design</strong>. The idea behind this is that more attention should be paid to the user experience and how users perceive the website. So what will happen in 2023? Will organic shapes continue to grow as a trend in web design, or will something new take over? </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">In this article, our </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/web-design-agency-chicago" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">web design agency in Chicago </span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">will give you a detailed insight into how the wider implementation of organic shapes design can impact the way companies interact with customers.</span></p>
<h5>Table of Contents</h5>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#types">How many different types of shapes do we have?</a></li>
<li><a href="/#geometric">What is the meaning of geometric shapes?</a></li>
<li><a href="/#organic">The meaning of organic shapes</a></li>
<li><a href="/#psychology">Is the Psychology of Shapes in Design a real thing?</a></li>
<li><a href="/#trends">Current web design trends</a></li>
<li><a href="/#2023">What will be popular in 2023?</a></li>
<li><a href="/#which">How to know which shapes to use when building websites?</a></li>
</ul>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/organicshapedesign.png" alt="example of organic shapes design" width="650" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h2 id="types"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">How many different types of shapes do we have?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Shapes play an essential role in our everyday lives. Shapes also play a crucial role in web design because they allow professionals to create a variety of user experiences. They can also be used to create emphasis and hierarchy on your website. But how many different types of shapes do we have? For instance, shapes can be categorized into three main groups:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Geometric shapes</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Organic Shapes</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Abstract shapes</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Deep knowledge of shape meanings will allow you to combine them into graphic design materials that trigger specific emotions in website visitors. Keep in mind that geometric, abstract, and organic shapes are equally important in web design, as each group can be used in a specific way to achieve desired business goals. In the following section of this article, we will explain the meaning of each shape type and how you can use it in your advance.</span></p>
<h3 id="geometric"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The meaning of geometric shapes</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Geometric shapes usually first come to mind when someone mentions word shapes. Web designers use such shapes as building blocks of a website&#8217;s look. It is a mathematical term for any two-dimensional figure that a set of points, lines, and curves can describe. It is possible to describe each geometric shape using mathematical equations. All geometric shapes are either polygons or non-polygons. A polygon is a closed geometric shape with three or more sides, while a non-polygon is a shape that is not formed by straight lines, therefore, has curved sides or is not entirely closed. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Let&#8217;s explore the most common geometric shape meanings in graphic design and web design:</span></p>
<h4>Squares and Rectangles</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Besides circles, squares and rectangles are considered basic shapes, meaning all other shapes are derived from them. These two shapes evoke feelings of trust and authority, and that&#8217;s why they are a popular choice in web design. A square can be used to create a simple and intuitive user interface for your website.</span></p>
<h4>Triangles</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">People often associate triangles with motion because of their dynamic look, and that&#8217;s why they are a popular choice in travel website design. A triangle can be used to create a more complex and interactive experience for your visitors. This shape usually evokes feelings of excitement, risk, danger, and similar &#8211; but in specific cases, web designers can utilize triangles to achieve a balanced and stable look of a website.</span></p>
<h4>Circles, Ovals, and Elipses</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Circles and similar shapes are specific because they don&#8217;t have angles. As they are often associated with Earth and Sun, such shapes often evoke feelings of harmony and peace in the observer. In graphic design, circles can be used to highlight an object, achieve a minimalistic look, put emphasis on a particular message, and create a youthful look. Keep in mind that you can use half circles to achieve a more dynamic look. Also, the halftone circle design has recently gained a lot of popularity among web content creators who want to achieve a unique visual appeal to their websites.</span></p>
<h4>Spirals</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Spirals can be found in nature, and that&#8217;s why people often associate them with growth. Graphic designers often use spiral shapes to achieve an aesthetically pleasing design that looks creative and intelligent. However, if used in a specific way, spiral shapes can also cause anxiety and create a sense of mystery.</span></p>
<h3 id="organic"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The meaning of organic shapes</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The easiest way to understand organic shapes is to think of them as shapes with natural, free-flowing curves. Unlike geometric shapes, which have clean lines and hard angles (except circles), organic shapes are often found in nature and are characterized by their smooth, flowing lines and lack of symmetry. Because organic shapes lack the mathematical precision that characterizes geometric shapes, they look unplanned and unorganized. Think of leaves, flowers, and clouds &#8211; these are all examples of organic shapes. While organic shapes are often found in nature, they can also be created by web and graphic designers who want to evoke specific emotions in website visitors. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Organic shapes design is often associated with the following:</span><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> </span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Nature</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Flow</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Freedom</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Unpredictability</span></li>
</ul>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The meaning of abstract shapes</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Abstract shapes are shapes that can represent real objects without being their exact representation. However, even though abstract shapes heavily rely on symbolism, they can also have no connection to anything that exists in the real world. Such shapes are often used in web design to create a feeling of space or to add visual interest. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> </span><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Graphic designers can create interesting abstract shapes in various ways &#8211; including drawing, painting, or using computer software. By implementing abstract shapes, web designers can add visual appeal to pages, break up content, and create a sense of movement. That can help you keep visitors engaged in exploring your website for a longer time. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> </span><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Abstract graphic design is very popular because it can convey a message without text, but unless you are utilizing it exclusively for aesthetic purposes, you should conduct research before implementing any abstract shape on your website. That is because, outside of the cultural context, such shapes have no real meaning. An example of abstract shapes is the hamburger menu icon. As we have seen many times, we don&#8217;t even need to think twice before clicking on it to navigate the website.</span></p>
<h2 id="psychology"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The Psychology of Shapes in Design</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Understanding the psychology of shapes is an incredibly important part of </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/custom-wordpress-website-design" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">custom WordPress website design</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">, as each shape influences a viewer&#8217;s emotions and perception. For example, rounded shapes are often seen as friendly and approachable, while angular shapes can be perceived as aggressive or harsh. The use of shapes can also create a sense of movement or energy, which can help draw attention to a particular area of a website.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> </span><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Unless you plan on applying concepts of minimalism, you will have to work with several types of shapes in your web design projects and find the best way to combine them. By using the right shapes, web designers can meet specific user requirements for a website design more efficiently. They can use geometric, abstract, and organic shapes to convey messages, evoke desired emotions and help users find what they&#8217;re looking for on a website without much trouble. </span></p>
<h2 id="benefits"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Main benefits of using organic shapes</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Organic shapes are gaining popularity among web designers, as there are numerous benefits to using them when creating a website. Once you understand different meanings of organic shapes, you can use them to: </span><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> </span></p>
<h4>Add a natural look and relax website visitors</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Organic shapes design can add a sense of naturalism and serenity to a website&#8217;s look. Unlike geometric shapes, organic shapes are not constrained by strict rules, which allows designers to create more fluid and natural designs. For example, using abstract floral artwork background or biophilic design on your website can help you relax your visitors and keep them exploring your pages for longer because organic shapes are less likely to cause eye strain.</span></p>
<h4>Build trust more easily</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Building trust with your potential customers is crucial for increasing conversion rates on your website. While there are many different ways to do it, such as implementing reviews and testimonials, how you design your visual elements will also play a huge role in visitors&#8217; decisions about whether to trust your business. As organic shapes are seen as friendly and approachable, you can utilize organic shapes design to start building trust with potential customers as soon as they land on one of your pages.</span></p>
<h4>Draw attention to a specific page area</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Organic shapes are visually attractive, and they have the power to grab attention quickly because of their distinctive look. That&#8217;s why organic shapes can help you guide a visitor&#8217;s focus to a page area of your choice and highlight your company&#8217;s name, special offers, specific messages, and similar.</span><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> </span></p>
<h2 id="trends"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Current web design trends</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Learning more about </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/latest-ui-ux-design-trends" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">current UI/UX trends </span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">before working on your next web project is crucial, as it can not help you extend the lifespan of your website but also increase conversion rates. Let&#8217;s explore some of the trends that have dominated the web design industry in 2022:</span></p>
<h4>Collage design elements</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Combining different shapes to create collage-style graphics is a powerful way to make your website pages visually attractive and memorable. That is especially a popular choice for the hero section. The collage-style graphic design opens opportunities for combining geometric, abstract, and organic shapes into powerful, eye-grabbing visuals that highlight the main brand&#8217;s message.</span></p>
<h4>Emphasis on white space</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The usage of white space has been the popular choice among web designers for a while, especially on websites with a large amount of information. Leaving the right amount of white space on your pages can help you better guide visitors&#8217; eyes, enhance the website&#8217;s navigation, and make it easier to optimize for a fantastic user experience on mobile devices.</span></p>
<h4>3D graphics</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">During 2022, web creators have increasingly used 3D graphical elements with the goal of creating eye-catching website designs. Since three-dimensional shapes look realistic, no matter how abstract they are, and that&#8217;s why they can hold attention for much longer than traditional 2D shapes. As this trend is likely to continue in the future, we recommend experimenting with 3D organic shapes design on some of your following web projects.</span></p>
<h2 id="2023"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">What will be popular in 2023?</span></h2>
<h4>Organic shapes design</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While geometric shapes have enjoyed the spotlight in recent years, we expect organic shape design to emerge as a massive trend in 2023. It is a great way to add a naturalistic feel to your website and make your business appear more friendly. And as they help web designers smoothly separate different sections of web pages, organic shapes are already a popular choice for background design.</span></p>
<h4>Combining photos with graphical elements</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Overlapping high-quality photos with geometric shapes such as squares, circles, and similar or even organic shapes to make visuals more exciting and eye-catching is already popular among web designers, and this trend is likely to continue during 2023.</span></p>
<h4>Abstract illustrations</h4>
<p>The current popularity of illustrations based around abstract shapes suggests that they will likely continue to grow as a trend in 2023. Abstract illustrations are visually attractive; they add contrast to web pages and successfully create a sense of minimalism in web design. Using an abstract wave motion illustration is a powerful way to grab visitors&#8217; attention and guide it to the brand&#8217;s name or unique offers. We also expect more and more websites to use abstract colorful vector backgrounds and abstract geometric backgrounds in the future, as those can encourage excitement in website visitors. Additionally, the integration of these styles in mobile app development and design is anticipated to rise, reflecting the increasing importance of visually engaging and user-friendly mobile interfaces.</p>
<h2 id="which"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">How to know which shapes to use when building websites for clients?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Choosing between basic and abstract shapes can be difficult when planning a website design. While there is no reason not to combine both, you need to base the decision on the client&#8217;s business&#8217;s short-term and long-term goals.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Use consultation calls to ask specific web design questions for clients in order to find out what they want to accomplish with their website &#8211; and then utilize the psychology of shapes to help them with that. If they want to appear approachable and friendly, opting for organic shapes design is probably the best course of action. On the other hand, if they want to achieve more of an authoritative look &#8211; using geometric shapes, such as squares and triangles, might be a better option. Just make sure to explain the meaning of each shape to your clients and how including it in their website design can benefit their business.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">However, keep in mind that you don&#8217;t have to follow the psychology of shapes strictly. Instead, use it as a guideline, and before launching a website, conduct A/B tests to find out how different designs influence the decisions of real users.</span></p>
<h2><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Do you need help from professional web designers?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Building a visually appealing website that functions perfectly is a task best handled by professionals with years of experience in the web design industry. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Alpha Efficiency follows only the best web design practices to build award-winning websites for its clients. Our </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/ecommerce-web-design-services" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">eCommerce web design services </span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">include applying the psychology of shapes to make your website more attractive and increase conversion rates by evoking the right emotions in your potential customers. </span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Get in touch</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">We hope this article helped you better understand the meanings of different shapes and how organic shapes design can change the way companies influence buyers&#8217; decisions. To stay in touch with the latest web design trends, keep reading Alpha Efficiency&#8217;s blog and start following us on social media channels.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you are interested in our web design and graphic design services, get in touch today by scheduling a call with one of our experts. During consultation calls, Alpha Efficiency&#8217;s team will try to learn as much as possible about your company culture and its business goals and create a detailed plan for your website that follows the latest web design trends. </span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/organicshapedesign.png',NULL,'[]','[357,353]','2022-12-08T13:46:14','2022-12-08T13:46:14',2342,4,1),
  (18568,'/duplicate-meta-descriptions','duplicate-meta-descriptions','post','blog','Are duplicate meta descriptions on your website a significant SEO risk?','Are duplicate meta descriptions is a SEO risk? - Alpha Efficiency.™','Our experts will share their opinion about duplicate meta descriptions with you and show you best practices when it comes to removing them.','https://alphaefficiency.com/duplicate-meta-descriptions',1,'If you&#8217;re like most website owners, you want to make sure your site is as search-engine-friendly as possible. However, many people get confused when it comes to the importance of meta descriptions. While we assure you that investing efforts into creating unique meta descriptions for each page on your site will prove beneficial for your &hellip; Continued','<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you&#8217;re like most website owners, you want to make sure your site is as search-engine-friendly as possible. However, many people get confused when it comes to the importance of meta descriptions. While we assure you that investing efforts into creating unique meta descriptions for each page on your site will prove beneficial for your business &#8211; you may still be wondering whether having duplicate meta descriptions across your website is a significant SEO risk.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">In this article, experts from our </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/seo-agency-chicago" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">SEO agency in Chicago</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> will share their opinion about duplicate meta descriptions with you and show you best practices when it comes to removing them. You&#8217;ll also be able to learn more about the importance of providing users with a brief description of your web pages in social media shares. Lastly, we&#8217;ll help you identify potential reasons why Google doesn&#8217;t use your descriptions on the SERPs. </span></p>
