</ul>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/duplicatemetadescription.png" alt="remove duplicate meta description" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h2 id="definition"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">What is a meta description?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you have a website, chances are you&#8217;ve come across the term &#8220;meta description&#8221; before. A meta description is an HTML element that briefly describes the content of a web page that appears in the search engine results, usually within 160 characters. Include this meta tag in the &lt;head&gt; section of your HTML. Here is what it should look like:</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">&lt;head&gt;</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">&lt;meta name=&#8221;description&#8221; content=&#8221;write your description here.&#8221;&gt;</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">&lt;/head&gt;</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Now that we understand what meta descriptions are let&#8217;s see why you should use them on your website.</span></p>
<h2 id="does"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Why Does Your Website Need Meta Descriptions?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Using meta descriptions can help you attract more search engine users to your website and improve the quality of your website traffic. They are meant to give the searcher an idea of what a page is about so they can decide if it&#8217;s relevant to their query. A well-written meta description can help you improve your website&#8217;s click-through rate (CTR), resulting in more traffic and, potentially, conversions. That makes them an essential aspect of on-page SEO. And as providing a great user experience is crucial for staying relevant in a highly competitive online sphere, you should also need to pay close attention to your website&#8217;s </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/text-to-html-ratio-seo" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">text-to-HTML ratio</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">.</span></p>
<h2 id="rankings"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Do meta descriptions affect search rankings?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Back in the day, meta tags were an important factor in search engine optimization. Focusing on the implementation of many keywords in meta descriptions and other meta tags was a common practice among SEO experts &#8211; which led to the birth of a practice known as &#8220;keyword stuffing.&#8221; To prevent low-quality content from ranking high in the SERPs, Google updated its algorithms and started penalizing website owners who did such practices.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Today, many website owners wonder whether or not meta descriptions still affect search rankings &#8211; and the answer is a little complicated. While meta descriptions are less important than they used to be and might not directly influence your Google rankings, they can highly influence click-through rate, which is an indicator of the overall quality of your search engine optimization.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Also, if your meta descriptions are misleading and don&#8217;t go hand-in-hand with content &#8211; the bounce rate percentage on your website might grow, sending negative ranking signals to search engines. That&#8217;s why, instead of ignoring the quality of your meta descriptions for your web pages, you need to follow best practices when writing them.</span></p>
<h3 id="social"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Meta descriptions in social shares</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Social meta descriptions are the short descriptions that appear beneath the title of your content when it&#8217;s shared on social media sites. Just like it&#8217;s the case with meta descriptions in the Google search console, meta descriptions in social shares give readers a brief summary of what your content is about, so they can be a powerful tool for driving traffic to your website.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A good social meta description should reflect the content on your page and be written in a way that is appealing to your target audience. While they may seem like a small detail, well-crafted meta descriptions in social shares can significantly impact your click-through rates. But what are the maximum number of characters Facebook and Twitter show when displaying meta descriptions? Let&#8217;s check:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Facebook: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The largest social media site displays up to 300-character-long descriptions of your pages</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Twitter</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">: With Twitter Card markup, you&#8217;ll get 200 characters to work with when providing users with brief descriptions of your web pages</span></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="duplicate"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">What are duplicate meta descriptions?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Duplicate meta descriptions are a common problem for website owners. That happens when the same meta description is used for more than one page on a website. Duplicate meta descriptions often occur on large e-Commerce websites when owners try to save time by copying the same meta description for multiple product pages instead of investing efforts to write a unique text for each.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Another reason why duplicate meta descriptions and meta titles might occur is that you are not correctly using a WordPress plugin for managing them. For example, if you set a meta description for your homepage using Yoast SEO plugin, it will automatically set it for paginated pages too. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While search engines won&#8217;t penalize you for having duplicate meta descriptions, this can be a problem because it can make your website look unorganized. You&#8217;ll also miss opportunities to attract more visitors to your web pages by including unique keywords that meet their search queries. And as your pages with the same meta description compete with one another, you&#8217;ll reduce the chances of ranking them all high in search engines.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Although duplicate meta descriptions are less harmful to your SEO than duplicate content issues, it is usually worth investing time into writing unique meta tags for each web page.</span></p>
<h2 id="google"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Why won&#8217;t Google use my meta description?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you&#8217;ve been wondering why Google isn&#8217;t using your meta description, you&#8217;re not alone. In fact, </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://ahrefs.com/blog/meta-description-study/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Google rewrites meta descriptions nearly 63% of the time</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">. The search engine giant has been known to ignore meta descriptions and pick a sentence from your copy instead, which can be frustrating for webmasters who want control over how their pages are presented in search results. So without further due, here are potential reasons why the descriptions you had written are not being displayed on the SERPs:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Your description is not relevant to search queries</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Your descriptions are too long or too short</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The search engine is pulling information from somewhere else</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Google still hasn&#8217;t crawled the updated version of your page</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Robot meta tag issues are disabling your meta description</span></li>
</ul>
<h3 id="unique"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Are Unique Meta Descriptions Important?</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">By writing unique meta descriptions, you can make your site stand out in SERPs and eventually attract more visitors. And by giving potential visitors an idea of what your web pages are about before they even click on them, you can reduce bounce rates which will prove beneficial for your rankings. And keep in mind that having the same meta description on every page tells potential visitors that you haven&#8217;t put any thought into your site, which can negatively influence your brand&#8217;s credibility.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Here are some tips for improving the quality of your meta descriptions:</span></p>
<h5>The first sentence matters the most</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The first sentence is most likely to determine whether or not someone clicks on your link. You have to make sure it&#8217;s interesting and relevant to what the users are looking for. </span></p>
<h5>Include your focus keyword</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You need to ensure that your focus keyword is at the front and center of your meta description. By seeing a keyword that they&#8217;ve typed in the Google Search Console, potential visitors will know that you might have an answer to their problems. That&#8217;s why including the focus keyword in your first sentence will help you get more hits and improve the quality of your traffic.</span></p>
<h5>Limit them to 155-160 characters</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While there is no perfect length for meta descriptions, it is generally a good idea to keep them under 160 characters long so they can be fully displayed on the search engine results page.</span></p>
<h5>Use active voice and emphasize the action</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Active voice makes your descriptions more engaging and easier to read, which can lead to higher click-through rates. In addition, using active voice can help you communicate your message more clearly and concisely. That is especially important given the limited space you have to work with. So give your best to deeply understand what motivates your potential visitors before writing meta descriptions.</span></p>
<h5>Ensure meta descriptions match your content</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Excitingly clicking on a web page link after reading the meta description only to find out that the content doesn&#8217;t deliver on the promise is a very frustrating experience. To avoid annoying your visitors, which usually leads to high bounce rates, ensure that your descriptions represent content on your pages as accurately as possible.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Writing unique meta tags for each page can be very resource-consuming if you run a large e-commerce website with countless product pages. Knowing that Google might rewrite your descriptions anyway, it usually doesn&#8217;t even pay off. In this case, we recommend focusing on the keywords with the highest search volume and the pages that generate the most traffic. </span></p>
<h3 id="duplicate"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">How To Remove Duplicate Meta Descriptions</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you identify duplicate meta descriptions on your website during your SEO audit, there is no need to worry. Chances are that these didn&#8217;t do much harm to your rankings. However, to help you make your business appear more professional, we have prepared duplicate meta descriptions SEO solutions you can apply:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Manually remove duplicate meta descriptions:</span></strong></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This approach can be very time-consuming, as you&#8217;ll first have to manually identify all the web pages with the same meta description and then write a unique description for each. We advise against this approach unless you have a team of SEO experts by your side.</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Remove duplicate meta descriptions by using Yoast SEO plugin:</span></strong></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Instead of a manual approach, we recommend using Yoast SEO plugin to fix this issue on your website. Once you access this plugin through your WordPress dashboard, navigate to Search Appearence&gt;General&gt;Homepage tab. After you write the meta description you want to show on SERPs for your homepage, add the &#8220;%%page%%&#8221; tag at the end. That will solve the duplicate meta description problem for paginated pages we discussed earlier in this article.</span></p>
<h2><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Get in touch with SEO professionals</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Are you having trouble achieving high search engine rankings for your website, no matter how much effort you invest? Google is constantly updating its algorithms; it can take a lot of work to keep up with the latest trends in the SEO industry &#8211; especially when you have a business to run.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you are looking for a reliable partner to help you connect with more potential customers through search engines, feel free to get in touch with our </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">digital marketing agency</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">. Alpha Efficiency hires an experienced team of SEO professionals with a proven track record in the most competitive industries. We will craft an advanced SEO strategy completely based on your business goals and put it into action so you can enjoy the benefits of increased online visibility.</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/duplicatemetadescription.png',NULL,'[]','[318,344]','2022-12-16T07:41:54','2022-12-16T07:41:54',1870,3,1),
  (18577,'/are-web-designers-in-demand','are-web-designers-in-demand','post','blog','Are web designers in demand?','Are web designers in demand? - Alpha Efficiency.™','If you are planning to start a new career, one of the first questions that might come to your mind is are web designers in demand or not.','https://alphaefficiency.com/are-web-designers-in-demand',1,'As the web design industry is constantly evolving, many people who would love to start a web design career wonder if it is still a wise choice. That shouldn&#8217;t come as a surprise, considering the uprise of DIY website creation platforms and artificial intelligence systems that will inevitably reduce the need for some of the &hellip; Continued','<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">As the web design industry is constantly evolving, many people who would love to start a web design career wonder if it is still a wise choice. That shouldn&#8217;t come as a surprise, considering the uprise of DIY website creation platforms and artificial intelligence systems that will inevitably reduce the need for some of the currently existing jobs. But are web designers in demand, and what are the benefits of starting a career in this industry in 2023?</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">After years of experience helping clients achieve their web presence goals, experts from our </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/web-design-agency-chicago" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">web design agency in Chicago</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> decided to share their opinion regarding the web designer job outlook.</span></p>
<h5>Table of Contents</h5>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#career">Is Web Design A Good Career Choice in 2023?</a></li>
<li><a href="/#web-dev-vs-web-design">What Do Web Developers and Web Designers do?</a></li>
<li><a href="/#benefits">10 Benefits of a Web Designer Career</a></li>
<li><a href="/#ready">Are you ready to Become a Web Designer?</a></li>
</ul>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/webdesigncareer.png" alt="Are web designers in demand" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h2 id="career"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Is Web Design A Good Career Choice in 2023?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you are planning to start a web design career in 2023, one of the first questions that might come to your mind is whether web designers are in demand or not. The answer is simple &#8211; there is still an increased demand for people who provide professional web design, web development, and graphic design services, and it will only grow in the following years as we are just entering the digital era. Bureau Labor statistics suggest that the demand for both web developers and web designers will increase by up to 13 percent by the end of the decade, which is a higher rate than with most other jobs.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The average web designer&#8217;s salary is currently around $60,000 per year and is also expected to grow continuously during the 2020s. That&#8217;s because many companies are shifting their focus to opening online shops, and an increased number of people find it more convenient to order products and services online. To increase their chances of standing in front of the competition, businesses hire professional web designers and web developers to build websites for them. </span></p>
<h2 id="web-dev-vs-web-design"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">What Do Web Developers and Web Designers do?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Many young people struggle to decide when choosing between tech jobs. For those who enjoy building websites for clients, the dilemma usually falls to picking either web design or web development. However, before starting a web design career, it is crucial to understand all the differences between web development and web design jobs.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A web developer is responsible for writing the code that makes a website work, while a web designers work on enhancing the look and feel of a website. It means that a web developer might also help with the design of a website but is not typically responsible for its layout or design. A web designer might create the entire layout of a website or just a part of it. Web design job includes providing graphic design services to clients and creating high-quality visuals for their websites.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Please note that people often confuse front-end development with web design. The best way to understand the difference between those two jobs is to imagine a button on a website: </span><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> </span></p>
<h4>Web Designers</h4>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web designers</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> work on enhancing the visual aspects of that button; they need to ensure that it looks good and the target audience will want to click on it. Of course, web designer jobs are much more complex than providing graphic design services, as web designers also need to design the whole logic behind the website and its structure. Web designers also need to communicate with clients to learn about their web presence goals and adjust web design to </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/how-web-design-can-build-trust-with-customers" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">build trust with customers </span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">who arrive on their websites.</span></p>
<h4>Front-end web developers</h4>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Front-end web developers</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> are responsible for the functionality of that button; they need to make sure that it is clickable, that the animation is working, and that it takes users to the desired place. They enable visitors to interact with a website.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Besides front-end development, there is also back-end development. Web developers&#8217; job is also to maintain the website and protect it from cyber-attacks. However, it would help if you also understood the differences between an</span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/ios-vs-web-development" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> iOS developer vs. web developer</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> job before starting a career. All in all, to step into a web development world, you usually need to learn at least some of the following programming languages:</span><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> </span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">JavaScript</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Java</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">HTML</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">PHP</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Ruby</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Python</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Angular</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">To successfully start a web design career, aim to develop your web design skills in the following software and markup languages:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Adobe InDesign</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Illustrator</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">XD</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Photoshop</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Figma</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">JavaScript basics</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">HTML and CSS basics</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While some believe that web development is more challenging to learn than web design, mastering any skill will take a lot of time and effort. That&#8217;s why you should choose a career path that suits your preferences. If money is one of the key motivators for you when choosing between tech jobs, keep in mind that a software developer&#8217;s salary is usually higher than the average salary web designers get. However, you can make a solid living with your web design work, especially after a few years in the industry, since the web designer job outlook remains positive.</span></p>
<h2 id="benefits"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Benefits of Web Designer Career</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Besides getting an answer to the question of whether web designers are in demand or not, it is also essential to understand the benefits web designer jobs provide. There are many benefits to pursuing a career in web design, including the opportunity to work in a creative field, have flexible hours, and make a good living. So let&#8217;s dive deeper into this subject and find out what you can expect when you start a web design career:</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web designers can work remotely</span></h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Most web design agencies allow their employees to work from anywhere in the world. That is possible because web developers and web designers work on computers, and with modern technology, they can easily stay in touch with the rest of the team. Hiring remote workers allows a web design agency to expand its business operations more quickly, and it also opens opportunities for people who prefer working from the comfort of their homes. Remote workers often report higher satisfaction levels with their jobs than those who work in an office. Here are just some of the reasons why this might be the case:</span><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> </span></p>
<h4>Better work-life balance</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you have family or personal obligations that prevent you from being available during traditional work hours, you will be able to achieve a healthy work-life balance by choosing a web design career. Working 8 hours shifts away from home can drastically reduce the time you get to spend with your family, especially when we count on the time lost in lengthy commutes. </span></p>
<h4>Higher productivity</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">At the office, you can expect your productivity to drop from time to time due to lengthy conversations with colleagues and other distractions that can easily move your focus away from web design work. Research suggests that </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://www.apollotechnical.com/working-from-home-productivity-statistics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">77% of workers</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> reported increased productivity when working from home. Higher productivity will allow you to enhance the quality of your graphic design services even more.</span></p>
<h4>Cost savings</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Working from home can save you commuting costs as you won&#8217;t have to pay for public transportation services or car maintenance if you are going to work with your own vehicle. It can also save money you&#8217;d have to invest in buying &#8216;business&#8217; clothes. Of course, you&#8217;ll still need fresh clothes for other occasions; we&#8217;re just suggesting that adequately dressing up for an office can be expensive.</span></p>
<h4>Flexibility</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Remote web design work opens opportunities for a lot of flexibility. You can go to a local coffee shop, beach, and from any country in the world as long as you have internet access. If their employers agree, people can even do web design jobs outside of traditional work hours.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">However, keep in mind that when starting a remote job, it is the best practice to remove any distractions that might reduce your productivity. For best results, web developers and web designers need to create their own workspace at home and set boundaries with household members.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You Don&#8217;t Need to Go to School to Become a Web Designer</span></h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While a bachelor&#8217;s degree in computer science or other relative fields, such as graphic design or marketing, will give you a leg up in the industry, you don&#8217;t necessarily need to go to college to start a web design career. In fact, there are many successful associate degree web design workers who are in high demand because of their web design skills.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Once you get a good grasp on UX typography, Adobe Illustrator basic shapes, and design composition, and you manage to put web design theory into practice, you should be able to land a web design job without much trouble. We recommend completing certificate courses or similar education learning programs crafted specifically for web designers, as those will help you upgrade your web design skills much faster than learning everything on your own.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Web Design allows you to be creative</span></h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You might also be wondering, are web designers in demand during the era of DIY website building platforms and artificial intelligence systems uprise? To successfully provide </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/ecommerce-web-design-services" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">eCommerce web design services</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">, besides technical skills, you also need a high dose of creativity that will allow you to come up with the right solutions for each client.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">To become successful, web designers and web developers need to have a vision of how the website will look and function from start to finish. They have to think outside the box and come up with unique ideas that will make a website stand out when compared to the competition. Agencies highly value web designers who can shine on the creative side of web projects.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Chance to work with advanced technology</span></h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">From graphic design services to advanced WordPress custom web design, web designers work with advanced software to deliver satisfying client results. If you are a tech enthusiast, you will enjoy doing a web design job. While some professionals fear that artificial intelligence systems might reduce the demand for professional web designers, it is likely that AI will actually help web developers improve the quality of their work and allow them to focus on the creative side of web projects.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Plenty of opportunities in a growing web industry</span></h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Once you polish your web design skills and build a name for yourself in the industry, you will have plenty of opportunities at your disposal. You will be able to choose between working for a web design agency or working as a freelancer. Both agency and freelance career paths have their own pros and cons &#8211; but for beginners, we recommend getting an agency job, as it will allow you to improve your design skills faster by observing more experienced colleagues.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It is also worth noting that the average salary web developers and web designers get is expected to grow during this decade, which means you will experience an improvement in your life standard as you progress in a web design career. Bureau Labor Statistics show that we can expect about 22,000 web designer job openings each year until 2031. That suggests that there will be a lot of opportunities for getting hired in a growing web design industry. </span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You get to help client&#8217;s businesses grow</span></h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you are still wondering whether web designers are in demand or not, remind yourself of the number of businesses that are struggling to grow their business in the digital environment. As a web designer, you will work closely with a team of web developers to turn website ideas into reality. There is always a special thrill in helping a small restaurant owner or a small clinic achieve a successful online presence and grow their businesses. </span></p>
<h2 id="ready"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Ready to Become a Web Designer?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">So are web designers in demand? We can assure you that passionate web designers and web developers with well-crafted skill sets are always welcome at Alpha Efficiency!</span></p>
<p><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/designer" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Join our team</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> and discover new career web design opportunities that are waiting for you. We offer fully remote work and plenty of chances to achieve personal growth while working on exciting web projects. So are you ready to become a web designer?</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/webdesigncareer.png',NULL,'[]','[353]','2022-12-17T11:36:46','2022-12-17T11:36:46',2025,5,1),
  (18584,'/website-content-migration','website-content-migration','post','blog','The Secret to Proper Website Content Migration','The Secret to Proper Website Content Migration - Alpha Efficiency.™','Our digital marketing agency have prepared some tips to help you smoothly go through the website content migration process.','https://alphaefficiency.com/website-content-migration',1,'One of the main fears business owners face when planning a site location change or a complete website redesign is losing hard-earned search engine rankings due to website content migration. And this is for a good reason, as a poorly executed content migration project can quickly become a user experience nightmare and setback their business &hellip; Continued','<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">One of the main fears business owners face when planning a site location change or a complete website redesign is losing hard-earned search engine rankings due to website content migration. And this is for a good reason, as a poorly executed content migration project can quickly become a user experience nightmare and setback their business for a few years. While content migration can be incredibly frustrating, it is also necessary for keeping your website&#8217;s high-performance levels after drastic changes.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you&#8217;re about to undertake a content migration, there are a few things you need to keep in mind. That&#8217;s why content migration experts from our </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">digital marketing agency</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> have prepared some tips to help you smoothly go through the website content migration process.</span></p>
<h5>Table of Contents</h5>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#migration">What is content migration?</a></li>
<li><a href="/#properly">6 steps on how to properly migrate your content to a new website</a></li>
<li><a href="/#issues">7 common issues with content migration</a></li>
<li><a href="/#tools">Are there any tools for website content migration?</a></li>
</ul>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/websitecontentmigration.png" alt="website content migration" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h2 id="migration"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">What is Content Migration?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Website content migration is the process of moving content from one content management system to another. It typically occurs in a </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/when-is-it-time-to-redesign-your-website" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">website redesign</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> or when a company completely changes its web platform. It&#8217;s essential to carefully plan your website content migration project so that none of the old content is lost and to ensure that you place it in the right spot after redesign or site location change. But what is even meant by the term &#8220;content&#8221;? Shortly speaking, we can refer to all the pieces of information on your website that help you deliver your message to visitors as content. Some of the common content types include:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Text</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Videos</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Images</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Links</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Documents</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">However, you shouldn&#8217;t approach content migration just like it&#8217;s a long copy-paste work between content management systems. Instead, think of it as a chance to re-write, re-organize, and re-structure your content to improve and clean your website and boost its performance with both internet users and search engines. </span></p>
<h2 id="properly"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">How to Properly Migrate Your Content to a New Website</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you&#8217;re planning on migrating your website to a new domain, there are a few things you need to do in order to ensure that you migrate the content successfully. Failing to do so could result in a loss of traffic and search engine rankings.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">There are a few key things to keep in mind when migrating content:</span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Analyze Data from Your Old Website</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Analyzing data from your old website can help you better understand your audience and what they are looking for. Gaining an insight into how users interact with your website content is crucial for improving the overall user experience on the new site and providing them with the content types they enjoy the most. This process should go smoothly if you have Google Analytics connected to your website. When analyzing website data for your content migration project, do the following:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Identify 50 pages that attract the most traffic: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">These are the pages that your target audience is the most interested in, so prioritize them during the content migration process.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Identify 50 pages that attract the least traffic: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Content on these pages might not be interesting to your target audience, so you can potentially ignore them when migrating your content.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Identify 50 pages with the highest bounce rate: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Topics on these pages might interest your website visitors, but consider rewriting the content to keep people engaged.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You can also conduct a short survey with your website visitors to find out which pages they loved the most, but keep in mind that the results you&#8217;ll get will be more subjective than those in Google Analytics. Still, surveys are helpful in case you didn&#8217;t set up any tool for analyzing your content performance on time. Hiring professional </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/7-essential-steps-to-profitable-keyword-research-service-that-drive-results" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">keyword research services</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> can also help you identify hot topics, improve your content quality, and boost your new website&#8217;s performance in search engines.</span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Determine a Content Migration Plan</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Once you obtain a good insight into the content performance on your old site, it is time to create a content migration plan. A content migration plan is a roadmap that outlines how you&#8217;ll move the content from its current location to its new home. To create it, you need to answer the following questions:</span></p>
<h5>Who will perform the content migration?</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If your company doesn&#8217;t have enough resources to migrate the website content successfully, consider outsourcing this work to the content migration team from another company.</span></p>
<h5>How long will the website content migration process last?</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It is not a good idea to make all site changes at once, as it could be disastrous for your search engine rankings. If you rush with your content migration work, you won&#8217;t be able to identify what went wrong in case any problem occurs. Ideally, you want to spread your website migration project over two months.</span></p>
<h5>Why are we performing a website content migration?</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">To successfully plan your content migration project, you first need to know which goals you want to accomplish with it. Understanding whether you want to improve your domain authority, do a complete rebrand, or change site architecture will allow you to create a more detailed plan for your web project.</span></p>
<h5>How are we going to preserve inbound and internal links?</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Links are an important part of how search engines index and rank content. If links are broken or redirected improperly, it can negatively impact the visibility of the content in search engines. Additionally, broken links can frustrate potential customers resulting in poor user experience.</span></p>
<h5>What is our 301 Redirect strategy?</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">When performing site location changes, it is crucial to set up 301 redirects as soon as possible. This way, you&#8217;ll tell search engines that your website has permanently moved to a new location so that users will be redirected automatically to your new address. A proper </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/the-only-guide-to-profitable-b2b-seo-youll-ever-need" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">SEO strategy</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> for content migration will help you preserve your rankings and avoid enormous traffic drops.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">With a bit of planning, migrating your content to a new website can be a painless process. It will allow you to avoid potential problems and ensure that all your content is transferred to the new platform smoothly.</span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Create a Content Inventory</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Before starting content migration work, it is crucial to have a clear picture of your overall content plan in mind &#8211; and there are not many better ways to achieve this other than taking a look at your content inventory. Simply put, a content inventory lists all the content on your website. That includes text, images, videos, and anything else on the site. A content inventory is essential for content migration because it helps you understand your content, its location, and how it is structured. This information is essential for planning and successfully executing a website content migration project, and that&#8217;s why you should create a content inventory before making serious site changes. Without a content inventory, it would be difficult to know what content needs to be migrated, where to migrate it to, and how to preserve its structure and organization. Keeping your content inventory organized will also help you prevent potential content loss during the migration process. To get started, include the following information next to each content piece:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">URL</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Publishing date</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Author</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Content Format</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Links included</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Does it need to be updated in the future</span></li>
</ul>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Well-organized content inventory</span></h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Well-organized content inventory will help your content migration team decide on the following:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Which content can they migrate in bulk during site changes</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">What they can move but will need to edit once the content migration work is done</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">What content can be excluded entirely from the website migration project </span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Which content types will need to be recreated</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Which users need to get access to the new Content Management System, and which roles and permissions they&#8217;ll have</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It is also crucial to keep track of the performance of different pages on your website. During content migration, prioritize the pages that bring the most traffic. To clean your website, you might want to completely ignore unused and low-performing content pieces during migration. However, if you still believe these articles have potential, consider hiring </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/website-copywriting-services-chicago" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">copywriting services in Chicago</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> to help you improve the quality of your old content work and enrich your new website with fresh content.</span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Define New Site Architecture</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">When migrating content to a new site, it is important to first plan the new site architecture. That will ensure that all content is categorized correctly and easy to find. A well-organized site will be easier for users to navigate and will encourage them to keep exploring your content for more extended periods.</span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Create a New Sitemap</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you try to migrate content without creating a new site structure first, you may end up with many broken links and other problems. That&#8217;s why it is important to work with your web design team on creating a new sitemap after analyzing your data and having the strategy in place. Taking your time to improve the sitemap is crucial if you want to improve the user experience for website visitors. Strive towards making your sitemap as simple as possible.</span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Migrate Your Content</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While the content migration process can be automated or done manually, the most common scenario is when both approaches are combined. Your web developers can create tools that will help you save time by moving content pieces in bulk between content management systems. However, you can rarely utilize such tools for transferring all the data when making site changes without harming your business&#8217;s online performance &#8211; and that&#8217;s why manual copy-paste work is crucial for a successful content migration project. By actively monitoring the process, you&#8217;ll be able to identify potential problems with the new CMS and fix them on time. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">No matter if you opt for a fully automated, manual, or combined approach &#8211; here is what your content migration process should look like:</span></p>
<ol>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Verify that you have created a functional backup</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Ensure bots can&#8217;t crawl your new site</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Perform a test migration</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you have changed your domain, you need to update your DNS and set up a proper redirect from the old site location to the new one</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If test migration has gone well, do the real content migration work</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Allow bots to crawl your new website again</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Test the performance of your new website, and keep an eye on the page speed</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Take necessary measures to avoid duplicate content</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Keep tracking the performance of your new content pieces in search engines in the long run</span></li>
</ol>
<h2 id="issues"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Common Issues with Content Migration</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Content migration is a big undertaking. There are a lot of moving parts, and if any one of them is not executed correctly, it can cause serious problems. Common issues with content migration include: </span></p>
<h5>Loss of data</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This can happen if you don&#8217;t adequately back up the data or if there is an issue with the migration process itself.</span></p>
<h5>Issues with data quality</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If not addressed, these issues can lead to lost or corrupted data, which can impact the usability of the new website.</span></p>
<h5>Formatting issues</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you don&#8217;t migrate the content properly, the formatting can be lost or changed, which can cause problems with displaying the content correctly.</span></p>
<h5>Links breaking</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If links are not migrated correctly, they can break, preventing users from accessing the content they need. If you have set up your content inventory correctly, you should be able to avoid this problem.</span></p>
<h5>Issues related to the migration process</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">These issues usually occur because of poor planning of project duration, lack of proper communication between content migration team members, lack of expertise, and no quality control strategy in place.</span></p>
<h5>Poorly set up redirects</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Redirects that are not well executed can cause users to be confused and might register as a 404 error to Google. For example, this can happen if there is a large number of old URLs redirected to an unconnected page, such as the homepage of the new site, instead of adequately setting redirects for each page.</span></p>
<h5>Crawlable testing environment</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">When migrating content to a new platform, it is important to set up a staging environment where you can test changes. However, if you forget to send signals to Google bots not to crawl your testing environment, you might end up with your content being marked as a duplicate or even accessible to users. This way, the SEO journey for your new website will start on the wrong foot, potentially harming your rankings long term.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While content migration can be time-consuming, expensive, and complex &#8211; by following the steps outlined in this article, you can avoid the common pitfalls and ensure a successful migration process. </span></p>
<h2><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Tools for Website Content Migration</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Using the right tools during the content migration process can save you a lot of time and energy and help your team members better coordinate their duties. Although we advise against completely automating the content migration work, experience has taught us that lack of proper tools can cause various problems &#8211; from data loss and compatibility issues to difficulties managing your content migration team. In this section, we&#8217;ll explore some of the most valuable tools that will help you easily keep track of your content inventory and the overall progress of your web project.</span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Tools for creating Asset Sheets</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">An asset sheet is a document that contains a list of all the assets that you need to migrate from one content management system (CMS) to another. It will contain all the text, images, metadata, page titles, URL, and instructions for your content migration team members. That can be especially helpful if you are moving a large amount of content or if you need to move content from one CMS to multiple content management systems. The following tools might help you with managing your asset sheets:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Confluence</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Google Suite</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Office 365</span></li>
</ul>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Tools for Tracking Progress</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Progress tracking tools can help you during content migration by allowing you to see how much content has been moved, what remains to be moved, and what errors have occurred. That can help you to plan and execute your content migration more effectively and avoid potential problems. We found these tools very helpful for tracking the progress of our content migration projects:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/trello-for-digital-marketing"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Trello</span></a></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Jira</span></li>
<li><a href="https://www.google.com/sheets"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Google Sheets</span></a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365/excel"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Excel</span></a></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While Trello and Jira are more advanced software for team management, you shouldn&#8217;t completely give up on classic tools such as Google Sheets and Excel, as these can also help you keep everyone informed about website content migration work progress.</span></p>
<h2 id="contact"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Contact us</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Website content migration can be tricky, and if you fail to execute it correctly, many obstacles will arise in your journey of building a strong online presence. That&#8217;s why, unless you are 100% confident in your skills, you should hire an expert content migration team to help you with your web project. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">With years of experience in successfully completing content migration projects for websites of various sizes, Alpha Efficiency might be the right partner for you. Don&#8217;t hesitate to </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/schedule-a-call" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">schedule a free consultation call</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> and introduce us to your business, so we can help you with finding the most effective solution for meeting your needs. Let&#8217;s get in touch today!</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/websitecontentmigration.png',NULL,'[]','[344,354]','2022-12-21T13:56:02','2026-03-09T12:13:42',2512,7,1);
