<h2><span data-preserver-spaces="true">What makes a good construction company website?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Good construction company websites serve as the online face of businesses. They help potential clients learn more about a company and its services. A good construction company website will help you establish credibility and professionalism and serve as a valuable tool in attracting new clients and growing your construction business. In this section, we&#8217;ll dive deep into areas that all good construction company websites have in common. Whether you&#8217;re creating a website on your own or you decide to hire a construction web design company, make sure to pay close attention to these:</span></p>
<h2 id="custom">Custom Construction Website Design: The Key to Success</h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">With the rise in popularity of drag-and-drop page builders, many construction companies fall into the trap of using them before even considering the advantages of a custom web design. These advantages include the following:</span></p>
<h5>It can be tailored for your brand</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Hiring a website design company instead of using templated websites will allow you to create a unique and consistent visual identity that reflects your brand&#8217;s values and personality. Custom web design gives you the flexibility to create a construction company website tailored to your specific needs and goals that delivers a cohesive user experience.</span></p>
<h5>Improved functionality</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">With a custom design, you can build custom functionality crucial for thriving in your industry. For example, our </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/web-development-agency-chicago" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">web development company in Chicago</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> implements functional forms for lead generation, custom shopping cart packages for selling products online, booking systems, customized content management systems, unique calculators for potential clients, and much more on construction company websites.</span></p>
<h5>Better SEO performance</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Custom web design offers many more opportunities to follow best SEO practices. From tailoring the design to the needs of the business and the target audience in order to improve the user experience to creating clean site architecture that helps search engines crawl your pages more easily, creating a </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/custom-coded-websites" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">custom-coded website</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> will give you much more control compared to following no-code solutions.</span></p>
<h5>Competitive advantage</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While drag-and-drop platforms allow you to customize your website to some extent, it will still look and feel similar to competitors&#8217; websites built with the same templates. On the other hand, construction website designs built by a professional construction web design agency not only have better performance but also look unique. That can help you stand out from competitors and create a memorable experience for website visitors.</span></p>
<h3 id="navigation"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Intuitive Navigation Will Help You Keep Website Visitors Longer</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you want to help users quickly and easily find the information they need, it is crucial to design an intuitive navigation for your construction company website. When a website has intuitive navigation, visitors are more likely to stay on the website longer, explore more pages, and return in the future. That can lead to increased engagement and conversions. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">On the other hand, </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://bloggingwizard.com/website-statistics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">37% of users claim</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> that poor navigation causes them to abandon the website. And the last thing you want is to have visitors leave your construction company website without finding any helpful information. That can lead to a high bounce rate, negatively impacting your website&#8217;s search engine rankings and overall performance.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">But how can you design easy-to-use navigation for your website? Here are some tips from our website design company that may help you get started:</span></p>
<h5>Start by considering the user&#8217;s needs and goals</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">What information are the website visitors looking for, and what do they want to accomplish on the website? The answer to this question will help you determine what links and categories to include in the navigation menu. Make sure to use clear labels to help users understand where each link leads to.</span></p>
<h5>Use visual hierarchy to draw attention to important links and sections</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You should use different font sizes, bolding, find adequate content body width, and add visual elements like icons or images to create a strong visual hierarchy. This way, you can naturally guide visitors&#8217; eyes and influence their decisions in the desired direction. </span></p>
<h5>Keep the navigation menu simple and organized</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Use clear, descriptive labels for each link, and group similar links together. Avoid using too many links or sub-menus, as this can make the navigation menu confusing and overwhelming.</span></p>
<h5>Use a consistent structure for the navigation menu</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This can help users learn how to navigate a construction company website more easily and feel comfortable using it.</span></p>
<h5>Test navigation on mobile devices</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It is crucial to ensure that your construction web design is intuitive for smartphone and tablet users. Many famous companies use hamburger menus to achieve this.</span></p>
<h5>Conduct user testing</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">By testing the navigation with real users, you can best determine how intuitive it is. That will allow you to identify issues and make improvements before finalizing the construction company web design.</span></p>
<h3 id="seo"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">SEO-Friendly Construction Web Design is The Key to Boosting Online Visibility</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you want your website to be seen by search engine users searching for the products or services you offer, you need to create an SEO-friendly construction web design. Increased traffic to your website can easily translate into more leads and sales for your business.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Several elements of SEO-friendly construction web design can help you improve your search engine rankings, including:</span></p>
<h5>Choose a relevant domain name</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">From an SEO perspective, a relevant domain name can help your website rank better in search results for specific keywords. For example, if your construction company specializes in residential renovations, consider including keywords such as &#8220;residential&#8221; and &#8220;renovations&#8221; in your domain name. On the other hand, beautiful interior design websites could benefit from having &#8220;interior design&#8221; in their domain name. With a relevant domain name, you can establish credibility for your business and earn the trust of customers who seek specific services.</span></p>
<h5>Conduct comprehensive keyword research</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Keyword research can help you identify the most relevant and popular keywords to use on your construction company website. By using these keywords in your content, you can satisfy user search intent, improve your rankings and attract more qualified traffic.</span></p>
<h5>Use alt text for images</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Alt text is a brief description of an image displayed when the image can&#8217;t load for website visitors. And as search engine algorithms don&#8217;t understand the meaning of images, by adding alt text, you can let crawlers know what your images are all about. That is important for improving your rankings and improving visibility in Google Images.</span></p>
<h5>Create descriptive and keyword-rich URLs</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">By using descriptive and keyword-rich URLs for your web pages, you can help search engines understand the content of your page, which will eventually earn you better rankings.</span></p>
<h5>Work on improving Page Speed</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">There are several reasons why </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/site-speed-and-seo" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">site speed and SEO</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> go hand in hand. Page speed affects both the user experience and search engine rankings. If the page takes too long to load, users may become frustrated and leave the construction company website, leading to a high bounce rate. Search engines want to deliver the best possible experience for users; therefore, by improving page speed, you can improve your rankings (or not lose them, at least). That&#8217;s why your construction website team needs to utilize browser catching and minimize large JavaScript and CSS files. And as there will probably be a lot of images on your construction website, you&#8217;ll need to optimize image file sizes to make your pages load faster.</span></p>
<h5>Structure your pages with header tags</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Use header tags (H1, H2, etc.) to help search engines understand the hierarchy of your content and create a better user experience for website visitors. Also, remember to include relevant keywords in each heading of your construction management website.</span></p>
<h5>Optimize your website structure</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Use a clear and logical structure with a hierarchy of pages and sub-pages. That makes it easier for search engines to crawl and index your content and helps users find what they&#8217;re looking for.</span></p>
<h5>Pay close attention to internal linking</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Using internal links can help you distribute link equity (the value passed through links from one webpage to another) throughout your website. That&#8217;s important for improving your website&#8217;s overall authority and ranking in search engines. But by placing the right link in the right place, you can provide valuable resources to website visitors and make them explore your content for longer. And having the right amount of internal links will also help search engines discover and index new pages on your website faster.</span></p>
<h3 id="mobile-friendly"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Mobile-Friendly Construction Website Design Provides Better User Experience</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">According to </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://www.statista.com/statistics/277125/share-of-website-traffic-coming-from-mobile-devices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Statista</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">, in Q2 of 2022, 58.9% of all website traffic worldwide was generated through mobile phones. This trend is expected to continue in the coming years, so it&#8217;s important to ensure that your website is optimized for small screens. Also, mobile users often have different needs and limited time to browse your website. And since Google started mobile-first indexing, having a mobile-friendly website is essential for SEO. So what should you do?</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">There are several key considerations to keep in mind when designing a mobile-friendly construction website:</span></p>
<h5>Use responsive design</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Responsive design ensures that your website automatically adjusts its layout and content body width to fit the screen size of the user&#8217;s device. That is crucial because potential clients may access your website from various devices, including smartphones, tablets, and laptops. Don&#8217;t assume that clients only browse for construction services while using desktop computers at their offices.</span></p>
<h5>Keep it simple</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A mobile-friendly construction website should have a clean, uncluttered design with easy-to-read text and clear calls to action. Use only a few large images or videos, as these can slow down the loading time of your website on mobile devices and diminish readability.</span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/constructionmobilefriendly.png" alt="example of mobile-friendly construction website" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h5>Use larger buttons and links</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Think with your thumbs when creating mobile-friendly web designs. Large buttons and links that are easy to tap with a finger will make the navigation smoother and create a better user experience.</span></p>
<h5>Optimize for load time</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Mobile users are often on the go and may not always have access to fast, stable internet connections. To ensure that your website loads quickly, optimize your images and other media, and consider using a content delivery network (CDN) to deliver your content more efficiently.</span></p>
<h5>Make it easy to contact you</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Construction clients may want to get in touch with you while they are out on the job, so make it easy for them to contact you by including your phone number and email address prominently on your website. Also, simplify all the forms you require users to fill by reducing the number of fields and enabling auto-fill options.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">By following these guidelines, you can create a mobile-friendly construction website that is easy to use and provides a great experience for your visitors.</span></p>
<h3 id="color"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Appropriate Color Palette Can Help You Evoke Desired Emotions</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Color can play a significant role in how a website is perceived by visitors. Different colors evoke different emotions and associations, so it&#8217;s essential to choose the ones that accurately reflect your company&#8217;s values. Also, by using an appropriate color palette and experimenting with contrast, you can highlight important elements of the website, such as CTA buttons or key messages. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Here are some of the best tips for choosing a color palette for construction website design:</span></p>
<h5>Consider the brand identity</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If your company has a specific color scheme that is already established, incorporate those colors into your web design. That will help you create a cohesive brand identity and make your construction website easily recognizable.</span></p>
<h5>Think about the target audience</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Colors on your website need to be visually appealing to your target audience. For those brands that target a younger audience, bold, vibrant colors are a good choice. However, as construction companies usually target a more professional audience, consider using more muted, subtle colors.</span></p>
<h5>Choose colors that are relevant to the construction industry</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Construction is often associated with specific colors, such as yellow, orange, green, black, red, and blue. These colors can help you evoke senses of trust, reliability, strength, durability, and similar. And by using colors that are relevant to your industry, you can create a sense of familiarity.</span></p>
<h5>Consider using a color scheme tool</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">There are many online tools that can help you choose a color scheme for your website. Tools such as </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://coolors.co/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Coolors </span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">allow you to input a base color and generate a palette based on that color. This way, you can find colors that complement each other and create a cohesive look. </span></p>
<h5>Test your color palette</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Once you have chosen a color palette, make sure to test it to see whether it looks good on the web. Check how your colors look on different devices and in different lighting conditions. That will allow you to fine-tune your palette and ensure it looks great on all website visitors&#8217; devices.</span></p>
<h2 id="elements"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Essential Elements of Construction Web Design</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Now let&#8217;s explore more elements that can help you ensure that your construction web design effectively communicates the company&#8217;s brand, values, and offerings:</span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A Powerful Hero Section That Hooks Potential Clients</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A hero section is a prominent area on the homepage of a website that you can use to showcase the company&#8217;s key services or products and hook website visitors to keep exploring. As it&#8217;s typically the first thing visitors see when they land on your website, the hero section gives you an opportunity to make an excellent first impression.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Here are some specific reasons why the hero section is important for a construction website design:</span></p>
<h5>It showcases the company&#8217;s key services or products</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The hero section is a prime spot to highlight the main services or products that your construction company offers. This way, you&#8217;ll immediately show visitors what your company does and what sets it apart from competitors.</span></p>
<h5>It sets the tone for the rest of the website</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The hero section sets the tone for the rest of the website, so it&#8217;s essential to get it right. Use colors, fonts, and images that are consistent with your brand guidelines and that convey the desired mood and message.</span></p>
<h5>It helps visitors quickly understand what the website is about</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Your hero section should clearly communicate the purpose of the website and what potential clients can expect to find there. That will help them quickly understand whether your construction company website is relevant to their needs.</span></p>
<h5>It can include a call-to-action</h5>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t hesitate to include a call-to-action (CTA) button in the hero section of your website. This way, you can encourage newcomers to take action quickly and engage with your website further. Having visible CTA buttons will help you improve conversion rates.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Overall, the hero section is a crucial element of a construction website design. You can use it to quickly and effectively convey the main message and engage website visitors. Before doing any design work, take your time and check our </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/website-hero-ideas" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">website hero ideas</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> that might inspire you.</span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Project Galleries and Testimonials For Building Trust</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Project galleries and client testimonials are one of the most powerful ways to provide construction website visitors with visual and written evidence of your company&#8217;s expertise. This element will help potential clients understand the capabilities and quality of your work, which is crucial for establishing trust and credibility.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Project galleries allow potential clients to see the scope and style of the company&#8217;s past projects. Make sure to showcase the level of detail and craftsmanship that goes into your work. These galleries are particularly useful for clients who need help with similar projects.</span></p>
<h4><span data-preserver-spaces="true">3 ways to implement project galleries in your construction website design</span></h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">There are several ways to implement project galleries in your construction website design, including:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Creating a dedicated page for the project gallery: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This is a common approach, where you create a separate page on the construction company website specifically for showcasing the company&#8217;s past projects. This page can include a grid of project images, a slideshow of images, and brief descriptions of each project.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Integrating the project gallery into the homepage or other main pages: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Depending on the layout and design of your boutique construction firm&#8217;s website, you may choose to feature a selection of project images on the homepage or service pages. That can be an excellent way to showcase your work and capabilities more prominently.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Using a third-party portfolio platform: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Several online platforms allow you to create and manage a portfolio of your projects, such as Behance or Dribbble. You can then embed a link to your portfolio on your construction company website and allow website visitors to view your projects in more detail.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">And why do you need client testimonials? People usually seek social proof before buying a product or hiring service providers. No matter how truthful your website copy is, chances are that potential clients will trust your previous customers more than you. Client testimonials can provide valuable insights into your company&#8217;s communication style, professionalism level, and overall customer satisfaction. You&#8217;ll build trust and credibility with potential clients by providing third-party validation of your company&#8217;s work.</span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A Blog will Help You Educate Your Audience and Earn Credibility</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Blogs are an important part of construction company websites for several reasons:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Sharing expertise and industry knowledge: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A blog allows you to share valuable information and insights about the construction industry with potential customers and clients. This way, you can establish your company as a thought leader and trusted source of information.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Showcasing completed projects: </span></strong>A<strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Blog is a great place to highlight the company&#8217;s capabilities and showcase completed projects. </span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">SEO benefits: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">There are not many better ways to expand the number of keywords your website ranks for in search engines than regularly publishing high-quality articles on your blog. By posting relevant and informative content, you can attract more traffic from search engines and gradually turn them into paying clients.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Engaging with customers and clients: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You can allow clients to leave comments and feedback on your blog posts. That will help you build relationships with customers and gather valuable insights about their needs and preferences.</span></li>
</ul>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Service pages will Help You Demonstrate Your Expertise</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Service pages provide information about the specific services that your company offers. These pages allow potential clients to learn more about what the company can do for them. There are a few key steps that you can follow when creating service pages during your construction website design project:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Identify the services the company offers: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Start by making a list of the services your construction company offers. Consider including information about the types of projects that you&#8217;ve completed in the past, as well as any specialized services or expertise you have.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Create a page for each service: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Create a separate page on your website for each service you offer. That will allow you to provide detailed information and make it easier for potential clients to find precisely what they need.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Write compelling content: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Use clear, concise language to describe each service and its features and benefits. Include details about the process for completing projects and any unique features or qualifications your company has.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Use images and videos: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">In addition to text, consider including images and videos on your service pages. These can help illustrate the services you offer and give potential clients a better sense of what to expect when working with your company.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Include CTAs: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">On each service page, include a call to action that encourages potential clients to get in touch with your construction company. That could be a contact form, a phone number, or a link to a &#8220;Request a quote&#8221; page.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">In addition to providing valuable information for potential clients, service pages can also help construction companies rank higher in search engine results and attract more website traffic. You can improve your visibility and reach a wider audience by including relevant keywords.</span></p>
