<h2 id="mobile"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">How to make a Canva website mobile-friendly?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">By using Canva for website design, you can easily create mobile-friendly websites. The crucial part is selecting the right options in the menu that appears after you click on the “Publish Website” button. You’ll see a box next to the “Resize on mobile” text; make sure to tick it. Just below, there is a dropdown menu containing two options – “Without navigation” and “With navigation.” Select the second one. That should be it; your website will be mobile-friendly upon publishing. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">However, if you’re still unsatisfied with the overall look and feel of your Canva website on mobile devices, you might need to redesign certain elements. Consider slightly changing the layout, button sizes, and placement, the way images are cropped, and similar. To prevent these problems, you can focus on a mobile-first approach when using Canva for website design.</span></p>
<h2 id="blog"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Can you create a blog with Canva?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you plan on using Canva for website design, you might be wondering whether this platform allows you to create a blog. Running a blog on your business website is an excellent way to engage with your customers and establish your company as an industry leader. It seems like Canva’s team was well aware of this before entering the website builder market. That’s why they enabled users to easily create Canva websites that support blogging options. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Creating a blog on this website design platform is as simple as choosing the website Canva template that resonates with your style preferences and then using drag-and-drop tools to customize details. Here is how to find blog templates for your future Canva website:</span></p>
<ol>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">When on Canva’s homepage, navigate to the </span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Design Spotlight</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> dropdown menu</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Click on the </span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Websites</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> item in the menu list</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Scroll a bit to find the </span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Browse all templates</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> button</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">From there, you’ll be able to find </span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Blog Website templates</span></strong></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Choose the template you want to start editing</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">An even simpler option is to utilize the internal search feature and type in “Blog website.” Canva should then provide you with more than 30 templates and an option to create a blank blog website. Keep in mind that you’ll need to log in to your Canva account in order to start customizing templates and save them later on. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">However, keep in mind that running a blog on the Canva website is not as easy and effective as running one on the WordPress website. Instead of entirely relying on your content marketing strategy on your Canva website, create a visually appealing, one-page Canva website design that supports a very specific goal, such as promoting a new product. You can then link to your new Canva website from WordPress blog articles.</span></p>
