<h2 id="ux-research"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Why Does Your Business Need To Conduct UX Research?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Exploring the best UX research tools wouldn&#8217;t make much sense without clarifying what UX research is and how it can help your business.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you decide to start a </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/website-creation-process" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">website creation process</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> without conducting user research, you&#8217;ll leave dozens of important questions unanswered. Despite having a basic idea of your target audience&#8217;s preferences, you&#8217;ll lack knowledge of their specific pain points, unique expectations, favorite features on competitors&#8217; websites, and much more. As a result, you might design a website full of experience gaps &#8211; the one your target audience won&#8217;t enjoy as much as expected.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">To prevent this from happening, UX professionals emphasized the user research process. It&#8217;s their job to minimize the need for pure &#8220;guessing&#8221; in the UX design process. By utilizing the proper user research methods and techniques, you can provide your development and design teams with valuable information they can use to boost the quality of their work. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">UX design is a broad field, and as a business owner, you should understand all the differences between </span>UX researchers vs UX designers<span data-preserver-spaces="true">. This way, you&#8217;ll be able to hire the right people in your team, the ones who will be able to make full use of the various user experience research tools you&#8217;re about to discover.</span></p>
<h2 id="tasks"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Different Tasks User Research Tools Can Help You With</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You&#8217;ll need to perform various tasks to conduct successful user experience research and gather valuable data. Knowing which tasks such research consists of is essential for understanding different UX research tool categories. So let&#8217;s quickly explore them:</span></p>
<h3>User interviews:</h3>
<p>Asking the right <a href="/user-experience-survey-questions">user experience survey questions</a> is a great way to gather qualitative user feedback. However, keeping track of all the information you gather through user research interviews can take time and effort. That&#8217;s where UX research tools come in handy. These tools can make your life easier when preparing and executing user interviews. Some of the UX tools we&#8217;ll show you can help you with all the interview preparation needs, making user interview recordings and transcriptions, organizing insights, and much more.</p>
<h3>UX surveys:</h3>
<p>User researchers often conduct surveys to collect quantitative data. Luckily, you can use many great UX survey tools to create and distribute your surveys and then automatically collect and analyze the responses. You&#8217;ll save lots of time compared to manually compiling the data.</p>
<h3>Card sorting:</h3>
<p>Card sorting is a method where participants organize items into categories. You can use it to better understand under which category they expect to find a specific product. Various UX research tools can help you conduct card sorting tests online. And what&#8217;s best, these tools also have features that allow you to analyze the results quickly.</p>
<h3>Tree testing:</h3>
<p>UX researchers use tree testing to evaluate the navigation of their websites. When conducting this type of usability testing, you&#8217;ll give participants a series of tasks and ask them to find the correct location to complete the task. We&#8217;ll show you some of the best tree testing tools that can help you streamline this process and get accurate usability test reports.</p>
<h3>Focus groups:</h3>
<p>With this method, you&#8217;ll need to gather a group of participants so they can discuss your digital product. It&#8217;s a great way to gather various opinions and ideas quickly. However, keeping track of all the information participants share can be challenging. Luckily, some tools can help you recruit the right participants and analyze their conversations quickly and efficiently.</p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/UX-research-tools-benefits.png" alt="5 Benefits of using UX research tools for your projects." width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h2 id="benefits"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Must-Know Benefits of Using UX Research Tools</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">When it comes to </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/creating-ux-strategy" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">creating a UX strategy</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> and making it work, using UX research tools can benefit you in various ways:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Gain deep insights into user behavior: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">One of the key benefits of using UX research tools is gaining insights into user behavior. Using tools like heat maps, click tracking, eye movement tracking, and session recording, you can better understand how people interact with your website or app. For example, heat maps can show you which parts of a page get the most attention from users, while session recordings can reveal where users are getting stuck or frustrated.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Save time and money: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Using the right UX research tools will save you a lot of time and money in the long run. These tools can help you identify areas for improvement early on to avoid costly redesigns down the road. And by utilizing some of the best feedback tools, you can avoid spending time and resources on designs that don&#8217;t work well for your users.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Validate design decisions: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Do you have several fabulous ideas for your web design but need help deciding which one to choose? By using A/B testing UX research tools, you can test those versions with real users to find the one that performs best. This can help you decide which design elements to keep and which to change. </span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Boost conversion rates &#8211; </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Ultimately, the goal of UX research is to help you meet various <a href="/user-requirements-for-a-website-design">user requirements for a website design</a> to improve user satisfaction. Once you gain insights into user behavior and validate design decisions, you&#8217;ll have a much easier time creating a website that converts leads into loyal customers.</span></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="find"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A Simple Way To Find The Best User Research Software For Your UX Projects</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Before you start exploring some of the best UX research tools we&#8217;ve prepared, carefully read this list of UX research methods:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Quantitative UX research: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A data-driven method you&#8217;ll use to collect and analyze numerical data, such as statistics and metrics. UX surveys and questionnaires will be your best friend for collecting large amounts of data from a representative sample of users. For example, you can use quantitative UX research to determine how many users are satisfied with your website&#8217;s navigation.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Qualitative UX research: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you want to better understand users&#8217; experiences, motivations, and emotions, then make sure to utilize qualitative UX research methods. Qualitative research is more subjective and relies on gathering insights through user interviews, observation, and user testing. For example, you can use qualitative UX research to understand why users are struggling with a particular feature or to identify opportunities for improvement based on user feedback. Or you can use it to find out how people feel about how you&#8217;ve implemented </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/typography-in-ux-design" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">typography in UX design</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Moderated UX research: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">With moderated UX research, UX researchers observe participants in real time &#8211; in person or remotely. The moderator guides the user through a series of tasks while observing and asking questions on the go. For example, you can use moderated UX research to gather immediate user feedback and learn how they feel while navigating your site.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Unmoderated UX research: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Unmoderated research is conducted remotely without the presence of a researcher. You&#8217;ll give users a set of tasks to complete and then record their interactions for later analysis. To make this work, you&#8217;ll need specialized UX research software to collect user behavior data without observing them in real time.</span></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="best-tools"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">7 Best UX Research Tools in 2023</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It&#8217;s finally time to start exploring the list of the seven best tools for UX research. These tools are designed to make the research process faster, easier, and more accurate, so you can create websites that truly meet your users&#8217; needs. From online surveys to user testing platforms, our <a href="/web-design-agency-chicago">web design agency in Chicago</a> has tested dozens of tools, and here are our favorites:</span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Userbrain-logo.png" alt="" width="800" height="205" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3 id="userbrain"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Userbrain</span></h3>
<p><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://www.userbrain.com/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Userbrain </span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">is one of the best tools for UX research you can use to check the quality of your UX design. The fact that UX researchers from popular companies like Spotify, Wish, Amazon, and AirBnB use this ser research tool tells enough about its quality.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The platform works by recruiting users from around the world who match the demographics of your target audience. But if you want to avoid recruiting users from this platform&#8217;s pool, you can invite your own testers. With Userbrain, you can test anything and collect user feedback in voice-over video form.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You can use dozens of preset templates for your user research, so it takes just a couple of minutes to get started. We also love the feature that allows you to schedule regular usability testing.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Userbrain comes with flexible pricing:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Starter plan &#8211; $90 per month or $990 per year: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">With this plan, you get three testers each month and can have up to ten sessions with your own testers. The Starter plan also includes one year of video storage for recorded sessions and testing automation features.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Pro plan &#8211; $299 per month or $2990 per year: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You get ten testers each month, and you can have a maximum of 30 sessions with testers that you invite. The Pro plan opens space for two additional admins and a few more benefits.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Agency plan &#8211; $799 per month or $7990 per year: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You&#8217;ll get 30 testers each month and the ability to run 90 sessions with your own testers. With the Agency plan, you also get a dedicated account manager.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Pay As You Go &#8211; $39 per tester: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A flexible model that is handy when working with a tight budget. Userbrain will store your video recordings for three months, which is quite enough time to gather insights.</span></li>
</ul>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/UserTesting-logo.png" alt="" width="800" height="205" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3 id="usertesting"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">UserTesting</span></h3>
<p><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://www.usertesting.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">UserTesting</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> is another powerful UX research platform that can help you with various user research methods. It comes with a wide range of features and three main products you can combine to conduct just any type of user research and </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/market-research-for-website-design" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">market research for website design</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Insight Core</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Product Insight</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Marketing Insight</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Flexibility is one of the most significant advantages of UserTesting. You can use it to test various designs, from wireframes and prototypes to fully functional products. Depending on your needs, you can also choose between moderated and unmoderated testing. This UX research platform lets you speak directly to your testers and focus groups. You can also conduct 1:1 user interviews and gather real-time user feedback.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It also comes with an easy-to-use dashboard you can integrate with other tools. You&#8217;ll be able to quickly analyze your data and use it to enhance your UX design.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Prices are fully customizable, and all plans come with a free trial you can request. If you&#8217;re running a non-profit organization, you can get full access to UserTesting for free.</span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/UsabilityHub-logo.png" alt="" width="800" height="205" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3 id="usabilityhub"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">UsabilityHub</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">As one of the best usability testing tools available, </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://usabilityhub.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">UsabilityHub</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> can help you test your design prototypes, website, and mobile app usability quickly and easily. It comes with a variety of features, including:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Card sorting: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This helps you find out how to organize content in a way your visitors want.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Prototype testing: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You can import your prototypes from Figma and get user feedback quickly.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Design surveys: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">UsabilityHub&#8217;s UX survey tools can help you get all the necessary answers and empower your UX process with accurate user feedback.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Five-second tests: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This feature helps you measure people&#8217;s first impressions about your landing pages, so you can optimize them to achieve higher conversion rates.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Preference tests: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you have multiple design solutions ready but are unsure which to use, ask users, and you&#8217;ll quickly find the path.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">First-click tests: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This user research software can help you polish the hierarchy of your content and put essential page elements into the spotlight.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Now let&#8217;s check UsabilityHub&#8217;s pricing plans:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">There is a Free plan available</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">$75 per month for the Basic plan</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">$175 for the Pro plan</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Custom price for the Enterprise plan</span></li>
</ul>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Loop-11-logo.png" alt="" width="800" height="205" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3 id="loop-11"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Loop 11</span></h3>
<p><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://www.loop11.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Loop 11</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> is a cloud-based platform that lets you design and run different usability tests, analyze the results and make data-driven decisions to optimize your user experience. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">What we love about Loop 11 is that it&#8217;s easy to use, even for people without a lot of UX research experience.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Another significant advantage of Loop 11 is its scalability. Whether you&#8217;re running a small usability test with just a handful of participants or a large-scale study with hundreds or thousands of users, Loop 11 can handle it all. You can customize your tests to fit your specific needs, from demographic targeting to task scenarios, and you can run multiple tests simultaneously to save time and resources.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This tool has advanced features to help you get the most out of your research. Here are just some:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Information architecture testing: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This helps you gather insights you need to improve the information architecture on your website.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Search engine findability: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This allows you to measure how easily people can find your website or specific pages through search engines.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Mobile &amp; tablet testing:</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> Loop 11 helps you conduct usability testing on various devices and screen sizes.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A/B usability testing: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Not sure which of your designs will perform best with real users? With Loop 11, you can conduct A/B tests to find out quickly. </span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">True intent studies: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This feature allows you to gain insights into actual goals people have when visiting your website and how easy it is for them to achieve those goals.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Prototype testing: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Save time and money by testing your wireframes and prototypes before you start the development phase.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Benchmarking: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Find out how your website stands compared to your competitors.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Loop 11 pricing</span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">$179 p/m for Rapid Insights</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">$358 p/m for Pro</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">$533 p/m for Enterprise</span></li>
</ul>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/hotjar-logo.png" alt="" width="800" height="205" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3 id="hotjar"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Hotjar</span></h3>
<p><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://www.hotjar.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Hotjar </span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">is one of the most popular UX research software among industry experts. Here are some of the features that make Hotjar a hot choice:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Heatmaps: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Heatmap tool makes Hotjar stand out. You can check where users click, scroll, and hover on your website or app. This way, you&#8217;ll be able to identify which areas of your site or app are most engaging and which areas users tend to ignore. Learning these patterns lets you polish your UX projects and craft more enjoyable experiences.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Session recordings: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You can record usability tests and playback videos of users&#8217; interactions with your website. It will help you identify user frustrations and discover bugs or usability issues, which is crucial for creating a more accessible user experience.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Conversion funnel analysis tool:</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> With this Hotjar&#8217;s feature, you can identify where users drop off in your sales funnel or conversion process. By understanding where users leave your site or app, you can optimize those areas to increase conversion rates and revenue.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Hotjar&#8217;s pricing is customizable, and it all comes down to your needs and preferences. You can opt for pre-made monthly plans ranging from $0 to $80 or pick a custom package.</span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Optimal-Workshop-logo.png" alt="" width="800" height="205" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3 id="optimal-workshop"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Optimal Workshop</span></h3>
<p><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://www.optimalworkshop.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Optimal Workshop</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> is more than a regular UX research tool, as it has many valuable tools for various tasks and research methods. You can also use it as a participant recruitment engine.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">With this user research software, you can check responses in real-time. And it also has impressive data visualization features that allow UX researchers to share their insights with others.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Optimal Workshop consists of 5 high-quality tools:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">OptimalSort: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A card sorting tool you can use to gain insights into how users expect you to organize categories on your website or app. You&#8217;ll find a lot of value in it if you&#8217;re trying to organize information on your website in a user-friendly way.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Treejack: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A tree testing tool you can use to find out if people can easily find the desired information on your website. With this tool, you&#8217;ll also be able to identify potential obstacles so you can polish your UX design.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Chalkmark: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you have a design ready, and want to test it with users, then this first-click testing tool will show how well people understand your interfaces. You&#8217;ll find out where people expect to find the information they&#8217;re looking for, so you can polish your UX design. You can conduct such tests by uploading screenshots, prototypes, or wireframes.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Questions: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">An excellent tool for conducting online surveys. It allows you to upload your wireframes to gather more specific user feedback. This tool can help you find the right question types for your surveys. And it supports more than 80 languages.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Reframer: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you&#8217;re looking for a user research tool to help you organize all your insights from qualitative research, Reframer is the answer.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Optimal Workshop pricing</span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Free plan</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">$166 p/m for Pro</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">$153 for each user p/m for Team</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Custom price for Enterprise</span></li>
</ul>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Typeform-logo.png" alt="" width="800" height="205" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3 id="typeform"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Typeform</span></h3>
<p><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://www.typeform.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Typeform </span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">is one of the best UX survey tools that can help you create surveys and collect responses from your audience in a user-friendly and engaging way. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">One of the main features of Typeform is its customizable and visually appealing survey templates. Typeform surveys are designed to look and feel like a conversation, which makes them engaging and enjoyable for respondents. This can help you achieve higher completion rates and gain more valuable insights.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Here are some of the critical features Typeform offers:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A range of question types you can use to collect different types of data, including text responses, multiple choice answers, ratings, and more</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Ability to add images, videos, and other multimedia to make your surveys even more interactive and engaging</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Advanced data analysis capabilities and built-in analytics tools</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Data visualization tools that will help you identify patterns and trends in your respondent&#8217;s answers</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Ability to export your data to other tools like Excel, Google Sheets, and more</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Considering all the features it comes with, Typeform offers valuable deals:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">$25 per month for the Basic Plan</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">$50 per month for the Plus Plan</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">$83 per month for the Business Plan</span></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="final-thoughts"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Final Thoughts on UX Research Tools</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">That&#8217;s it; we&#8217;ve just explored the best UX research tools in 2023. With these 7 UX tools, you&#8217;ll be well on your way to conducting high-quality research that will help you improve your digital products and boost customer loyalty. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Also, if you need to decide which one to try first, consider the specific needs and goals you want to accomplish. This may help you narrow your options and find user research tools to elevate your UX design.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">To find other exciting tools that can help you thrive in the digital space, you can check our </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/category/app" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">app blog section</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">.</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/UX-research-tools.png',NULL,'[]','[166,357]','2023-03-31T11:00:59','2023-03-31T11:00:59',3225,9,9);
