  (19242,'/ux-researcher-vs-ux-designer','ux-researcher-vs-ux-designer','post','blog','UX Researcher Vs UX Designer: Differences Might Surprise You','UX Researcher Vs UX Designer - Alpha Efficiency','Understanding differences between UX researcher vs UX designer will help you choose the career path you''re going to enjoy the most.','https://alphaefficiency.com/ux-researcher-vs-ux-designer',1,'Are you interested in pursuing a career in the world of UX? Great choice! But before you dive in, it&#8217;s crucial to understand the difference between two critical roles that often get mixed up &#8211; UX researcher vs UX designer. These two job titles may sound similar, but they&#8217;re distinct career paths requiring different skill &hellip; Continued','<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Are you interested in pursuing a career in the world of UX? Great choice! But before you dive in, it&#8217;s crucial to understand the difference between two critical roles that often get mixed up &#8211; UX researcher vs UX designer. These two job titles may sound similar, but they&#8217;re <strong>distinct career paths requiring different skill sets, responsibilities, and personalities</strong>.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">To help you choose the right career path, our </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">digital marketing agency</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> will explore the UX researcher vs UX designer topic in detail in this article. You&#8217;ll learn where these two roles fit into the design process, the salary range for both positions, which skills to demonstrate with your UX portfolio, and much more. But before you continue reading, please understand that both UX roles are great choices. We&#8217;ll try to explain the difference between UX research and UX design to help you set your foot in the right direction and get a job that you&#8217;ll enjoy. Now, let&#8217;s start!</span></p>
<h5><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Table of Contents:</span></h5>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#difference"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">What&#8217;s the Difference between UX Research and UX Design?</span></a></li>
