<h3 id="seo-vs-ppc"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">SEO Vs. PPC &#8211; How to allocate your budget as a healthcare professional?</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">SEO and PPC are both essential strategies in digital marketing for doctors. However, they serve different purposes and bring different benefits.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">SEO is a long-term investment. It takes time to see the results. But once your website starts ranking high on search results, you&#8217;ll reap the benefits without paying for each click.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">On the other hand, PPC provides immediate results. It immediately puts your ads in front of your target audience. This is particularly beneficial when you&#8217;re just starting and need to attract patients quickly. </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="https://www.wordstream.com/blog/ws/2019/08/19/conversion-rate-benchmarks" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Statistics </span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">suggest that the average PPC conversion rate was 4.6% in search engines and 0.75% on the display network. As long as you&#8217;re seeing a return on your investment, you should keep investing in PPC.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">But as your SEO efforts start to pay off, you&#8217;ll gradually depend less on PPC for patient acquisition. And another strong reason to invest in SEO even before launching your website is that as you optimize your website for search engines, you&#8217;re simultaneously optimizing it for end-users too.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you&#8217;re still unsure about where to invest more, you may want to read my comprehensive guide on </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/seo-vs-google-ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">SEO vs Google Ads</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">.</span></p>
<h3 id="social-media-marketing-investment"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">How much should doctors invest in social media marketing?</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The cost of social media marketing for doctors can vary widely, depending on several factors:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The number of platforms you decide to use: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">With many social media platforms available, it might be tempting to try and win an audience on each one. But the more platforms you&#8217;re active on, the more resources you&#8217;ll need to create and post content consistently across all of them. Responding to every patient and analyzing patient behavior on each platform will also take more time. If budget is a concern, it&#8217;s better to be active and consistent on one or two platforms rather than spreading yourself thin across many.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The number of posts and unique images: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Although publishing posts on social media is free, creating engaging content isn&#8217;t. You&#8217;ll need text, images, videos, infographics, and more. Depending on the complexity and volume of content needed, you may need to hire a professional content creator or designer, adding to your cost.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Boosting posts: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Organic reach on social media is great, but sometimes, you need to boost your posts to reach a larger audience. Paid promotions or boosting posts can increase visibility, but they add to your expenses.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While social media marketing for doctors is a goldmine of opportunity, I strongly advise against allocating most of your budget to it &#8211; especially if you don&#8217;t have a loyal patient base you can engage with yet. PPC and SEO will get you more new patients who are actively searching for your services.</span></p>
<h2 id="get-started"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The Best Way To Get Started With Digital Marketing For Doctors</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">As a healthcare professional, your expertise lies in working with patients rather than in digital marketing. While you could attempt to learn and handle all these strategies on your own, the learning curve is steep, and mistakes can be costly. Therefore, the best way to get started with digital marketing for doctors is to hire digital marketing experts.</span></p>
