<h2 id="transformation">1st, I was Shitposting, and then Twitter Completely Transformed My Life&#8230;</h2>
<p>I only wanted to have fun, but then this happened&#8230;</p>
<p>I got <strong>ADDICTED</strong>. Being somewhat introverted as a person and a big computer nerd, I thoroughly enjoy mangling text.</p>
<p>It struck me that Twitter was this big multiplayer online game where you needed to collect account followers, and that&#8217;s all that mattered. I&#8217;ve invested tons of time to learn how to write tweets that drive growth.</p>
<p>I grew two accounts above 20 000 followers. My personal account: Brian Dordevic, grew to 55 000 followers. This growth helped me generate over $250 000 in revenue through Twitter, and it helped me solidify my position as a web designer. I got tons of clients for my <a href="/">web design agency</a>, established authority, got invited to podcasts, and received free software services. The flywheel that Twitter creates is absolutely bananas, and the only thing that got me more value than Twitter is the SEO consulting that I&#8217;ve provided for more than a decade.</p>
<p>If you decide that you need my help, you could fill out this form and <a href="/#contact">request a proposal from Alpha Efficiency</a> for <strong>Twitter Ghostwriting services</strong>.</p>
