<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It&#8217;s actually easy to get back on track. Once you realize how the whole perspective on web analytics has changed with Google Analytics 4, you&#8217;ll prefer the GA4 engagement rate metric to the bounce rate (which is now in GA4 too).</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">By effectively using the engagement rate in GA4, you can optimize traffic quality, find the most profitable traffic sources for your content, and maximize user satisfaction. Throughout this article, I&#8217;ll help you with that. You&#8217;ll <strong>learn the best ways to use engagement rate in GA4 as a marketer</strong>, so you can earn the team&#8217;s trust and boost your career.</span></p>
