<h2 id="professional-work"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Should you even use Elementor for professional work?</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">When discussing professional web development, the debate between </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/custom-coded-websites" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">custom coded websites</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> and using a page builder like Elementor is inevitable.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It’s important to stay realistic.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Custom coding still holds the upper hand in creating highly specialized, complex websites. But websites built from scratch are expensive and take</span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> 4-6 months to complete</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">For a significant number of projects, Elementor Pro is more than sufficient. And you can build high-quality websites </span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">with Elementor within 2-4 weeks</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While my agency, </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Alpha Efficiency</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">, is still far from solely relying on Elementor Pro, we did incorporate it into our toolset. We offer it as a solution to clients who require speedy delivery along with other benefits of using this platform.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Elementor has been evolving in a positive direction in recent years, making the gap between traditional coding and page builders smaller than ever before.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">So, if you’re wondering whether you should even use Elementor as a professional, I’d advise you to experiment with this platform.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you’re satisfied with the quality of the websites you can create, then there’s no reason not to use Elementor for specific projects. Find the right balance and always communicate with your clients to learn about their needs.</span></p>
<h2 id="free-vs-pro"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Elementor Free is solid, but I’ll never go back to it after upgrading to Elementor Pro</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">So, using Elementor is acceptable and sometimes even beneficial for professional web designers. But now there’s another challenge – deciding between Elementor Free vs Pro.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The free version of Elementor is, unlikely most other WordPress page builders, not restricted. You’ll get all the essential tools you need to build a website. You can also use over 30 free widgets and a few templates.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you don’t work on complex web design projects and you find free widgets enough to achieve the desired functionality, using Elementor Free might be a good option. The absence of some advanced features might make you feel less overwhelmed.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">But if you seek more than the free version has to offer – I recommend checking out Elementor Pro.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">In upcoming sections, I’ll show you additional features you can unlock with the paid version so you can decide is Elementor Pro worth it.</span></p>
<h2 id="features"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Elementor Pro Features that make it a better choice in professional environments</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">When I first decided to test Elementor for my agency, we went for a free version. The results were solid. However, we found specific limitations that Elementor Pro promised to solve.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Here’s a breakdown of Elementor Pro features you can expect to get upon subscribing. These features will increase the flexibility of this page builder, help you finish designs faster, and allow you to provide an additional level of functionality to end users.</span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Elementor Pro Widgets help you expand website functionality without developing custom plugins</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While the free version gives you access to 30 widgets, with Elementor Pro, you unlock plenty of other widgets to enhance your website’s functionality. This is a considerable advantage, especially when working under tight deadlines or with limited resources. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Some of the notable Elementor Pro widgets include:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Posts widget (for customizing your post layouts)</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Share buttons</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Form Builder – it speeds up the process of </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/form-ui-design" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">form UI design</span></a></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Gallery</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Countdown</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Table of content</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">CTA</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Mega menu</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Facebook Embed</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Progress tracker</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Testimonial carousel</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Price Table &amp; Price List</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Lottie Widget (for animations)</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Elementor Pro’s array of widgets effectively eliminates the need to develop custom plugins or purchase third-party ones. They empower you to add almost any feature to a website, simplifying the design process while delivering high-quality, functional websites to your clients. Pair them up with </span><a href="/essential-addons-for-elementor">essential addons for Elementor</a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">, and you’ll be able to improve website functionalities further.</span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Gain more control over your designs with Elementor Pro Theme Builder</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Elementor Pro’s Theme Builder functionality is a step up from the free version, especially if you highly value design control. It removes the need for a premium theme, allowing you to tweak all parts of your site directly in Elementor.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The real benefit here is customization. You can design headers, footers, single posts, archives, and even specialized pages like 404s and search results. This level of control wasn’t possible with the free version, where you’re often stuck with your theme’s limits.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">What makes the Theme Builder practical is its use of dynamic content. You can set up a design for one post, and it applies to all similar content. This saves time and allows you to achieve design consistency with less manual work.</span></p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Popup-Builder-WordPress.png" alt="Popup Builder WordPress" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Elementor Pro gives you access to a highly-customizable Popup Builder</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If you’ve ever struggled with adding popups to a website (without custom coding), you know the drill. You find a separate popup plugin, install it, and then watch as your carefully optimized </span><a href="/elementor-page-speed">Elementor page speed</a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> takes a hit.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Elementor Pro addresses this issue head-on by incorporating a Popup Builder directly within its interface. I was positively surprised by the level of customization Elementor Popup Builder provides.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The tool also comes with a variety of trigger and targeting rules. You have options like time delays, scroll depth, and exit intent triggers. These ensure that your popups appear at the right moment, increasing engagement without being intrusive.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">You can set a popup to appear when a visitor is about to leave the site (exit intent) or after they’ve scrolled through a certain percentage of a page. You can also target specific pages or user behaviors, making your popups more relevant and less annoying.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Moreover, with Elementor Pro, you can decide how your popups will display. You can decide whether you want popups to display in fullscreen, with a slide-in effect, or to subtly appear at the bottom of a screen.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">I found combining Elementor Popup Builder with Form Builder particularly effective. This combination allows you to add depth to your </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/inbound-marketing-funnel" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">inbound marketing funnel</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> and generate leads more effectively. </span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Design faster – Elementor Pro unlocks a complete Template Library with over 200 layouts and 100+ website kits</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Using pre-made themes as a foundation for web design can be a huge time-saver, but the limited selection in the free version of Elementor might have left you wanting more. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Once you become an Elementor Pro user, you can access over 200 templates for various use cases.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Moreover, Elementor Pro offers 100+ exclusive website kits to its users. These are tailored for various categories, such as blog, business, education, health and wellness, and others. Website kits provide a comprehensive starting point, ensuring that you have a well-thought-out design framework to begin with.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While I prefer creating a design from scratch or performing </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/figma-to-elementor" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Figma to Elementor</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> conversion, Elementor’s Template Library and website kits can come in handy when you’re tight on deadline or run out of inspiration.</span></p>
<h3><img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Elementor-Pro-WooCommerce-Builder.png" alt="Elementor Pro WooCommerce Builder" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></h3>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Elementor WooCommerce Builder for quickly setting up profitable online stores</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The <a href="https://elementor.com/features/woocommerce-builder/">WooCommerce Builder in Elementor Pro</a> extends the functionalities of its theme builder to your WooCommerce store. So, instead of designing in WooCommerce, you can use Elementor’s familiar drag-and-drop editor to customize your product pages and shop listings fully.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Elementor Pro recently expanded its capabilities by adding dedicated widgets for the Cart, Checkout, and My Account pages. These widgets allow you to fine-tune every aspect of these crucial pages.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Elementor WooCommerce Builder is especially valuable for web designers who need to deliver high-quality eCommerce solutions quickly without compromising on the unique needs of each business.</span></p>
<h3><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Additional features that make Elementor Pro beneficial</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Elementor Pro isn’t just about core features like the Theme Builder or Popup Builder. It’s the additional, often overlooked features that round out its capabilities, making it an indispensable tool for professional web design. Here are some of the key extras that make Elementor Pro stand out:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Custom Fonts:</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> In Elementor Pro, you’re not limited to Google fonts. You can upload your custom fonts or use TypeKit fonts, giving you more freedom to maintain brand consistency across your designs. If you need help understanding the process, I wrote a guide on </span>how to add font in Elementor.</li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Action Links:</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> A unique feature that allows you to connect buttons or links directly to apps like WhatsApp, Google Calendar, or Waze. This integration creates a more interactive and functional user experience on your sites.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Custom Fields Integration:</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> If you rely on Advanced Custom Fields (ACF), Pods, or Toolset, Elementor Pro seamlessly incorporates these into your designs. This integration means you can display custom content more intuitively within your layouts.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Premium Support:</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> Pro users have access to 24/7 support. This is a huge benefit, especially when dealing with complex projects. Having expert help at your fingertips ensures that any issues with Elementor are resolved quickly, keeping your projects on track.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Custom CSS and Custom Code:</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> For those who like to get under the hood, Elementor Pro offers the ability to add custom CSS and custom code. If you’re a web design professional, this feature is actually a must-have, as it will allow you to craft unique experiences and not cut corners on </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/web-design-branding" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">web design branding</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Form Integrations:</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> Connect forms with popular email marketing platforms such as MailChimp, HubSpot, ActiveCampaign, and others, facilitating efficient lead generation and marketing efforts.</span></li>
</ul>
<h2 id="final-thoughts"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Is Elementor Pro worth it in 2024? Final thoughts by a 7-figure agency owner</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Deciding whether Elementor Pro is the right investment for your web design needs in 2024 boils down to understanding your requirements and the scale at which you operate.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The free version of Elementor is far from just a beginner’s tool; it’s a comprehensive platform in its own right, capable of handling a wide array of design tasks. It’s perfect for those who need to create straightforward, effective websites without the bells and whistles. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">However, the transition to Elementor Pro offers a noticeable shift in your design process.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It’s not just about having more features at your disposal; it’s about enhanced flexibility and control over your projects. This can be crucial in a professional environment where meeting diverse client requirements and maintaining high design standards are everyday challenges.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">But what if you’ve been relying on coding websites from scratch? </span><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Is Elementor Pro worth it, then?</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While I still hold that custom-coded websites will always have their unique place, I’ve also experienced how Elementor Pro can complement these skills, especially for projects where time is of the essence. It’s about choosing the right tool for the job, and in many cases, Elementor Pro fits the bill perfectly.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">I recommend experimenting with Elementor Pro in your workflow. Its continuous evolution and commitment to improving its features make it a tool that’s likely to become even more important in 2024 and beyond.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Whether you’re an independent designer or running a full-fledged agency, Elementor Pro has the potential to streamline your design process and elevate the quality of your work.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">That said, while Elementor Pro is a powerful builder, it won’t solve all your conversion issues.</span></p>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Many designers and developers focus on mastering technical skills and following the latest trends, but they often overlook the needle-moving knowledge that can unlock $10k or more in additional monthly revenue by creating and selling websites.</span></strong></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">That&#8217;s why I&#8217;ve prepared an interactive roadmap, <strong>Profitable Websites From Scratch</strong>.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It’s designed to teach you the essential skills that truly matter for building high-converting websites:</span></p>
<ul>
<li>Fundamentals of design.</li>
<li>Main principles of UX.</li>
<li>High-impact copywriting.</li>
<li>Light code &amp; no-code skills.</li>
<li>Offer creation.</li>
</ul>
<p>You&#8217;ll learn how to craft highly profitable digital assets and sell them to a craving market.</p>
<p><strong>Ready to start? </strong><a href="https://get.alphaefficiency.com/profitable-website-from-scratch">Order your Profitable Websites From Scratch here</a>.</p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Is-Elementor-Pro-worth-it.png',NULL,'[]','[166,353]','2024-01-10T14:20:01','2024-01-10T14:20:01',2239,9,3);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (wp_id,path,slug,type,track,title,meta_title,meta_description,canonical,robots_index,excerpt,body_html,hero_image,wp_template,tags,categories,published_at,updated_at,word_count,internal_links,image_count) VALUES
  (23097,'/ui-design-process','ui-design-process','post','blog','UI Design Process: 7 Steps Every Professional Should Master','UI Design Process: 7 Steps for Mastery | Alpha Efficiency.™','In this article, I''ll show you seven key steps to a successful UI design process you can follow to tackle every project with confidence.','https://alphaefficiency.com/ui-design-process',1,'Did you ever get stuck in the UI design process despite initial waves of creativity? I have bad news &#8211; this probably happened because you lack a structured approach to UI design. If you don&#8217;t fix this, you&#8217;ll likely get stuck again during future projects. How do I know? Because I was stuck in the &hellip; Continued','<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Did you ever get stuck in the UI design process despite initial waves of creativity?</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">I have bad news &#8211; this probably happened because you lack a structured approach to UI design. If you don&#8217;t fix this, you&#8217;ll likely get stuck again during future projects.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">How do I know? Because I was stuck in the same loop in the past.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">But then I defined a step by step UI design process for my </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/web-design-agency-chicago" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">web design agency in Chicago</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">, which we make sure to follow during every project. In this article, I&#8217;ll show you these <strong>seven steps to a successful UI design process</strong>. This results from over 15 years of experimenting and finding what truly matters for creating highly effective user interfaces.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">By the end of this guide, you&#8217;ll have a clear, structured approach to UI design. You&#8217;ll be able to<strong> tackle projects with confidence, meet client expectations, and create interfaces that users love</strong>. You&#8217;ll tackle future web design projects with confidence and be able to organize your team more effectively.</span></p>
<h5>Table of Contents:</h5>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#importance"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">There&#8217;s Much More To UI Design Than Pure Creativity</span></a></li>
<li><a href="/#steps"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">UI Design Process: 7 Steps To Creating Top-Quality User Interfaces</span></a>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#research"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 1: Conduct User Research and Define Your UI Design Goals</span></a></li>
<li><a href="/#sketches"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 2: Create Sketches &#8211; This can save you weeks of hard work</span></a></li>
<li><a href="/#wireframing"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 3: Wireframing User Interface</span></a></li>
<li><a href="/#components"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 4: Designing UI Components</span></a></li>
<li><a href="/#flows"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 5: Creating User Flows and Task Flows</span></a></li>
<li><a href="/#final-design"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 6: Crafting Pixel-Perfect UI Design</span></a></li>
<li><a href="/#prototype"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 7: Create a Prototype That Connects All Screens And Flows</span></a></li>
<li><a href="/#final-thoughts"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Final Thoughts</span></a></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/UI-design-process.png" alt="UI design process" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h2 id="importance"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">There&#8217;s Much More To UI Design Than Pure Creativity</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While creativity spark is crucial for creating beautiful web design, you still can&#8217;t afford to neglect the importance of a structured approach to the UI design process.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Often, the initial instinct is to dive straight into your design software and start churning out the visual design. It&#8217;s a natural reflex for creative minds – we see a blank canvas and itch to fill it with colors and shapes. However, this approach can be misleading. Sure, you might end up with a visually appealing user interface, but aesthetics alone don&#8217;t guarantee a successful design.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The truth is that without a clear plan, even the most stunning user interfaces can fall short. They might look good but fail to connect with end-users, leading to a frustrating experience. That&#8217;s because good design is not just about how things look but also how they work. And to ensure they work well, you need a roadmap – a series of steps that guide you from conception to completion.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">In this upcoming section, I&#8217;ll show you seven key steps </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Alpha Efficiency</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> started following after we realized that you can&#8217;t guarantee the success of the user interface design process without.</span></p>
<h2 id="steps"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">UI Design Process: 7 Steps To Creating Top-Quality User Interfaces</span></h2>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/UI-design-process-7-steps.png" alt="UI design process 7 steps" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3 id="research"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 1: Conduct User Research and Define Your UI Design Goals</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">At the very beginning of the user interface design process, you must define your target audience and try to learn as much as possible about them. If you have dedicated UX researchers within your team, then they&#8217;ll equip you with most of these insights.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Things you learn during this stage will directly impact your design decisions.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Understanding your audience&#8217;s demographics, pain points, and behavior will allow you to craft designs that hit the mark.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">But you must dig even deeper. Try to be as specific as possible.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While brainstorming sessions with your team are very helpful, conducting user interviews and using </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/ux-research-tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">UX research tools</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> allow you to deepen your insights about end users even further.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Also, don&#8217;t be afraid to send your client a long list of questions about the product itself. The more you learn, the easier it will be to connect dots later on.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Don&#8217;t move on to the next step of the UI design process before doing the following:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Define end-user persona</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Learn about the client&#8217;s selling points</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Define clear goals your UI design should accomplish</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Define the scope of the project</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Which team members will be involved in the UI UX design process</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Once you have defined </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/user-requirements-for-a-website-design" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">user requirements for website design</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> and goals your clients expect you to accomplish, you&#8217;re ready to move on to the next UI design process steps.</span></p>
<h3 id="sketches"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 2: Create Sketches &#8211; This can save you weeks of hard work</span></h3>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Creating-UI-sketches.png" alt="Creating UI sketches" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">One of the common mistakes design teams make is spending too much time on details early on in the UX UI design process.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Creating high fidelity visuals before you even agree on the layout design for your user interface is risky. You&#8217;ll rarely come up with the best solution on your first try.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Instead, I recommend starting this phase of the UI design process with sketches.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Sketches are great because they allow you to experiment with various layouts and design ideas without spending much time or other resources. You can sketch on paper, on whiteboards, in your favorite design software &#8211; practically anywhere.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">While there are no strict rules for sketching UI design(as the whole point is to brainstorm ideas), here are two things I like to include:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Outlined boxes that will give you a general idea of the user interface layout (for example &#8211; you can experiment with <a href="/bento-box-design">bento box design</a>)</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Placeholder boxes for text, images, videos, CTAs, etc.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">After you have several sketches ready, you can present them to your design team and clients to kick off a conversation about UI design. Once you agree on the general direction the user interface design should head into, it&#8217;s time to develop your sketches further.</span></p>
<h3 id="wireframing"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 3: Wireframing User Interface</span></h3>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Wireframing-user-interface.png" alt="Wireframing user interface" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Wireframes are a natural upgrade to sketches. It&#8217;s where your layout starts to take shape, but it&#8217;s still far from the final look. The benefits of wireframing are similar to sketching &#8211; it will save you time and allow you to experiment with design without spending too many resources.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">At this stage, focus on the placement of key elements like navigation menus, content areas, and interactive components. The goal is not to dive into detailed design elements like colors or typography yet. Instead, concentrate on the overall flow and user journey through your interface.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">When creating wireframes, remember to:</span></p>
<ol>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Keep it simple</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">: Avoid getting bogged down in details. Stick to the core layout and structure.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Prioritize usability</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">: Ensure the user journey is logical and intuitive.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Encourage collaboration</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">: Share your wireframes with team members and stakeholders for feedback. Collaboration at this stage can reveal crucial insights and improvements.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Iterate</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">: Be prepared to revise and refine your wireframes. This iterative process is critical to evolving your initial ideas into a functional design.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Once you have </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/high-fidelity-wireframes" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">high fidelity wireframes</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> ready, you&#8217;re ready to add more depth to your design in the next steps of the UI design process.</span></p>
<h3 id="components"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 4: Designing UI Components</span></h3>
<p>Modern UI design<span data-preserver-spaces="true"> is dynamic. That&#8217;s why you must add depth to each element on your page. During this step, you&#8217;ll break down the design into smaller, manageable pieces &#8211; components that together create a cohesive whole.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Begin by creating a library of UI elements. This involves detailed work on the smaller yet vital aspects like buttons, icons, and input fields. These elements should be visually aligned with the overall design and adaptable to different user interactions &#8211; think about how a button changes on hover or how a form field reacts when selected. Understanding </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/ui-animation" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">UI animation principles</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> will help you craft more natural and enjoyable experiences.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Also, design with the end in mind. Ensure that developers can easily translate each component into code, which will make the handoff process smoother.</span></p>
<h3 id="flows"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 5: Creating User Flows and Task Flows</span></h3>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Creating-user-flows-and-task-flows.png" alt="Creating user flows and task flows" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Defining how users will move between screens and how they&#8217;ll complete various tasks is the next crucial step of the UI design process. It should all feel natural for the end user. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">User flows are the routes users take to achieve a specific goal within your app or website, like making a purchase or finding information.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Task flows, on the other hand, are more detailed, focusing on the sequence of actions users take to complete a single task.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Here&#8217;s how to approach this step of the UI design process:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Visualize the Journey</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">: Start by laying out the different screens or pages your users will interact with. Sketch the paths users might take to move from one screen to another to visualize potential roadblocks they might face.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Consider Different Scenarios</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">: Not all users will follow the same path. Map out alternative routes for different user personas or objectives (which you hopefully defined in the first step of the UI design process).</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Test and implement</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">: As you develop these flows, test them. In one of the previous articles, I&#8217;ve shared </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/user-experience-survey-questions" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">user experience survey questions</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> you can use to gather feedback.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This stage is crucial for transforming your static designs into dynamic, interactive experiences that resonate with your users. But two essential UI design process steps are left before you&#8217;re done&#8230;</span></p>
<h3 id="final-design"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 6: Crafting Pixel-Perfect UI Design</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It&#8217;s finally time to put all of your design skills into practice and design the best version of the user interface.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">In this phase, precision and attention to detail are key. You need to:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Create the final look of your UI design</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Have a copy ready</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Ensure consistency across all the screens and interface elements</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Implement </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/web-design-branding" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">web design branding</span></a></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">I recommend learning how to use Figma for web design so you can </span></p>
<h3 id="prototype"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Step 7: Create a Prototype That Connects All Screens And Flows</span></h3>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The UI design prototype is an interactive model that mimics the user experience and ties everything together.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It can be considered as a no-code version of your app or website. UI prototyping helps you ensure your design is ready for production, making the job easier for developers later on.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Here&#8217;s how to approach this crucial step:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Simulate the Real Experience:</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> Use tools for UI prototype design to build an interactive version of your interface. </span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Conduct tests with real users:</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> Watch how they interact with the prototype and note any areas of confusion or difficulty.</span></li>
<li><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Prepare for Development</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">: A well-crafted UI prototype makes the job easier for developers. It serves as a clear, interactive guideline for what needs to be coded. By effectively using UI prototyping, you bridge the gap between design and development.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This step is the culmination of your design efforts, ready to be transformed into a live digital product.</span></p>
<h2 id="final-thoughts"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Final Thoughts</span></h2>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A good UI design process involves comprehensive research, planning, and creativity. Once you bring structure to your work, you&#8217;ll confidently tackle every project.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Remember, every step in this process, from understanding your users to prototyping your design, is crucial. They collectively ensure that your final product isn&#8217;t just visually stunning but also highly functional and user-centric. </span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Now, if you need guidance or seek to refine your UI design process further, I&#8217;m here to help. When you </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/schedule-a-call" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">schedule a call</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">, we can discuss your specific challenges and goals.</span></p>','https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/UI-design-process.png',NULL,'[]','[353,308]','2024-01-11T14:22:20','2024-01-11T14:22:20',1824,10,5),
  (23111,'/elementor-page-speed','elementor-page-speed','post','blog','8 Elementor Page Speed Issues And How To Fix Them','8 Elementor Page Speed Issues And How To Fix Them - Alpha Efficiency','Discover the main reasons why your website performance can be slow, and how to improve Elementor page speed.','https://alphaefficiency.com/elementor-page-speed',1,'Is your Elementor page speed less than optimal? Did you successfully migrate your web design from Figma to Elementor, but the end result is not performing as you expected? Are users leaving your site before they get a chance to check your content? Elementor is an outstanding page builder that enables web designers and developers &hellip; Continued','<p>Is your Elementor page speed less than optimal? Did you successfully migrate your web design from <a href="/figma-to-elementor">Figma to Elementor</a><strong>, </strong>but the end result is not performing as you expected? Are users leaving your site before they get a chance to check your content?</p>
<p>Elementor is an outstanding page builder that enables web designers and developers to create fully functional websites with ease. However, some Elementor websites present speed-loading issues due to easy-to-fix mistakes designers and developers make.</p>
<p>Poor website loading speed is the number one reason for high bounce rates. Website speed is also one of the main Gogole&#8217;s ranking factors. If your site speed performance is even slightly slow, that will compromise your site conversion rates.</p>
<p>As a <a href="/web-design-agency-chicago">Chicago web design agency</a><strong> </strong>owner, I also faced this problem when started using Elementor. That&#8217;s how I learned that Elementor&#8217;s sites only load slowly when you make some common mistakes. Luckily by knowing a few website speed tricks, you can quickly solve any Elementor page speed issue.</p>
<p>In this article, I&#8217;ll show you the <strong>main reasons why your Elementor website performance can be slow</strong>, how to test your website speed, and the<strong> best optimization tips</strong> to improve Elementor page speed.</p>
<h5>Table of Content:</h5>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#core-web-vitals">Website Loading Speed aka One of Google&#8217;s Core Web Vitals</a></li>
<li><a href="/#problems-and-solutions">Why Your Elementor Page Speed Runs Slow And How To Fix It</a>
<ul>
<li><a href="/#hosting">1. Your Hosting Service Is Compromising Your Site Speed</a></li>
<li><a href="/#too-many-plugins">2. Too Many Plugins Slow Down Your Site</a></li>
<li><a href="/#cdn">3. You Don&#8217;t Use a Content Delivery Network (CDN)</a></li>
<li><a href="/#images">4. Too Large, Unoptimized Images</a></li>
<li><a href="/#caching">5. You Didn&#8217;t Enable Data Caching</a></li>
<li><a href="/#theme">6. The Theme You Chose is Too Slow</a></li>
<li><a href="/#code">7. You Have Unnecessary CSS or JSS</a></li>
<li><a href="/#fonts">8. Third-Party Custom Fonts Can Hurt Loading Speed</a></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><a href="/#measuring">How To Measure Your Site Loading Speed &#8211; Let&#8217;s Find Out How Bad The Problem Is</a></li>
<li><a href="/#plugins">Use Plugins To Boost Your Elementor Website Page Speed</a></li>
<li><a href="/#your-turn">It&#8217;s Your Turn To Optimize Elementor Page Speed And Create Profitable Websites</a></li>
</ul>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Elementor-page-speed.png" alt="Elementor page speed" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h2 id="core-web-vitals">Website Loading Speed aka One of Google&#8217;s Core Web Vitals</h2>
<p>A website that takes 1-3 seconds to load increases bounce rate probability by 30%. And as the loading time increases, so does the bounce rate percentage.</p>
<p>Slowly performing sites can easily scare customers away; poor loading speed is considered a huge negative point when it comes to user experience. Conversely, website owners that optimize their sites to load fast deliver greater user satisfaction earning more traffic and closing sales.</p>
<p>That&#8217;s why Google includes website load times on its specific metrics called Core Web Vitals &#8211; a set of indicators that provide site owners with an understanding of what Google considers to be a website that provides high-quality customer experiences.</p>
<p>Neglecting Google&#8217;s Core Web Vitals can hurt your search engine optimization strategy, engagement levels, and conversion rate.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Largest Contentful Paint (LCP): </strong>Paint is a fancy word for saying &#8220;show all the elements you can see on the screen in front of you.&#8221; This metric refers to the time it takes for your website to load the majority of its content since the user clicks on a link. What is a good LCP score? You should aim for your content to load whiting 2.5 seconds from when the page starts loading.</li>
<li><strong>First Input Delay (FID): </strong>This indicator tests interactivity, or how well can users interact with your page. FID measures the time between a user interaction with your page (such as clicking a link or choosing a menu item) and your browser processing and responding to that interaction. Ideally, your website FID should be less than 100 milliseconds.</li>
<li><strong>Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS):</strong> Think of CLS as &#8220;visual stability,&#8221; marking the stability of a web page as it loads. Your website reaches visual stability when page elements are no longer shifting around. If layouts, images, text, or buttons move around as your website loads, that indicates you have a high CLS &#8211; which is not good. Always aim to maintain a CLS of less than 0.1 seconds.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="problems-and-solutions">Why Your Elementor Page Speed Runs Slow And How To Fix It</h2>
<p>There are dozens of reasons why your Elementor WordPress website may perform slowly. To tackle the problem, you first need to find what is causing it.</p>
<p>Below are the primary culprits behind poor loading websites:</p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Elementor-page-speed-problems-and-solutions.png" alt="Elementor page speed problems and solutions" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3 id="hosting">1. Your Hosting Service Is Compromising Your Site Speed</h3>
<p>Sometimes, there is nothing wrong with your Elementor website, but your hosting provider fails to power up your site.</p>
<p>Your website loading speed is directly linked to the type of hosting service you are using. If you have a business website with a <a href="/luxury-website-design">luxury website design</a><strong> </strong>and use a minimum plan &#8211; like shared hosting &#8211; your site is likely to experience slow loading.</p>
<p>Shared hosting means your site is sharing server resources with other users. Whenever other websites on the server get abundant traffic, your website speed may be compromised.</p>
<p>Cheap hosting often comes with a higher cost &#8211; poor loading speed, bad user experience, and low SEO ranking.</p>
<p><strong>Solution: Hire A Good WordPress Hosting Service</strong></p>
<p>If you run a business website that gets large amounts of traffic, the best option is renting a physical service for hosting your site.</p>
<p>There are many great hosting providers that offer services specifically for WordPress websites; when using Elementor website builder, I highly recommend you get a managed hosting service. That way, you will get a configured server with security settings, regular updates, ongoing support, and automated backups &#8211; all great advantages for website performance and SEO.</p>
<h3 id="too-many-plugins">2. Too Many Plugins Slow Down Your Site</h3>
<p>Elementor page builder offer hundreds of plugins you can implement to increase your website features and functionalities. However, some plugins may prejudice your site&#8217;s seep performance and lead to high bounce rates.</p>
<p>There is a misbelief that too many plugins will slow down your Elementor page speed. That&#8217;s not exactly true. Only non-optimized or poorly coded plugins will have a negative impact on your website loading speed.</p>
<p><strong>Solution: Be More Selective About Your Plugins</strong></p>
<p>Plugins are a must to create unique, feature-rich websites. Getting rid of them is not a feasible option.</p>
<p>What I recommend you do is be more selective about the plugins you include in your website design. Only choose top-quality plugins and the ones that will actually enhance your website &#8211; no need to add extra features without a purpose in mind.</p>
<p>Analyze your plugins carefully and get rid of any low-quality add-ons that hurt site speed. You can check my list of <a href="/essential-addons-for-elementor">essential addons for Elementor</a> to find the plugin that best meets your goals; all the addons from that list provide interesting features without compromising loading speed.</p>
<h3 id="cdn">3. You Don&#8217;t Use a Content Delivery Network (CDN)</h3>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Content-Delivery-Network-CDN.png" alt="Content Delivery Network CDN" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<p>Your website hosting server is located in one particular city; when users from other zones enter your site, that can slow things down.</p>
<p>If you own a local business and most of your website visitors are locals, you are unlikely to experience this issue. On the other hand, if you plan to expand your business reach and attract website users from other areas, that may slow down your WordPress hosting server seed.</p>
<p><strong>Solution: Improve Load Time By Using a CDN</strong></p>
<p>A content delivery network stores a cached version of your site&#8217;s content on several server locations around the globe. When a user from afar enters your Elementor website, the CDN closer to them will deliver the website data. As a result, website loading speed increases significantly.</p>
<p>Some good CDT options for WordPress sites include <a href="https://uploadcare.com/cdn/">Uploadcare</a>, Cloudwatch, and others.</p>
<h3 id="images">4. Too Large, Unoptimized Images</h3>
<p>Images, videos, and other media files enhance user experience and help visitors engage with your website content. But if you are including too large or unoptimized images, then I must tell you you are using images wrong.</p>
<p>Adding any type of media file without resizing it is just bad practice. It can significantly slow down Elementor page speed, leading to user dissatisfaction and high bounce rates, increasing your website traffic, and more.</p>
<p><strong>Solution: Optimize Your Images So They Look Great And Load Fast</strong></p>
<p>On average, images and media files make up around half of the file size of a website. That makes image optimization an excellent opportunity to seep up your site.</p>
<p>Image optimization takes two parts:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Resized dimensions: </strong>You must resize your images&#8217; dimensions depending on their purpose. For example, when you add background images, the recommended size is 1920px x 1080px. On the other hand, if you are featuring the image on a blog, the ideal size would be no larger than 1200px x 628px.</li>
<li><strong>Compression: </strong>After you resize the image to a proper size, you must compress it to further reduce its size. You can choose between lossy compression (some image quality loss but high file size reduction) or lossless compression (zero quality loss but smaller file size reduction). I highly recommend the latter one; low-quality images look unprofessional. Your site may load fats now, but potential clients will get a poor first impression.</li>
</ul>
<p>You can use tools, such as <a href="https://tinypng.com/">TinyPNG</a>, to resize and compress your images and gain website speed without compromising quality.</p>
<h3 id="caching">5. You Didn&#8217;t Enable Data Caching</h3>
<p>Whenever a user requests a page from your website, your WordPress server has to assemble that page from scratch. That includes executing PHP for files and &#8220;building&#8221; the page before delivering the finished HTML version of your website.</p>
<p>That process usually takes time and resources, causing two negative effects:</p>
<ul>
<li>It slows down your website loading speed, scaring visitors away</li>
<li>The server uses more resources for each visitor, which translates into an even lower website during high-traffic hours</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Solution: Use A Cache Plugin</strong></p>
<p>Page caching eliminates this speed issue by storing a finished HTML product of your website pages in a cache. It can also store data on users&#8217; browsers, so if they decide to revisit your website, they experience an even faster loading speed and greater user experience.</p>
<p>Many WordPress hosting services do page caching automatically for you; make sure to use one that includes caching among their services.</p>
<h3 id="theme">6. The Theme You Chose is Too Slow</h3>
<p>Can my theme slow down my Elementor site? Yes, the WordPress theme you choose is the foundation of your site&#8217;s front-end content; therefore, it has an impact on front-end optimization, including speed.</p>
<p>A theme is a collection of files, many of which you won&#8217;t even decide to use, such as layouts or other page design elements. That leads to many WordPress Themes looking good on the front, but they are actually hurting your site speed.</p>
<p><strong>Solution: Use A Fast Theme</strong></p>
<p>If you are planning to use a theme to build your Elementor website faster, you&#8217;ll want to go with an optimized one. Choose a well-coded theme with good functionality but also a simple one so it doesn&#8217;t include unnecessary features.</p>
<h3 id="code">7. You Have Unnecessary CSS or JSS</h3>
<p>This issue relates to the previous one. The theme you picked may come with unnecessary CCS or JSS codes, or perhaps you wrote those codes, but your website is not currently using them.</p>
<p>JSS codes can take a lot of resources, and CSS codes add to a site&#8217;s loading times. Therefore, having those codes for no use, is just compromising your website speed and performance for nothing.</p>
<p><strong>Solution: Remove Unused JSS and CSS Codes</strong></p>
<p>This solution is pretty straightforward: get rid of or minimize as much as possible any JSS or CSS codes you are not using on your site.</p>
<p>You can find out what CSS and JSS codes you are not using with one of the website speed tests I&#8217;ll mention further down this article.</p>
<h3 id="fonts">8. Third-Party Custom Fonts Can Hurt Loading Speed</h3>
<p>Third-party, custom fonts, such as Google Fonts or Font Awesome, are the perfect way to paint your website with your brand&#8217;s identity and make it stand out. Sadly, fonts loading slowly means your site will also run slowly.</p>
<p>An easy solution would be to deactivate third-party fonts and use the default ones. But unless Elementor default fonts go really well with your website design, I wouldn&#8217;t discard custom fonts so fast &#8211; they can incredibly enhance the look and feel of a website while improving reliability and user experience. Let&#8217;s explore other solutions.</p>
<p><strong>Solution 1: Store The Fonts Locally</strong></p>
<p>Google Fonts are excellent for leveraging the look of your site, but they are terrible at performance. What you can do to overcome this issue is self-hosting openly licensed custom fonts.</p>
<p><strong>Solution 2: Use Moder Web Formats</strong></p>
<p>When learning how to add font in WordPress Elementor<strong>,</strong> one of the first things to know is what file forms are supported by Elementor page builder. Elementor supports WOFF, WOFF 2, SVG, TTF, and EOT font file formats.</p>
<p>Just like images, font file formats have evolved to become more compact. WOFF and WOFF2 are the formats with superior compression, and are less likely to hurt your website loading speed.</p>
<h2 id="measuring">How To Measure Your Site Loading Speed &#8211; Let&#8217;s Find Out How Bad The Problem Is</h2>
<p>You can&#8217;t start making adjustments while being in the dark. Before starting to optimize your Elementor website performance, you must measure its speed to gain insight into how much and what kind of improvements you&#8217;ll need to make.</p>
<p>Most web developers&#8217; new tools for speed test support Gogole&#8217;s Core Web Vitals. Here I leave you (number) you can use to check your WordPress website loading speed:</p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Measuring-site-speed.png" alt="Measuring site speed" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3>Google PageSpeed Insights</h3>
<p>PageSpeed Insights has been the go-to loading speed tool for years. This simple tool created by Google analyzes the web page and grades it on a scale from 1 to 100 for desktop and mobile devices. The higher the score, the faster your website is.</p>
<p>Besides being free and not needing registration, this tool is extremely simple, you only have to add your website URL. Then, PageSpeed Insights will run a website speed test and give you information such as:</p>
<ul>
<li>First Contentful Paint (FCP)</li>
<li>Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)</li>
<li>First Input Delay (FID)</li>
<li>Render-blocking code</li>
<li>Page Size</li>
<li>Unused CSS and JSS codes</li>
</ul>
<p>This Google tool will also offer recommendations on paths of action to improve website speed.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">WebPage Test</h3>
<p>While PageSpeed Insights is efficient and user-friendly, it doesn&#8217;t offer its users control over testing conditions. That&#8217;s where WebPage Test comes into play.</p>
<p>If you target a local market, it&#8217;s crucial you test your website from the closest servers. WebPage Test allows you to do just that. This simple but effective tool enables you to select testing conditions by navigating to the &#8220;Advance Configuration&#8221; button to access the settings. There, you can choose the testing location, the browser, and the connection type.</p>
<p>WebPage will give you a large volume of page speed details, such as:</p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Time to First Byte</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">First Content Paint</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Largest Contentful Paint</span></li>
<li>Cumulative Layout Shift</li>
</ul>
<p>With that insight, you can start optimizing your WordPress website&#8217;s loading speed to deliver a better user experience.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">GTmetrix</h3>
<p>Do you want to test your website speed and see how it stacks up with your competitors? GTmetrix allows you to measure your site speed and compare it with your rivals.</p>
<p>Besides that, GTmetrix stands out for enabling test customization and counting with testing servers that cover the entire planet. This tool is ideal for professionals who need a large volume of information. GTmetrix will provide you:</p>
<ul>
<li>Summary: displays your site&#8217;s main speed issues</li>
<li>Performance: shows a bunch of valuable metrics</li>
<li>Waterfall: request-by-request visualization &#8211; useful for expert web designers</li>
<li>Video: the tool records a video to give you a better understanding of your website&#8217;s visitors experience</li>
<li>History: see how your site has performed over time</li>
</ul>
<p>In addition to those benefits, BTmetrix has another feature called Structure, which groups issues by importance and gives you tips to solve them.</p>
<h2 id="plugins">Use Plugins To Boost Your Elementor Website Page Speed</h2>
<p>How would you like a tool that takes care of most of your website speed issues for you?</p>
<p>After running a website speed test, you may find yourself overwhelmed with the amount of work to do to fix the problem.</p>
<p>Besides, website speed is an ongoing task; you must regularly check all site speed aspects to ensure your site keeps running smoothly and prevent loading issues from driving customers away.</p>
<p>Fortunately, there are some tools that can help you streamline that process. At <a href="/">Alpha Efficiency</a>, I&#8217;ve used these tools in the past to tackle website issues that were causing loading speed trouble and get them to run smoothly and convert clients efficiently.</p>
<img src="https://alphaefficiency.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Plugins-to-boost-elementor-website-speed.png" alt="Plugins to boost elementor website speed" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
<h3>Try WP Rocket &#8211; A User-Friendly Plugin To Boost Website Speed And Performance</h3>
<p><a href="/wp-rocket-elementor">WP Rocket Elementor</a> is one of the best combinations for improving your website speed. As a huge plus, WP Rocket has one of the most user-friendly interfaces I&#8217;ve ever seen.</p>
<p>This WP plugin will take care of all of your website caching tasks and comes with some interesting features, such as database optimization and lazy loading plugins.</p>
<p>Here are some of WP Rocket features that will help with your site performance:</p>
<ul>
<li>Minify HTML, JSS, and CSS files</li>
<li>Page caching</li>
<li>Cache preloading</li>
<li>Image lazy loading</li>
<li>CDN integration</li>
<li>Database optimization</li>
<li>Google Fonts optimization</li>
<li>Google Analytics integration</li>
</ul>
<p>As you can see, this is a quite complete WordPress plugin. If you want a user-friendly tool to boost your site speed, I highly recommend you check WP Rocket.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Perfmatters &#8211; A Lightweight Tool To Get Rid Of Unnecessary Clutter</h3>
<p>WordPress comes with some options enabled that aren&#8217;t always necessary for your website and can slow down its performance. Perfmatters allow you to identify those elements and disable them with just one click.</p>
<p>Disabling unused elements sounds simple but can do wonders for your site seed. With Perfmatters, you can selectively deactivate scripts and styles on a per-page basis.</p>
<p>Besides helping your site stop loading plugins that aren&#8217;t needed, Perfmatters also comes with other useful features:</p>
<ul>
<li>Database optimization</li>
<li>Remove WordPress bloat</li>
<li>Script manager</li>
</ul>
<p>You can combine this plugin with WP Rocket to have greater control over every aspect of your website&#8217;s loading speed. While WP Rocket will tackle your site caching issues, Perfmatters will get rid of unnecessary clutter that slows down your website.</p>
<h3>Use NitroPack For a One-Click Solution To Site Speed</h3>
<p>You don&#8217;t have time to optimize your Elementor WordPress website? NitroPack is a plugin that can take care of standard and advanced website speed issues, such as image optimization and removing unnecessary CSS files.</p>
<p>Let&#8217;s take a look at this optimization tool&#8217;s features:</p>
<ul>
<li>Automatic image optimization</li>
<li>Global CDN</li>
<li>HTML, CSS, and JS compression and minification</li>
<li>Scripts optimization</li>
<li>Caching optimization</li>
</ul>
<p>NitroPack fees are high, but if it fits into your budget and you&#8217;re looking for a quick and easy solution, this tool is the right choice for you. You have a free plan option, but it adds a badge at your site footer.</p>
<h2 id="your-turn">It&#8217;s Your Turn To Optimize Elementor Page Speed And Create Profitable Websites</h2>
<p>Slow Elementor page speed will negatively impact your website and, therefore, your business.</p>
<p>If you create visually appealing web designs that look good on paper but fail to load fast, you have a big problem on your hands. Poor speed is a main SEO ranking factor, it hurts conversion rates and guarantees a bad user experience.</p>
<p>By optimizing your Elementor WordPress website, you will build sites that look good and perform even better. Not sure where to start? Optimizing an Elementor website can be difficult, especially if you just started using this software. That&#8217;s why I developed a comprehensive Elementor course with all the info you&#8217;ll need to create high-performing sites.</p>
<p>In this course you&#8217;ll gain insights on:</p>
<ul>
