<p>Split layouts are visually captivating and convey a modern and creative feeling. Still, despite their benefits and popularity, you don&#8217;t see many websites with split screens. Why? Because split layouts look great as an idea, they can be very difficult to attain.</p>
<p>To nail split screen layouts, you must first know when and how to use them. This technique can elevate and make your website stand out, but only if it is the right fit.</p>
<p>I&#8217;ve prepared a<strong> free-mini course</strong>, <a href="https://get.alphaefficiency.com/7-days-to-profitable-aeshtetics">7 Days to Profitable Aesthetics</a>, which will show you must-avoid mistakes that can significantly ruin your conversion rates, especially if you&#8217;re using split screen techniques. You&#8217;ll also learn psychological triggers I&#8217;ve been using in the past 15 years to achieve up to 50% more sales for clients across various industries.</p>
<p>In this article, I will share the split screen web design secrets I learned at my <a href="/web-design-agency-los-angeles">Los Angeles web design agency</a>. Continue reading to learn when you should take this approach and 4 invaluable tips for <strong>creating high-performing split screen website designs</strong>.</p>
