  (18041,'/web-development-northbrook-il','web-development-northbrook-il','page','location','A web development company near Northbrook, IL explains why you should skip website builders','Web Development company in Northbrook, IL - Alpha Efficiency.™','Let’s look at why you should avoid website builders for your web development in Northbrook, IL.','https://alphaefficiency.com/web-development-northbrook-il',1,'There are many builders online, and they run extensive marketing campaigns. They promise easy-to-use and cheap solutions to web development. But, it’s not all merry because you’re only hurting your business. Let’s look at why you should avoid website builders for your web development in Northbrook, IL. The reasons why you should skip website builders  &hellip; Continued','<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">There are many builders online, and they run extensive marketing campaigns. They promise easy-to-use and cheap solutions to web development. But, it’s not all merry because you’re only hurting your business. Let’s look at why you should avoid website builders for your </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">web development </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">in Northbrook, IL</span><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br />
</span></p>
<h2>The reasons why you should skip website builders <b><br />
</b></h2>
<h4>Cheap online presence</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Online presence is vital for your business. You do not want to look sketchy or cheap. That’s what you get from website builders. They don’t give you flashy designs that are sustainable in the long term to attract all types of customers. Take the initiative to avoid website builders. The preset templates will make you look like millions of websites online. They don’t have a suitable </span><a href="/text-to-html-ratio-seo"><span style="font-weight: 400;">HTML to text ratio</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> to accommodate flexible designs.</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br />
</span></p>
<h4>Poor SEO</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Creating a website on an online builder is easy, but you most likely won’t incorporate SEO in the right way. Search engines won’t crawl through your website to read your content. It’s because website builders do not have structured code; you lose control of the content you add to your site, yet you need it for optimization.</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br />
</span></p>
<h4>Limited features</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Website builders are not dynamic enough to let you improve user experience. The limitation is a problem if you want to scale up your business. You don’t also get to customize the available features. A lack of customization will make your website boring. It won’t inspire users to browse the site. It would be best if you had professional </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">web development </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">in Northbrook, IL </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">to create a compelling website.</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br />
</span></p>
<h4>Low competitiveness</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The limitation of website builders leads you to fall behind the pack. In a competitive market, your website loses relevance, and competitors will get ahead. You lose out on the reputation and monetary value of your business. Visitors will notice that you hardly invested in creating a competitive website. You can’t achieve a custom design, like one you create though a </span><a href="/sage-framework-wordpress"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Sage WordPress Theme</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br />
</span></p>
<h4>Lack of control</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Website features lack many technical features that you could use to your advantage. There are many risks associated with using a website builder. If a website builder closes, you lose all your data, and the time you spent building the brand. A solution is to create your website from scratch and host it on a reliable and fast server. It can be through </span><a href="/google-cloud-hosting-wordpress"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Google Cloud Hosting</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. You keep control of your site, data, and brand. Also, you are not part of the </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">website creation process</span><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br />
</span></p>
<h4>Ineffectiveness</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Website builders do not deliver the best performance. You might see it as cheap, but it costs you in the long run. It’ll force you to a fallback plan, which is what you tried to evade all along. You don’t get to review the performance of your website through analytics. A stand-alone website gives you this freedom. The only way you can improve on a DIY (do it yourself) website is to collect data from visitors’ activity and reviews. Also, its </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">average website lifespan</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"> is low because of the changing web design trends. So, you have little control in changing your site’s design.</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br />
</span></p>
<h4>Monetization deficit</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">You are at a disadvantage when it comes to the monetization of website builders. Instead, they are making you pay more than you should. You’ll pay for a subscription to maintain your website, or they control the ads on your site. Website builders do not support ad services like; </span></p>
<ul>
<li aria-level="2"><a href="http://ads.google.com"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Google Ads</span></a></li>
<li aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Direct publisher deals</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br />
</span></li>
