<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Engagement</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Leads</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Equate these factors against the time at which you want to achieve them. They are part of your performance metrics that you’ll track and report. At this point, you should decide between </span><a href="/seo-vs-google-ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="font-weight: 400;">SEO vs. Google Ads</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></p>
<h4><i>Keyword research</i></h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Keywords are essential to help you achieve results and display ads to the right audience. It assists search engines in pushing your ads. Even though you get </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">optimized targeting</span><span style="font-weight: 400;">, you still need to get your keywords right. Consider the following when selecting keywords and keyword phrases;</span></p>
<ul>
