<h3 id="crm">Best CRM For Small Businesses</h3>
<p>Business data gets overwhelming. If you don&#8217;t start organizing it on time, it can drown your small business. The right customer relationship management solution can help you keep all your information under one roof. Your CRM should be a starting point for all your business operations.</p>
<p>Here are CRM for small business solutions you should consider:</p>
<h4>1. HubSpot CRM</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">HubSpot is a go-to CRM choice for my digital agency. It brings various tools under one roof. You can use it to track customer interactions, generate leads, automate marketing campaigns, and build a robust </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/inbound-marketing-funnel" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">inbound marketing funnel</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">. HubSpot helps us organize all our data and keep track of business operations effectively.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">This platform also offers a free-forever plan, which is okay for starting out. However, I recommend upgrading to paid plans as you scale your business. You&#8217;ll get access to advanced features that way. </span></p>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Key Features:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Lead distribution</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Sales engagement tools</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Reporting and analytics</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">CPQ capabilities</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Payments</span></li>
</ul>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Pros:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Easy to use thanks to a clean interface</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Ability to keep track of customer demands easily</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">A wide range of tools under one roof</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Supports 1,500+ integrations; it will probably fit nicely with your other tools</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Offers a free plan</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Excellent customer support</span></li>
</ul>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Cons:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It can become pricey as your needs grow</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Slightly geared toward enterprises</span></li>
</ul>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Price: </span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Offers a free plan; Starter plan starts at $18 per month; Professional plan starts at $800 per month; Enterprise plan starts at $3,600 per month.</span></p>
