<h3 id="project-management">Project Management Tools For Small Business</h3>
<p>Effective project management is the lifeblood of any thriving company. It&#8217;s pivotal for overseeing tasks and ensuring every effort drives your business forward. To scale and thrive, you must have a precise pulse on the time invested, the endeavors undertaken, and the outcomes achieved.</p>
<p>The ideal project management tool does more than merely organize tasks. It acts as a compass, guiding you and your team even amidst the most intricate projects. With the right tool, you can help your team maintain focus, ensuring that each step aligns with the larger goal.</p>
<p>I&#8217;ve tried various project management tools for my digital agency. Here is a list of 9 project management tools I found to work best for small businesses:</p>
<h4>22. Hubstaff Tasks</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Hubstaff Tasks has been a ground base for my agency&#8217;s project management. It&#8217;s where we track every single task each employee is doing. Hubstaff Tasks make it very easy to organize your projects within folders and keep track of how much time is spent on each moving part. Over the years, we started using other project management tools, too. However, Hubstaff Tasks is still the only platform where we store all projects without exception. It helps everyone on the team gain a holistic overview of the current progress and the time they spend on each task.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">My employees submit standups at the end of each day, which helps me get quick insights into work done and whether anyone needs further assistance. This makes it much easier for me to manage a remote team.</span></p>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Key features:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Agile project management</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Visual boards</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Sprints</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Automated stand-ups</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Time tracking</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Project timelines visualization</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Checklists</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Workflows</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Pre-made and customizable templates</span></li>
</ul>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Pros:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It&#8217;s easy to use and looks visually organized.</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It comes with pre-built templates, but I can&#8217;t tell you much about their quality because we quickly created custom templates with my agency.</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Sprints help everyone on the team keep track of priority projects.</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> </span></li>
</ul>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Cons:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The free plan offers limited functionalities.</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It might take some time to get used to the Agile framework if you&#8217;re new to it.</span></li>
</ul>
<h4>23. ClickUp</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">If your small business team is struggling to keep up with tasks, deadlines, and communication, ClickUp could be the answer. My agency has been relying on this tool to organize and manage our remote team, and it&#8217;s been a game-changer. I even created a guide on </span><a class="editor-rtfLink" href="/how-to-use-clickup-for-project-management" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-preserver-spaces="true">how to use ClickUp for project management</span></a><span data-preserver-spaces="true">, which you can check out.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">I particularly appreciate the option to invite guests for free, allowing us to keep clients in the loop on project status without incurring extra costs. The built-in automations are another time-saver, which allows me to auto-assign tasks, move their statuses, and even auto-comment.</span></p>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Key features:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Customizable Workspaces</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Task Assignments</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Due Dates &amp; Reminders</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Guest Invitations: Collaborate with clients or external team members at no extra cost.</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Time Tracking</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Real-time chat with team members</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Whiteboards</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Built-in Automations</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">ClickApps</span></li>
</ul>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Pros:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">With ClickApps, you can customize this platform&#8217;s functionality to match your project needs.</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Real-time updates and communication features keep everyone on the same page.</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Great for keeping clients updated on project status.</span></li>
<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Intuitive design makes it easy to get your team up and running quickly.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Cons:</span></strong></p>
