<li><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The user experience can be less pleasing on smaller screens.</span></li>
</ul>
<h4>24. Notion</h4>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">I use Notion for organization and taking personal notes. It helps me put ideas and observations into one place. But I also use Notion to run my core management team and build a knowledge hub for my company. Although it started as a note-taking software, I&#8217;ve recently noticed that Notion is evolving to become an excellent choice for project management.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">It doesn&#8217;t have time tracking capabilities like Hubstaff and ClickUp. But with various templates, you can still estimate complete dates very accurately. One of the main reasons I love using Notion is its visual appeal. Everything looks neat and clean, which makes it easy for me and my team to quickly find notes and collaborate effectively. If you want to learn more about how I&#8217;m using this app for my business, I recommend reading my guide on Notion for agencies.</span></p>
<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Key features:</span></strong></p>
