<h3 id="accounting">Best Accounting Software For Small Business (+ Tax Filling, Payment Processing, and eSignature Tools)</h3>
<p>Keeping track of your finances is especially important when your business is still small. You don&#8217;t have room for mistakes enterprises can make without any harm. Overlooking a tax detail, mismanaging expenses, or even a minor oversight in payroll can lead to larger issues down the line.</p>
<p>Fulfilling your tax responsibilities isn&#8217;t just about staying in the good graces of the tax advisors or the small business administration. It&#8217;s about ensuring that your business operates smoothly, ethically, and profitably.</p>
<p>A reliable accounting solution can be your vigilant guardian, keeping track of every dollar and cent, ensuring that salaries are disbursed on time, and even helping you discern patterns in your expenses. By understanding these patterns, you can make more informed decisions when allocating resources and planning your budget.</p>
<p>Moreover, collecting payments and managing invoices become a breeze with the right tool in place. Remember, consistent cash flow is the lifeblood of any business. You want to ensure that you&#8217;re billing correctly and on time, and also that you&#8217;re being paid promptly.</p>
<p>Here&#8217;s the most important tip &#8211; you must ensure your accounting software tools integrate smoothly with your CRM. I recently made the switch to a Stripe + HubSpot combination. This streamlined my invoicing and payment processes and helped me unlock a level of oversight and automation that made my business operations much easier and error-prone.</p>
<p>Here&#8217;s my list of the ten best accounting software for small business. This list contains tools for running your books, payment processing, and also software for document signing.</p>
<h4>81. Intuit QuickBooks</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Intuit QuickBooks is a popular accounting software small businesses can use to manage their financial operations more efficiently. It offers a wide range of tools and features to help users handle accounting tasks, invoicing, expense tracking, and more. It is a versatile and user-friendly booking system for small businesses and startups.</span></p>
<p><strong>Key features</strong></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Invoicing</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Expense tracking</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Financial reporting</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Payroll management</span></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Pros</strong></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">It offers a wide range of tools for accounting and financial management, all in one platform</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Intuit QuickBooks automates many financial tasks, reducing manual data entry and potential errors that come with it</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">It is a cloud-based software, meaning you can access it from anywhere with access to the internet</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">It is simple to use and highly accessible</span></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Cons</strong></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">It is relatively expensive software, depending on the subscription plan you choose</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Intuit QuickBooks has limited international support, meaning that some features may be made specifically for U.S.-based businesses. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Exporting data from Intuit QuickBooks can represent an issue sometimes, as it limits data portability</span></li>
</ul>
<h4>82. FreshBooks</h4>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">FreshBooks is a cloud-based estimation and invoicing software created to simplify financial management for small businesses, freelancers, and self-employed professionals. It offers a variety of tools to help users manage their finances, invoicing, expenses, and more. It’s overall universal accounting software ideal for smaller-scale businesses, but the pricing can represent a problem.</span></p>
