<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you’re running an online store, I highly recommend including PayPal because it’s the most user-friendly option for customers. As it allows one-click checkout, this tool can be a great addition to your checkout page design, helping you improve conversion rates. As most eCommerce platforms support integration with PayPal, you shouldn’t face much trouble implementing it on your website. However, you can also use this processor to receive payments in person, which makes it a better choice than Stripe if your business is not strictly online.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">However, PayPal has a more complex pricing structure than other payment processors, so you should consider combining it with Stripe and other tools to lower your costs. PayPal is known for its security features, which is why many customers still prefer it over other options.</span></p>
